(Turkey) - Turkey will begin releasing tens of thousands of prisoners to reduce the spread of COVID-19 in prisons, as the country is also suffering from unusual levels due to the global epidemic. This was quoted from the Xinhua news agency on Tuesday morning, April 14, 2020.
The Turkish parliament on Tuesday approved a draft law on the release of prisoners. According to the law, about 45,000 prisoners will be temporarily released under the close supervision of the authorities until the end of May, and the release period can be extended two more times, one at a time. At most 2 months.
