Ministry of Education issues guidelines on the promotion of distance learning and e-learning by private institutions at all levels
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, on April 13, 2020, issued a new guideline on the promotion of distance learning and e-learning by private institutions at all levels. .
In the spirit of ensuring the effectiveness of this measure, the Ministry would like to make the following recommendations:
First, educational institutions that are conducting teaching and learning through distance education system or electronic system must prepare their respective mechanisms and calendars of teaching and learning from distance learning system or electronic system to ensure quality. And the effectiveness of teaching, learning and evaluation.
Second, for students who have to take the lower secondary school diploma and high school diploma exam, the Ministry will allow the examination to be taken by distance learning system or electronically according to the calendar of their respective educational institutions, ensuring acceptable quality standards. If necessary, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will cooperate with educational institutions to ensure this quality standard.
Third, educational institutions that follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports can issue lower secondary school diploma and high school diploma with the recognition of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, but the educational institution must sign it himself. The Ministry will conduct inspections as necessary to ensure the quality of the degree.
Fourth, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports encourages all parents and guardians to encourage and monitor their children to study electronically according to the calendar set by the educational institution and to promote self-study at home so that their children Go to some places that have a high risk of infection.
Fifth, educational institutions must ensure the standard of health and well-being of staff and students without coercion, and must prepare work schedules that help staff and students who are in this unusual situation.
Sixth, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports calls on the owners of land leased for the operation of some educational institutions to reduce the actual rent to relieve some of the burden affected by Kovid 19 and find a win-win solution for both All together.
