On the first Monday of this week, the day that Sankranti New Year will arrive at about 8 pm, which is a tradition every year, when Cambodians across the country have to take a break from their work to celebrate the New Year. New years, this national tradition.
On the morning of Monday, April 13, 2020, it was observed that the street view in Phnom Penh was normal with the traffic of vehicles. This aspect shows that civil servants, workers and employees in public and private institutions continue to come to work normally.
Heang Sotheayut, spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, told Fresh News that today, leaders and officials of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport came to work as usual. In addition to the Ministry, officials working in the Department of Public Works and Transport throughout the country also perform their normal duties.
Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, also said that at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, both leaders and civil servants of the Ministry came to work as usual. In addition, civil servants in the department also come to work as usual. In addition to these two ministries, other state institutions are also reported to be in the process of performing their normal duties, with no ministry taking leave.
In addition to government institutions in factories, enterprises, companies, private institutions and restaurants in Phnom Penh also continue to open as usual. Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that more than 95% of the factories were operating normally and the workers were working normally.
It should be noted that in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government not only postponed the New Year holiday, but also decided to close the travel of people from one province to another. In addition, Cambodians returning from Thailand were taken into custody by authorities for 14 days.
