Residents Protest Against Land Dispute 88 after Military Officials Raise Army Base Labels on Unresolved Disputes
(Kampong Chhnang): More than 30 families representing more than 120 families who own land at Khleang Ka 88, a disputed land in Trok Lech village, Sre Thmei commune and Preah Ream Rainsy village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province. Protests resume after the military raises military bases on disputed land.
Mr. Yim Chin, the people's representative, said that more than 200 hectares of land at this point, the people have occupied the fields since 1982. It was not until 1987-1988 that they saw the army come to live for a while and then withdrew due to protests from the people. Only in 2015 did the army come to protest and demand the occupation of the land above as the land of the 88th Armed Forces of the Ministry of National Defense.
Regarding the land dispute, the people said that in 2018, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, the governor of Kampong Chhnang province, made a report to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, about the history of this land, asking him to help solve it for the people.
But then suddenly, the military, the Ministry of National Defense assigned four military officers to investigate the land, then a SPDC handed over the disputed land as the land of the 88 arms to the military, while this is not the case. There is still a settlement with the people.
Regarding the raising of the military base on the disputed land, the people requested the military to remove the banner, because if this area is used as a military base, they will not be able to go in and out of the fields. Cattle can no longer, because this area is the land that they used to enjoy, as well as a geography that they occupy and go out to see cattle, cut firewood since 1982.
They urged Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help solve the people's worries in the above matter so that the people can get the land that they used to enjoy for a long time to return to farming.
