On that occasion, Preah Po Vongsa Pov Ratana also called on the monks of all pagodas to unite to educate the people on measures to protect themselves from Kovid 19 by strictly implementing the Ministry of Health and respecting the message of the head of the Royal Government in Participation in the prevention and fight against Kovid 19.
At the same time, Mr. Ou Chheang, Governor of Kien Svay District, also thanked all the monks in Kien Svay District for their attention. He added that this is not the first time that all the monks in Kien Svay district have participated in alleviating the needs of our people.
The governor of Kien Svay district said that from the beginning, the monks in the pagoda in Kien Svay district have always participated in donating money, materials and food to the poor, especially when the people have Emergencies and disasters: Monks are always actively involved in humanitarian work.
Moreover, the monks are always in touch with the local authorities to provide continuous support, obviously, as now our people are in short supply when this terrible disease Kovid 19 occurred in Cambodia. He thanked the monks who donated all kinds of resources, property and materials. "I will take this gift and distribute it according to the necessary goals to alleviate the hardships of our people."
At the same time, he thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for taking wise measures to prevent the 19 Kovid in Cambodia, which made the people all over the country feel as warm as in other countries. Global and called for teams at all levels to educate and help people to know the well-being to help people solve problems in a timely manner.
