(Phnom Penh): This morning, Sunday, April 12, 2020, with the cooperation of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, institutions, associations and youth groups, as well as Coca-Cola Company, a charity project initiated by Mani Foundation, brought a donation. To all Sangkats in Phnom Penh to continue to distribute to people in need in the actual locality of each Sangkat.
Starting from Stung Meanchey III Sangkat with the participation of Mr. Hun Many in other Sangkats, including Prek Ek Sangkat, Mr. Sar Sokha was present and at the same time in 23 other Sangkats, the youth group of the charity project This is also active.
This charity project aims to bring the donations that the Mani Foundation team and youth volunteers from 15 different groups have packed and distributed to all 105 communes throughout Phnom Penh to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in the campaign. Against COVID-19 in Cambodia.
Obviously, in response to the spread of COVID-19, the Royal Government has led and taken clear and thorough measures, but all of these measures need to involve all stakeholders to ensure effective implementation.
In this morning's donation ceremony, Stung Meanchey III Sangkat Hall received 250 packages that will be distributed to needy people, of which 150 packages have the logo of Mani Foundation along with the message "We will all Get over this challenge together ”and another 100 packs with the logos of all 15 youth volunteer groups. For each gift package: 5 kg of rice, 1 bar of hand soap, 1 bottle of soy sauce and 1 can of soft drink.
It should be noted that from today, the youth volunteer team will start to bring the package to distribute to all 105 Sangkats in Phnom Penh as planned, hoping that all donations will contribute more. In order to alleviate the difficulties of the poor people.
Through this charitable activity, it is clear that the spirit of helping each other in difficult times and the spirit of working together to overcome the obstacles that the nation is facing.
