Anti-Drug Police Arrest 2 Suspects in Drug Trafficking Case
(Phnom Penh): Two drug trafficking suspects with more than 1 kg of drugs were cracked down by the Anti-Drug Department in Phnom Penh and Kampong Speu Province.
A senior official of the Anti-Drug Department told Fresh News this morning, April 12, 2020, that the two suspects and more than 1 kg of drugs were cracked down on April 8, 2020 in Kampol commune. Khan Kambol, Phnom Penh and in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province.
The crackdown on drug cases took place under the direct leadership of General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, and Lt. Gen. Loek Vannak, Director of the Anti-Drug Department, after receiving orders from Lt. Gen. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner. The operation was conducted by Major General Kheung Sarath, Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Department (A4), with the coordination of Mr. Soeun Moniroth, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The first suspect in Phnom Penh was Chhay Samnang, a 23-year-old Cambodian male, and the second suspect in Kampong Speu was Sim Sokchon, a 27-year-old Cambodian male. There is also cooperation from the Kampong Speu Provincial Police Force.
The confiscated items included: more than 1.2 kilograms of methamphetamine, a scale for weighing some packaging materials.
The same police officer also confirmed that the two suspects and the exhibits were difficult to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
Please be informed that on April 2, 2020, the Anti-Drug Department (A4) led by Major General Kheng Sarath, Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on another drug case in Phnom Penh. Addicted to more than 1 kg, but the suspect came to his senses and escaped. History of Khmer New Year!
