Cambodia, China conclude second round of FTA talks
(Phnom Penh): Despite facing the crisis of Kovid 19, Cambodia and China continue to negotiate to reach a free trade agreement with each other. On April 9, 2020, the working group of the two countries opened the second round of talks together via online video.
According to a press release issued on April 11, 2020, the Ministry of Commerce said that the second round of negotiations on a free trade agreement between the two countries has closed. The Cambodian side was chaired by Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, and the Chinese side was led by Mr. Yang Zhengvy, Deputy Director General of the Ministry of Commerce.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, in the second round of talks, the two sides praised the results achieved by the 10 negotiating teams, which were achieved through active exchange of views and online negotiations, despite the two countries' busy schedule. The implementation of measures to prevent and combat the epidemic of Kovid 19.
During the talks, the two working groups agreed on a number of chapters on investment cooperation, economic and technical cooperation, belt and road initiatives and e-commerce.
It should be noted that the negotiation of the Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement is an initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China, in a bilateral meeting on January 20-23. 2019 in Beijing with the aim of deepening trade, investment, services and cooperation for the benefit of the two peoples.
Following the initiative, the two countries' working group began the first round of talks on January 20-21, 2020 in Beijing, China.
