FUNCINPEC Supports Government Measures to Raise New Year Holidays and Restrict Travel to Prevent COVID-19 Outbreak
(Phnom Penh): FUNCINPEC has announced its support for the Royal Government of Cambodia's urgent action to lift the Khmer New Year holiday for civil servants and workers and to restrict travel within the country to prevent and curb it. Epidemic of COVID-19 virus in Cambodia. This is according to the party's press release obtained by Fresh News.
At the same time, FUNCINPEC also called on all compatriots, government officials, factory owners, enterprises, establishments and workers, as well as all members of FUNCINPEC to follow the instructions and respect the regulations of the Royal Government responsibly. Must be high to protect the lives of the Cambodian people and society as a whole.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has announced the suspension of the traditional Khmer New Year celebration, which is scheduled to take place from April 13 to 16 to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease, but must receive angels. The new year is at home, as every year, while public institutions and private companies must continue to work normally, the state will reimburse five days off at an appropriate time later.
Meanwhile, from 12:00 pm on April 9 to 12:00 pm on April 16, 2020, the Royal Government also imposed a curfew from one province to another, except in the area between Phnom Penh and Kandal. Only.
