Minister of Agriculture and Dr. Mong Reththy urge investors to seize golden opportunities to increase livestock production to ensure food security at a time when the country is facing the crisis 19
The main objectives of this visit are:
* First: Monitor and monitor the progress of the agro-industrial sector on all production lines (MPic feed mill, Ta Koeng pig farm, the fourth commercial farm, coconut oil plantation and the first processing plant Anlong Krapeu)
* Second, hold joint discussions on behalf of the Royal Government and the private sector in the common will is to increase agricultural productivity, ensure food security in the context of our country is in crisis due to the global communicable disease Kovid-19.
During the visit, Minister Veng Sakhon and Dr. Mong Reththy inspected and received the following information:
1: The factory can produce all kinds of animal feed about 6,000 tons per month, supply to farms and partners to raise using local raw materials per month: 3,000 tons of corn, 700 tons of bran and wheat bran, 400 tons of beer And 1,000 tons of potatoes. In addition, the factory also imports raw materials to meet the shortage. Currently, local materials are available to supply the factory and the prices are acceptable to both producers and consumers.
3. Pig farm on 100 hectares equipped with modern equipment, automatic security system, etc. This farm plans to produce 1,000 pigs per day to supply the local market.
Minister Veng Sakhon's visit today has many important benefits, and all of these benefits are important messages that both of them want to send to consumers, producers and investors to consider seizing this golden opportunity to Together, ensure food security in the context of the nation facing a global Kovid 19 epidemic crisis, and the key points are as follows:
* Animal feed manufacturers must strive to use local raw materials to the best of their ability to promote local production, ensure the supply, standard and quality according to market demand. Take this opportunity to create opportunities for agriculture, agro-industry, create local jobs and increase income.
As the Co-Chair of Group "A", Dr. Tha will continue to fully cooperate with the Ministry of Agriculture to contribute to the creation of opportunities for agriculture and agro-industry, both now and in the future.
