BANGKOK: Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-ocha on Friday urged Thais to stay indoors during the New Year, which has already been suspended, to reduce the risk of infection. Outbreak of COVID-19, which is already prevalent in Thailand. This is according to a quote from the Xinhua news agency on Friday, April 10, 2020.
In a televised message across Thailand, Prayuth said that all Thais should stay at home rather than visit relatives in their hometowns as usual or organize a Sangkran celebration. New Year, which has already been postponed. If not postponed, the New Year in Thailand is to be held from Monday to Wednesday next week, no different from Cambodia.
During the Thai New Year this year, street throwing, as well as public places that used to be held every year with large crowds, is strictly prohibited throughout the year. Countries under the framework of measures taken by the Thai government under the state of emergency to combat COVID-19, and the holiday has been postponed without setting a new date.
