Coalition Forces Crack Down on Fake Alcohol Depot in Po Sen Chey District, Detain Chinese Owner and Seize Thousands of Liters of Alcohol
(Phnom Penh): A counterfeit alcohol depot in Phnom Penh's Po Sen Chey district was raided by coalition forces, confiscating thousands of liters of alcohol and methanol and arresting a Chinese owner at 28 Street 11. In New World Borey, Trapeang Thleung 4 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
This operation took place on April 9, 2020. The forces participating in the operation include: the force of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud, in cooperation with the Department of Economic Crime Police, the Phnom Penh Camcontrol Force and the force. Po Sen Chey district authorities include the district police and gendarmerie, as well as commune authorities and the 1st Chao Chao police station.
Authorities involved in the operation said the raid was led by Deputy Prosecutor Soeun Moniroth of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, while forces searched for 20 liters of counterfeit alcohol and methanol, equivalent to 4,000 liters. 10 more is equal to 300 liters.
According to the source, for some time now, the above-mentioned law enforcement forces have been cracking down on the importation of alcohol without any clear source, illegal and counterfeit, and confiscated tens of thousands of liters in Phnom Penh and Kandal provinces. Secretly stockpiled for sale to users protected against Kovid-19 virus.
