Awareness campaign on measures to reduce the risk of Kovid-19 disease of senior officials of the Royal School of Administration was held on April 08, 2020 in front of the Royal School of Administration.
During this educational outreach, senior students informed the people to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to reduce the risk of infection with Kovid 19, such as:
First: Wash your hands often with soap and clean water or alcohol. Wash your hands with alcohol gel. Second: Cover your mouth and nose when coughing or sneezing with your elbows or toilet paper and throw it in the trash properly. Avoid contact with people who have a fever or flu. 4: Avoid contact with eyes, nose or mouth. 5: Eat well-cooked food.
Students and senior officials also told residents that if there are any symptoms or suspicions related to the disease, please call 115.
At the same time, Mr. Tep Kosal, Director of the First Training Department of the Royal School of Administration, who led the implementation of this social activity, called on cyclo drivers, construction workers, motodup and other people to wash their hands regularly with soap and water. Clean or alcohol, wash your hands regularly and wear a mask regularly to maintain good health, that is, better protection than cure, must always be clean and hygienic.
