The plenary session was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and was attended by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as a total of 115 members of parliament and representatives of the Royal Government.
Defeated by Keut Rith, the new Minister of Justice, the "Draft Law on Ruling the Nation in Emergency" was voted 115 by 115 by all lawmakers.
The draft law on governing the country is in five chapters and divided into 12 articles. This draft law is designed in the spirit of the new Article 22 of the Cambodian Constitution, which states that "when the nation is in danger, the King shall publicly declare the nation in a state of emergency after The consensus of the Prime Minister, President of the National Assembly and President of the Senate.
The draft law also provides a legal basis to ensure the implementation of the new Article 22 of the Constitution and a legal basis to determine the authority of the Royal Government to introduce the necessary measures that are indispensable to respond to the situation in the country. Emergency aims to protect security, public order, protect the life and health of the people, as well as protect property and the environment.
The draft Law on the Management of the State of Emergency will also set out the procedures and conditions for declaring the country in a state of emergency, as well as the necessary measures that the Royal Government has the right to adopt while the country is in a state of emergency. Emergency.
Putting a nation in a state of emergency can only happen when nations are in danger, such as war or foreign aggression, public health emergencies caused by the spread of disease, serious chaos to security National and public order, as well as serious disasters that threaten or endanger the nation.
In the draft law, Article 4, Chapter 3 stipulates that when a country is declared a state of emergency, the Royal Government has the right to issue the following rules:
Legal entities that intentionally do not comply with the measures imposed by the Royal Government as stated in Article 5 shall be criminally liable as stated in Article 42 (Criminal Liability of Legal Entities) of the Penal Code and shall be punished. A fine of 50 million to 500 million riels, as well as one or more additional penalties as stated in Article 168 (additional penalties applicable to legal entities) of the Penal Code.
The decision was made at an emergency meeting in Brussels, the European Union's headquarters. The meeting came after the Spanish prime minister announced that the European country was about to reach the worst point of infection and death due to COVID-19.
The leaders of the United States, Russia and Saudi Arabia made the decision after a telephone conversation on Thursday and were announced by the Russian Government House on Friday morning. The three leaders also agreed to hold a special OPEC + meeting as well as a G20 energy ministerial meeting in a video conference in the near future.
International Committee of the Red Cross donates 20 tons of sanitary ware to General Department of Prisons to prevent 19 Kovid disease in prisons
(Phnom Penh): The International Committee of the Red Cross in Cambodia (ICRC) has donated 20 tons of sanitary ware to the General Department of Prisons to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease in prisons at Correctional Center 1 (M1).
The handover took place this morning, April 10, 2020, with the participation of Mr. Roman Paramonov, President of the ICRC Mission in Cambodia, General Santibandit Chan Kimseng, Director General of the General Department of Prisons, and Mr. Nut Savana. Spokesperson of the General Department of Prisons.
The purpose of sponsoring these materials is to support and complement the efforts of the General Department of Prisons in preventing and controlling the spread of Khovid 19 disease in correctional centers and provincial prisons. The General Department of Prisons is responsible for managing and distributing these materials.
Roman Paramonov said the Kovid 19 epidemic continues to have a significant impact on the world. While the practice of social gaps and hand washing is being practiced by the general public, these points can be considered the most luxurious things in prison. However, the detainees' practice revealed another challenge: the lack of clean air and overcrowding in prisons.
The ICRC also ensures that rehabilitation centers in Battambang and Kampong Speu provinces remain operational. In addition, support with the National Red Cross Society in raising awareness of sanitation, health and safety measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the 13 affected provinces.
