In fact, some may see this as blocking people's freedom of movement, especially during the traditional New Year, when Cambodian families need to get together once a year.
In Europe and the United States, which was under full attack by Kovid-19, which caused hundreds of thousands of deaths and tens of thousands of deaths, it was because people disobeyed the government's instructions and marched incessantly.
In this sense, the Cambodian government, which has decided not to allow its citizens to travel from Phnom Penh to another province, or from one province to another, or from one district to another, is the most viable option. In a spirit of high responsibility and in the concept of "prevention is better than cure".
Especially in the battle against the shadowless enemies such as Kovid-19, etc., do not underestimate the situation at all. Currently, Cambodia has not been severely affected by Kovid-19 yet. This is because the government led by Prime Minister Hun Sen has the wisdom to know and assess the situation properly and know the circumstances and know when to do something.
The process of managing the Prime Minister from the first stage until now is to organize the cell well in both the national and international framework to prevent our country from falling into the disaster of Kovid-19 until This is at a time when countries in the region and the world are deteriorating the most.
So, in conclusion, we, the Cambodian people, have no better choice than to listen to and follow the government's instructions, and especially to miss a New Year's Eve reunion is not something we can not do. New Year celebrations can still be held on the spot with relatives, friends, family on a small scale. But most importantly, "after the New Year, we are safe from Kovid-19, that is good news."
