ASEAN foreign ministers plan to set up ASEAN fund to resolve Kovid crisis 19
(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN Foreign Ministers agreed to establish the ASEAN Fund for the Response to Kovid 19 in order to mobilize financial resources to address the shortage of medical equipment, to support research and development of medicines against Kovid 19 and to use it. For responding to emergencies in the future.
The agreement to establish the fund was made at the 25th meeting of the 19th ASEAN Coordinating Council on Kovid Disease through a video conference, which was held on the morning of April 9, 2020. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News.
The Deputy Prime Minister also proposed the following priorities that ASEAN should focus on:
1. Promote regional cooperation, enhance readiness and response measures to reduce and eliminate the effects of Kovid 19 virus by promoting policy coordination among ASEAN member countries.
3: Continue to provide necessary assistance and support to the people of ASEAN, especially those who are facing difficulties caused by travel restrictions, factory closures and temporary borders, as well as ASEAN people who are unable to seek assistance. And consular support from representatives of their respective countries in third countries.
4. Promote closer consultation to minimize barriers to regional trade and supply chain activities by continuing to open ASEAN markets to ensure the flow of supply. Necessary goods, especially food and medical supplies.
5. Work closely and timely with ASEAN dialogue partners and international organizations, as well as regional and multilateral development banks, to address these challenges not only in the field of public health, but also in the formulation of financial package measures. Immediate, robust, clear and effective to address economic and social impacts.
The meeting ended with all ASEAN Foreign Ministers expressing solidarity in their respective national languages, meaning "We unite with all ASEAN Member States to fight Kovid 19". The meeting hopes that the Special ASEAN Summit on Q 19 and the ASEAN Plus Three Special Summit on QV 19, which will be held on April 14, 2020 via video, will be fruitful.
