Samdech Techo added that the Royal Government will also continue to improve the social protection system, improve the quality of health services and the construction of physical infrastructure, roads, bridges and irrigation, increase electricity sources, continue to expand the power distribution network to cover the whole country, especially At the major economic poles, develop industries, handicrafts, services, transportation, trade, tourism and agriculture to grow more and more.
In this message, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also announced that the Royal Government will continue to make every effort to maintain peace, political stability, security and public order, defend the Constitution, protect the monarchy in accordance with the national and religious motto. The King will protect all the achievements of the Royal Government and the people as a whole in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia is changing its economic structure from a country that depends on agriculture to a country that depends on industry and services. Cambodia has pursued prudent macroeconomic policies and stabilized the economy, and has promoted and promoted economic diversification, competitiveness, and domestic production and consumption.
International trade volume is more than 34.596 million US dollars, while exports are more than 14.915 million US dollars. Exchange rate is stable, inflation rate is low and manageable International reserves are increasing every year due to good foreign direct investment and good balance of payments.
Samdech Techo continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia has announced its strong commitment to deepen reform and encourage more investors to invest in Cambodia, while the Royal Government has organized trade facilitation and strengthened competition for investors. In Cambodia, under the umbrella of peace, democracy, liberal multiparty, without discrimination.
As for the electricity sector, in 2019, the amount supplied by hydropower and coal-fired power plants, which is Cambodia's direct energy source, reached more than 10.620 million kWh compared to the previous year, which was more than 9.660 million. KWh increased by 9.93%.
Connected power lines to the people who use electricity until 2019, the total number of households has reached 2.68 million houses, accounting for 74.78% of the total number of 3.57 houses. Million and covers about 92.68% of the total 14,394 villages in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In the year Kor Eksak BE 2563, due to the favorable weather for rice cultivation throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia, the amount of rainfed and dry season rice production reached more than 10.88 million. Tons is similar to 2018, which we estimate has a surplus of more than 5.76 million tons of rice, equivalent to 3.69 million tons of rice for export. More than 620,000 tons of rice was exported to 59 countries.
Until now, in the Kingdom of Cambodia, industry and handicrafts have grown steadily. There are more than 1,700 factories, mostly garment and footwear factories, and more than 52,000 small and medium-sized industries and handicrafts, which employ a total of nearly 2 million workers.
In line with the growth of industry and handicrafts, the Royal Government has taken care of the living standards of workers by raising the minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment and footwear industries to $ 190 and opening twice a month. 2020, free of charge, other additional benefits from the implementation of the Royal Government's National Social Protection Policy.
Meanwhile, the Royal Government has been assisting more than 60,000 Cambodian workers working abroad, including Thailand, the Republic of Korea, Malaysia, Japan, Singapore, Hong Kong and Saudi Arabia, to ensure legal benefits and technical skills.
The construction sector has been growing with more than 1,700 high-rise buildings from 5 to 40 floors in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and some provinces.
About 6.61 million international tourists came to the Kingdom of Cambodia, an increase of about 6.60%, and about 11.30 million domestic tourists, an increase of about 2.30% compared to 2018 and established There are more than 630,000 direct jobs for Cambodians.
Revenue from tourism was about US $ 4.919 million, an increase of 12.40%, and revenue from ticket sales at Angkor received more than US $ 99 million and more than 2.2 million international tourists visited. This demonstrates the maintenance of security, public order, safety and peace throughout the country by implementing the strict legal measures of the Royal Government.
