Authorities seize more than 30 tons of damaged pig intestines in Kien Svay district, Kandal province
(Kandal): Officials of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) in collaboration with Kandal provincial officials seized more than 30 tons of damaged pig intestines belonging to Mr. But Chanthu, President Food Supply Association of Cambodia. The raid took place on April 8, 2020 on National Road 1 in Chey Udom village, Samrong Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
According to the CPP branch official Kandal province said that after complaints from residents, Kandal provincial authorities, including deputy governors, economic crime police, customs and excise officials, veterinarians, local authorities and district inspectors inspected intestinal products. Two containers of pigs weighing more than 30 tons stored in an unnumbered warehouse located in Chey Udom village, Samrong Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
However, the joint authorities decided to temporarily store these goods in the above warehouse to complete the procedure to be destroyed according to the procedure. The owner of the goods was taken for questioning at the Kandal Provincial Police.
