(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union on April 08, 2020, issued an appeal expressing its full support for the Royal Government's decision to extend the holiday period on the occasion of the Khmer New Year. To prevent as well as prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The appeal states, "We are united by the Cambodian Workers' Happiness Union, a professional organization representing the voices of workers working in enterprises in the textile, garment, footwear and bag factories industries." Institutions in Cambodia would like to express their full support for the Royal Government's decision to extend the holiday period on the occasion of the National New Year 2020. "
This decision is an appropriate measure in response to the real situation to prevent and curb the spread of Kovid 19, a global serious problem. This holiday is one of the most cost-effective options, as enterprises and establishments that will continue to operate normally on the occasion of the traditional New Year are considered to be the safest places for workers in the current situation. Currently.
Of course, the workers who are working in those enterprises, even though they are still working together, they are all non-Kovid 19 and they do not meet with a large group of people. The composition is different: they only meet the same people at work and after work they travel home to meet the same family, so the risk of infection is lower.
On the other hand, if the workers take a break, tens of thousands of workers will be allowed to travel across the country to visit their families in their respective villages and towns. Serious danger to society and family.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on April 08, 2020, issued a sub-decree to extend the time limit for 4 days off on the occasion of Khmer New Year. Coming soon.
