Cambodian Ambassador to Switzerland informs people of extension of Swiss Government's measures to prevent and reduce the spread of Kovid 19 virus
(Switzerland): The Cambodian Embassy in the Swiss Confederation has issued a new notice informing all Cambodians who are staying, working and studying or intending to enter the Swiss Confederation to extend the validity of restrictive measures aimed at preventing and cutting Reduce the transmission of Kovid 19 virus in Switzerland.
The announcement, received by Fresh News on April 9, the Cambodian Embassy in Switzerland has informed the Cambodian people of the extension of the Swiss sanctions as follows:
1. Since March 2020, the Swiss Federal Government has introduced a number of restrictive measures that are valid until April 19, 2020, in order to prevent and reduce the transmission of Kovid 19 virus.
On April 8, 2020, the Swiss Federal Government decided to extend the validity of those measures for another week, until April 26, 2020. The following measures are taken into consideration:
* Public places are closed (eg shops, restaurants, nightclubs, bars, entertainment venues and sports venues, etc.), except for essential stores, food delivery services, pharmacies, postal services, banks, gas stations, public transport, public administration, companies. Power supply and hotel. Locations and businesses that are not affected by the ban must continue to implement the social and sanitation gaps recommended by the Swiss Public Health Authority.
* All private and public gatherings and gatherings of more than five people in public places are prohibited. Gatherings under five are allowed, but must be kept at least two meters apart.
* Prohibit all non-emergency procedures and treatments in hospitals, clinics and medical or dental clinics.
Stay at home as much as possible, especially those who are sick or over 65, except for those who have to go to the doctor to buy food or help others.
3. Restrictions on entry to Switzerland at the border and suspension of visas to Switzerland continue to apply by Swiss authorities. Mr. Chey Rithy, Deputy Director of Legal Department of the General Department of Taxation, volunteered to donate 300,000 Riels for 4 months to the National Commission for Combating Kovid-19
