(Oddar Meanchey): Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governor Mr. Pen Kosal said that on April 8, 2020, about 1,859 Cambodians working in Thailand have returned to Cambodia through the O'Smach border crossing in the city. Samrong and Chrak Choam in Anlong Veng district.
According to Mr. Pen Kosal, on April 8, 2020, the authorities in Thailand's Surin province will not allow people to cross the border between Thailand's Surin province and Cambodia's Oddar Meanchey province to follow the Thai government's measures to prevent the spread. Kovid's disease 19. However, seeing Cambodians crowded along the border, Mr. Pen Kosal also contacted the Surin provincial governor to facilitate the opening of the border for these Cambodians to enter Cambodia.
The people who invaded through the two border crossings in Oddar Meanchey province are not only the people living in Oddar Meanchey province, but also from other provinces. According to the information from the governor of Surin province, Mr. Pen Kosal said that the Cambodian people working in Thailand to cross the border in Oddar Meanchey because the border in other provinces of the two countries are not allowed to enter. Cambodia.
Along with the influx of people from Thailand, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Assistance Team and Mr. Pen Kosal, Provincial Governor, also organized a team of doctors at the border to check the health of people crossing the border. From Thailand and set up a disinfection system before entering Cambodia.
Before being allowed to go to their destination, a team of border guards examined them and instructed them to follow the rules of the Ministry of Health to prevent the transmission and transmission of Kovid 19. In particular, they were advised to isolate themselves for 14 days upon arrival at home to avoid transmitting Kovid 19 to their families in case they became ill.
