(Phnom Penh): Mr. Un Oeun, Member of Samaki Trapeang Chak Agricultural Community in Trapeang Chak Village, Tram Kak Commune, Takeo Province, showed his progress in farming under the guidance and support of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Mr. Un Oeun stated that the business of growing agricultural vegetables on more than 2 hectares of land can earn 65 million riel per year.
Mr. Un Oeun's presentation of progress was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture and his colleagues continued their journey from Kampot to Tram Kak district, Takeo province to inspect the activities of farmers to grow mixed vegetables.
Mr. Un Oeun said that at present, the price of all kinds of safe vegetables has increased significantly after the government closed the import. With the increase in prices, farmers, teachers and some officials and commune authorities will gradually turn to planting crops to seize this opportunity to increase agricultural productivity and contribute to ensuring local food supply. Height of living standard to gradually improve.
