(Oddar Meanchey): On the morning of April 8, 2020, about 244 Cambodians left Thailand and returned to Cambodia through the O'Smach International Border Crossing in Samrong City. But this morning, Thai authorities decided to close the border to prevent people from crossing the border, so these workers were temporarily detained at the border.
Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, asked the authorities to intervene on the Thai side and open the way for the 244 Cambodians to come to Cambodia. After this intervention, the Thai authorities also agreed to open the door for the Cambodian workers to enter Cambodia.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the National Task Force for Oddar Meanchey Province, said that after arriving in Cambodia, the 244 Cambodians were subjected to primary health check-ups for 19 Kovid. The senior minister confirmed that none of the 244 people had 19 cases of Kovid.
In addition to medical check-ups, authorities and border guards also educate workers on health care measures when returning home, especially to be isolated for 14 days and to contact village authorities for health information. After educating the authorities and the provincial working group, the 244 workers were sent to their respective hometowns.
