Minister of Social Affairs Conducts Consultation Meeting on the Mechanism of Rapid Survey on the Impact of 19 Kovid Diseases in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, on April 8, 2020, chaired a consultation meeting on the mechanism of rapid survey of the impact of Kovid 19 on the implementation of cash subsidies for pregnant women. Pregnancy and children under 2 years.
The meeting was also attended by representatives of the Ministry of Planning, the General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Support, relevant units of the Ministry and online participation with development partners and the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in the 25 capitals and provinces.
During the meeting, Minister Vong Soth initiated ideas and long-term vision to prepare in advance for the provision of social assistance interventions to poor and vulnerable families in accordance with the policies and mechanisms of the Royal Government. Recently created. The most important goal is to ensure the provision of social services to truly poor families in a timely manner.
Minister Vong Soth also instructed all specialized units of the Ministry and the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of the 25 provinces to be more active to monitor the changes in the people at their local level. Plan responses and provide timely interventions in the provision of social services.
In addition, the Economic and Monetary Policy Committee has set up a working group to design and manage social assistance mechanisms to assist the poor and vulnerable during the fight against Kovid 19, composed of relevant ministries and institutions. Led by Ms. Nguon Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The task force is tasked with identifying poor families, vulnerable groups and other people in need of protection during the fight against Kovid 19. The working group must develop specific intervention measures and action plans to address the impacts and help stabilize the lives of the target groups.
