Siem Reap Provincial Health Department Continues to Receive Donations of Alcohol Masses from Donors to Fight Kovid 19
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Health Department on April 7, 2020 received a donation of alcohol, mass, glycerin, oxygen from the Cambodian Business Club to contribute to the Cambodian government in the fight against Kovid-19.
Ms. Ly Vannak, Director of the Pharmaceutical Office of the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, said that the contribution of the philanthropists of the Cambodian Business Club for today, the Department of Health received 20 cans of alcohol per 30 liters, 50 boxes of mass, glycerin. 25 bottles, 60 pieces of oxygenated water, worth about 10 million riels.
Mr. Pon Panha, a representative of the Cambodian Business Club, said that the reason he brought these materials to the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, seeing that Cambodia, as well as around the world are working hard to fight Kovid-19. Therefore, on behalf of the Cambodian people, help contribute to the government by providing materials such as alcohol and masks to the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department for daily use.
He added that in addition to providing materials such as alcohol and masks to the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, the Cambodian Business Club also provided these materials to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration and also plans to prepare food to distribute to people who come. From Thailand and was kept in isolation for 14 days as well.
