Want to know more about her work, please visit Facebook: Ally Rendall, Minister of Education and Minister of Information, sign an agreement on the production and dissemination of electronic curricula
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Information on April 08, 2020 organized the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on the production and dissemination of distance learning programs and e-learning.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, at the Ministry of Education this morning, April 8, 2020.
The signing of this agreement aims to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in controlling and preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia and in the spirit of ensuring equitable education services, especially for rural students to receive the same quality education. Students in the city.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron confirmed that the Ministry of Education, in collaboration with the Ministry of Information, has signed this Memorandum of Understanding to set up an educational television channel to broadcast online lectures on television so that students can learn across the country.
At the same time, the Minister of Education also instructed all parents to provide their children with a proper place to study, such as desks, chairs and textbooks, etc., in order to have control over online learning.
In addition, Minister Hang Chuon Naron confirmed that in the future, the Ministry will set up an additional question and answer system to make it easier for students who have questions when studying online.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that to date, the number of students who have registered as well as used online learning is about 20 percent of the total 3 million students.
