(Kampot): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, this morning, April 08, 2020, instructed farmers who produce vegetables, fish, meat to seize the golden opportunity to create production in both quantity and quality to supply demand. District while Cambodia reduces imports to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The Minister's introduction was made during his visit to inspect the actual activities and progress of the project on "Dissemination of new agricultural techniques that are resistant to climate change called ASPIRE in Banteay Meas district, Kampot province."
Visiting the vegetable farm, meeting with Mr. Tes Sary and Mr. Yim Bon, the owner of the farm and the head of the community, he received a lot of important information that arises from the implementation of this project, both positive and negative points. Income savings in the community, implementation of techniques such as cultivation, maintenance, harvesting, packaging, storage, labeling, transportation, lack of water resources and some other important support infrastructure.
The Minister continued to meet with community members and the broiler business community about the significant achievements made in implementing the project on living standards, well-being and health, mainly related to Kovid-19.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister thanked the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the IFAD Foundation for supporting and financing the implementation of the ASPIRE program with remarkable results.
He said that assistance for the development of the agricultural sector, focusing on raising the standard of living by increasing productivity, promoting the implementation of diversified agriculture using modern technologies in response to climate change, capacity building of farmers, business units. And agricultural communities based on the goodwill of the Royal Government's long-term initiatives and vision for 2030 and 2050.
He added that the program is currently having a positive impact on poverty reduction and increasing resilience to climate change for poor farmers, small production scale and vulnerability, focusing on: First, improving the efficiency of responsive agricultural services. And the needs of smallholder farmers; and secondly, to help those farmers to know how to run agribusiness from subsistence to commercial farming, be resilient to climate change, and become entrepreneurs in rural areas.
The Minister requested the provincial, district and commune authorities to fully cooperate with the provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to facilitate and provide all kinds of support in the main direction is to increase domestic production sufficiently while: We block the import of agricultural products from outside.
In order to make the implementation of the project more effective and efficient, the Minister requested the officers of the relevant professional units and all relevant inter-institutional officials to develop strategies, action plans to make the implementation of the program better as expected. And the use of transparent financing in a responsible manner in response to the real needs of the people and the strategy of the Royal Government.
He urged all to increase vigilance to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 effectively by strictly following the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
Please be informed that in the press conference on "Evolution 19" on April 7, Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people to work hard to promote local production, including raising pigs, chickens, ducks. Fish and vegetables to meet domestic demand, taking this golden opportunity to create opportunities for agriculture as we reduce imports to contribute to the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19.
