It should be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of March 31, 2020, chaired a meeting of the Standing Committee of the Council of Ministers to review the draft law on national emergency management.
In a press release showing the results of the meeting, it was stated that the draft law has been reviewed and sent to the National Assembly for review and approval without submitting it to the full meeting of the Council of Ministers.
The draft law states that the state of emergency is drafted in the spirit of the new Article 22 of the Cambodian Constitution, which states: "When the nation is in danger, His Majesty "Public announcement to put the country in a state of emergency after the approval of the Prime Minister, the President of the National Assembly and the President of the Senate."
The draft law on governing the country is in five chapters and 11 articles. Chapter 1 contains two articles on general provisions that set out the purpose of drafting this law and the scope of this law.
Chapter 2 deals with the procedures and conditions for declaring a country in a state of emergency. Emergency and Regime Report on emergency measures to the National Assembly and the Senate. Chapter 3 also has two articles.
Chapter 4 has three articles on provisions. This chapter deals with the penalties for obstructing operations when the country is in a state of emergency, the penalties for disobeying measures when the country is in a state of emergency, and the criminal liability of legal entities.
The request of Samdech Techo Prime Minister was made in the press conference regarding the current status of Kovid 19 on April 7, 2020 at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is very concerned about the health, safety and mobility of workers from Thailand, despite the well-managed more than 60,000 workers who came to Cambodia. However, for workers who continue to come and plan to come to Cambodia, there is a real concern.
Therefore, the Royal Government would like to appeal to the Cambodian workers who are working and staying in Thailand, if there is still work, there is a proper place to stay there, please do not return to Cambodia to prevent Kovid 19 infection, because if you come When I returned home, I had to stay in solitary confinement for 14 days, and when I returned to work in Thailand, I had to stay in solitary confinement for 14 days. In total, it was not easy.
The Prime Minister continued that despite the concerns about the movement of Cambodian workers from Thailand, the Royal Government of Cambodia can not close the border to prevent people from entering the country, but must take measures to prevent disease. This spread to the country and its families, especially the authorities have to control the situation of some workers entering and leaving through various corridors.
The head of the Royal Government added that among the options presented by the Committee for the Prevention of Kovid 19 to Samdech to solve the problem of workers from Thailand, Samdech Techo decided to choose the fourth option is to allow the return, but to strengthen control. Check with delivery to the local and manage the local thoroughly. Paragon International University launches online video conferencing via Google Meet
