The senior minister also urged all relevant authorities to continue to monitor the people in the villages and communes just returned from Thailand and advised them to stay away from their families for 14 days.
As a result, to date, about 700 people in Anlong Veng and Trapeang Prasat districts have not been infected with Kovid 19, he said.
However, in order to prevent the transmission of 19 smallpox from people in Thailand to their families and in the community, the senior minister urged the medical staff to be careful in measuring the temperature of people from Thailand. Thailand will advise them who have just returned from Thailand to live separately from their families for 14 days.
Please note that there are nearly 4,000 Cambodians in Oddar Meanchey province who have just returned from Thailand. The Thai residents have been quarantined by the authorities to make sure they are free of Kovid 19 and not transmitted to their families and villagers.
