(Kandal): Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kandal Province, on April 6, 2020, paid tribute to the body of Colonel Min Bun Chhean, Director of the Anti-Drug Office of Kandal Provincial Police. Died on April 5, 2020 in Leuk Dek commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province by disease.
During the condolence ceremony, Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat expressed his deepest condolences for the loss of Colonel Min Bun Chhean, as well as the loss of a police officer who had previously served the people and the Royal Government.
Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat handed over 7,300,000 Riels and US $ 1,860 to the family of Colonel Min Bun Chhean to facilitate the funeral. After paying his respects and handing over the money, Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat urged the specialized office to prepare enough documents to expedite the payment of 6,000,000 Riels to the Friends of the Police Association to the families of the dead.
