Three arrested after rescuing a suspect at Mondulkiri Provincial Court
(Mondulkiri): Mondulkiri Provincial Armed Forces arrested 3 out of 5 people after releasing Touch Hoeun in a criminal case (using violence against real estate occupants) to Mondulkiri Provincial Court .
Mr. Ai Chamnap, Director of the Justice Research Department of the Mondulkiri Provincial Gendarmerie, told Fresh News Unit in Mondulkiri Province on the morning of April 6, 2020: "Come and release the accused to court at 8:10 pm on April 5, 2020, where he himself beat the three of them."
He added that three people were arrested, including the mother, wife and siblings of the accused, and two others escaped, including one of the accused's father. According to the disclosure from the authorities, the case of Touch Hoeun, who was detained by the police, did not have a detention letter from the magistrate, so the families of the accused came to release Touch Hoeun. .
According to the military, Touch Hoeun also did not have a certificate to release Touch Hoeun. The accused are currently being questioned by a trial judge on whether to detain him today. Separately, three suspects are being questioned by the provincial military authorities and sent to the prosecutor's office may be charged.
Please be informed that a land trader was arrested by the Mondulkiri Provincial Gendarmerie after receiving a complaint about the use of violence against the legal occupants of the real estate and the fraudulent sale of other people's land.
According to the report, the man who arrested the former teacher and now a land broker who was making a lot of money was arrested by the Mondulkiri Provincial Gendarmerie after the police received a complaint from the victim. In criminal matters.
