Last February, Samdech Techo announced a reduction of about 443 million US dollars. The decision to cut the two national budget expenditures saves the Royal Government a total of 918 million US dollars to solve the problem caused by Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces another reduction in the national budget at the press conference on solving the problem caused by Kovid 19 on April 7, 2020. With the announcement of the reduction of national budget expenditures, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked for the understanding of the leaders and civil servants in various ministries and institutions.
"I understand the national institutions at all levels, both national and sub-national, that the government is forced to cut spending twice. The first is to reduce spending by $ 443 million, and yesterday I issued an order at the request of HE Aun Porn Moniroth to reduce spending by another $ 475 million. In total, the two expenses were reduced by 918 million US dollars. Samdech Techo, head of the Royal Government, emphasized.
Samdech Techo stated that these state budgets must be opened to ministries and institutions, but must be withdrawn for use in resolving the current crisis.
It should be noted that in 2020, the Royal Government plans to spend about 8,223 million dollars, of which about 4.888 million dollars from the state budget and 3,335 million dollars from the state budget. But now decided to withdraw $ 918 million to fight the crisis caused by Kovid 19.
