Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed this on the morning of April 7, 2020 in a press conference related to the current news of Kovid 19 at the Peace Palace.
Samdech reiterated that as long as doctors can not protect or do not have protective equipment will not be allowed to treat 19 patients. According to the Prime Minister, the Royal Government must have at least 10 million masks and the medical team must have at least 5,000 masks.
Samdech continued, "I have already bought 5,000 sets of medical uniforms, but I will buy another 5,000 sets for the Royal Government's reserve stock when the Ministry of Health uses up, the Royal Government has to release them." When the Royal Government releases 1,000 copies, buy another 1,000 copies and keep 5,000 copies in stock. "N95 medical masks have another 500,000 masks to buy in stock, so that doctors do not run out."
