Highlights of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Speaking and Answering Questions at the Press Conference on Kovid 19 Update
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, April 7, 2020, held a press conference for about 4 hours regarding the current status of Kovid 19 disease. The press conference was held at the Peace Palace, with live broadcasts on TV, Fresh News and many other Cambodian media outlets.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech and answering questions with the media:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that our people are easily frightened, panicked and forgetful, so Samdech thought of a scenario for future plans for Kovide 19.
* Samdech stated that the Cambodian people must not be happy to forget themselves, there must be additional measures that will be announced as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the medical team for testing 19 Kovid, both Cambodia and its partners.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the front line doctors for treating 19 Kovid patients. As for medical equipment, the Royal Government is always ready not to be short of doctors.
* Samdech thanked the King and Samdech Mey, as well as other philanthropists who have so far received more than 11 million dollars in the hands of Mr. Mam Bun Heng
* Samdech Techo thanked political officials and officials at all levels for donating their salaries to the National Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19, which has more than 1,800 people as of yesterday.
* Samdech Techo stated that the salary donation for officials will be implemented from May, because the salary for April is already open.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this salary donation requires each official to make a letter on their own voluntarily.
* Samdech Techo thanked the World Health Organization, the World Bank and other partners for helping Cambodia with Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some countries have lost tens of thousands of lives due to 19 Kovids, but still criticized Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he asked the World Health Organization to evaluate the management through the public health sector, which country died more and which country died less due to Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Expresses Condolences to Cambodians Who Killed 19 Kovids Abroad, Including the United States
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks more than 150 Cambodians traveling by air from Malaysia to understand the denial of entry into Cambodia because we need to prevent the spread of the disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government hopes that the decision to increase the allowance for front-line doctors will not be envied
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the Cambodian army, which is out of the country with the outbreak of Kovid 19, to take care of its health and be very careful.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that, first, the fight against the 19 cases of Kovid infection imported from outside must continue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks for understanding from more than 150 Cambodians in Malaysia, please continue to stay in Malaysia first.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Royal Government is really concerned about the workers from Thailand, but despite the concerns, we can not close the border and not take back our citizens.
* Samdech Techo hopes that Cambodian workers with proper jobs will not return to Cambodia during the upcoming New Year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to Cambodian workers in Thailand, if they have a job or accommodation in Thailand, if possible, please do not return to Cambodia by staying there because Cambodia must be kept separate for 14 days.
* Samdech Techo stated that the second arrow that the Royal Government is fighting is to prevent transmission from the sick to the unborn.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government has no plans to close pagodas, temples or places of worship, but the Royal Government calls for respect for homes and arranges for gaps as directed by the Ministry of Health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the best measure to prevent Kovid 19 is to educate the people.
* Samdech Techo thanked all the media for providing educational messages to the people on how to prevent Kovid 19. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not thank those who polluted the information.
Samdech Techo stated that the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and our doctors, despite being despised, worked well to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the suspension of the traditional Khmer New Year to prevent the spread of Kovid, while state institutions and private companies continue to work normally and the state will reimburse for 5 days when appropriate.
* Samdech Techo proposed to prevent the spread to the community because it is the most dangerous issue that must continue to work on this.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he asked civil servants, workers and workers to ask for understanding on this difficult decision of the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also requested to reduce travel to his hometown and other places to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo calls on workers to continue working to get the money, waiting for the rest of the day off when appropriate.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a group with a strong character is asking the World Health Organization for Cambodia to show how to treat Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has prepared more than 3,000 treatment rooms.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia was also ready to reserve a team of doctors, including volunteer doctors, who paid directly for 100 days.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is always ready to stock up on medical equipment to ensure that our medical team is not in short supply.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Ministry of Health must sign with SKD and another company to buy alcohol to buy stocks for storage.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the two factories will help Cambodia have enough alcohol to use.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered the Ministry of Commerce to control the quality of alcohol traffic.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he had ordered the Ministry of Health to sign an agreement to purchase oxygen from a private company.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the case of rice, salt, fish, the Royal Government is prepared not to run out.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged people to expand the cultivation of vegetables and livestock to supply the local market, which is in need while imports are reduced.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered the Ministry of Agriculture to encourage people to cultivate vigorously to meet local needs, which are opportunities for agriculture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call for the understanding of the private sector to reduce the rent.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the banking sector should not confiscate land, houses and should delay the construction, reduce interest rates, etc. for the affected people.
Regarding the banking sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen told Mr. Pich Sros, President of the Cambodian Youth Party, not to take the words of Samdech Keng for political gain.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reacts to analysts who make inappropriate comments regarding the creation of a law on the country in times of emergency.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that placing the country in an emergency, if not necessary, is not used for fear of affecting the national economy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that the people will accept the Royal Government's request to suspend the New Year, but not to suspend the New Year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the economies of all countries in the world have been affected by the 19 diseases of Kovid to Cambodia as well, but the extent of the impact has not been assessed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the industrial and service sectors were severely affected, but the agricultural sector was the biggest beneficiary.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if the situation returns to normal, Cambodia will be ready for the affected factories and companies, but there will also be a diversion from production to export to produce to replace imports.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as of April 6, 2020, there are more than 100 factories in Cambodia that have closed due to lack of raw materials and buyers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in Cambodia, there is a mass factory in Sihanoukville that produces and supplies to the Royal Government of Cambodia, and some companies are applying to divert garment production to mass production.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that not allowing more than 150 Cambodians in Malaysia to come to Cambodia is not a virtue, but a difficult time, only to ask for their understanding so as not to affect more than 16 million Cambodians. People.
* Samdech Cho Hun Sen raises his hand to beg for the people's understanding for the suspension of the New Year, because if there is an infection, the dead are the people themselves.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for the people who violated the ban of the Royal Government to suspend the New Year, the Royal Government has nothing to punish, but Samdech has raised his hand to beg for understanding.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 is a lesson for Cambodia to strengthen itself, strengthen ownership, solve problems.
* Regarding the factory shutdown, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a worker must receive $ 70 per month, including $ 40 from the government and $ 30 from the factory owner, without requiring the same skills training as before.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that China had provided assistance for the fight against the 19 diseases of Kovid arrived in Cambodia before the outbreak and that Cambodia had not yet used Chinese aid.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia respects China's sovereignty, treating it as respecting Cambodia's sovereignty.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech is open to military exercises like with China, although the United States, Samdech accepted but had to undergo medical examinations like the Chinese military.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia does not take any country as an enemy, even if Cambodia does not establish diplomatic relations because Cambodia does not support the separation of states.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the probability of Kovid 19 disease is only 0.1% in the country of emergency, but Cambodia needs to have this law in hand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The declaration of a state of emergency is still very low because the result of Kovid disease is only 0.1%
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the use of the law, the placement of the country in times of emergency, is used only during the rhetoric.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that, in Samdech's view, only the King, the acting head of state, can declare a country in a state of emergency only if there is a legal interpretation of the council. Charter.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Ministry of Health to hold a press conference on the development of Kovid 19 once a week.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Kovid 19 crisis has led the Royal Government to adjust policies such as reducing the costs of national and sub-national institutions and diverting economic focus by promoting agriculture to ensure domestic food security. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ends the press conference at 12:40 pm (approximately 4 hours). Ms. Nou Vanny was elected as a Member of Parliament for Takeo Constituency and Mr. Loy Sophat was elected as the Chairman of the Third Commission in place of Mr. Chea Vandeth.
The meeting was held in the presence of Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly. The meeting also discussed and approved a number of other agendas, including:
* Appointed Mr. Chay Borin as Deputy Chairman of the Economic, Financial, Banking and Auditing Committee to replace Mr. Loy Sophat * Appointed Ms. Ly Kimleang as Secretary of the Economic, Financial, Banking and Auditing Commission to replace Mr. Chay Borin Economic, Financial, and Banking Audit Committee on behalf of Ms. Ly Kimleang
At the same time, the meeting approved the handing over of the draft law on "Management of the country in a state of emergency" to the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly in cooperation with the National Assembly Committee on Interior, National Defense and Public Works. To the National Assembly Standing Committee.
