(Kampong Thom): While the Royal Government of Cambodia is working hard to prevent and combat 19 cases of Kovid every day, lower-level authorities are also busy educating and disseminating measures taken by the Ministry of Health. In fact, in Baray and Taing Kork districts of Kampong Thom province, these activities are also being carried out vigorously.
Baray and Taing Kork districts are known as the strengthening bases of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kampong Thom Province, which the Minister always visits to support supply as well as provide Many recommendations to the authorities and the working group to implement to serve the people with all their strength.
On the day of the outreach to the people in Treal commune, Mr. Hak Mong Huot, the governor of Tang Kork district, a newly established district in Kampong Thom province, said that as of April 4, 2020, foreign workers There are 776 people in Tang Kork district, most of them from Thailand.
The district governor confirmed that during the influx of workers into Tang Kork district, the district administration did not neglect the slightest by ordering the authorities in the commune to educate and disseminate the measures of the Ministry of Health, as well as to monitor. The health of the people every day, and he himself always goes to do these activities on a regular basis, even though some days are late at night, the team never complains.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot continued that in addition to the above-mentioned educational activities, the working group of Tang Kork District Administration, as well as himself, always brought gifts of food, budget and some materials to distribute to the poor people, the elderly, etc. Whether they are people who have lived in the past or workers who have just come from abroad.
While sitting under the house while isolating himself, Mr. Chea Ton, a resident of Svay Moung village, Treal commune, Tang Kork district, described that he and his five children had returned home since the 22nd. March, while his wife, Neang Rin, returned home on March 18.
Mr. Chea Ton and Ms. Neang Rin and their children went to work at Long Klung Market, Sa Kaeo Province, Thailand, but after learning that there was an outbreak of Kovid 19 in Thailand, the family returned home when Arriving home immediately and receiving instructions from the authorities, this model family began to adhere strictly.
Ms. Neang Rin said that every day, the village chief goes to check the temperature with the thermometer, as well as the district and commune authorities to visit and monitor the health. However, the symptoms of Mr. Chea Ton and Ms. Neang Rin and their five children are not abnormal, that is, they are in good health.
Through his activities as well as supporting the local people, Mr. Hak Mong Huot always received financial contributions as well as food from the monks and philanthropists to be distributed. To people in need.
It is also good news for Taing Kork district that so far no one has been suspected of contracting Kovid 19, both residents and migrant workers. Normal health.
Despite such exemplary results, the governor of Taing Kork district continues to encourage people to participate in the implementation of the measures of the Ministry of Health and the Royal Government to protect health and safety in the community.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot is determined not to loosen his grip on the fight against Kovid 19, he will continue to lead the team to continue activities until the Kovid 19 problem is gone from Cambodia.
Not much different from the Tang Kork district administration in Baray district, they also actively follow the instructions of Minister Thong Khon and the Kampong Thom provincial administration. Mr. Khorn Chanthai, Deputy Governor of Baray District, said that as of April 4, 2020, 291 workers from abroad came to Baray District, of which 248 were mostly from Thailand (female 95) other than that from Malaysia, Korea and so on.
The deputy district governor said that after receiving instructions related to the 19 cases of Kovid, the district administration has taken measures as well as controlling the statistics of the workers, including educational measures, disseminating measures to stay separately for 14 days as instructed by the Ministry. Health. Village and village officials took the heat of the people who came to stay for 14 days and set it aside every morning.
Although four people from Baray district were sampled at the Institut Pasteur du Cambodge, they were not infected or infected with Kovid 19 (negative).
Among the people from Thailand, Mr. Sisay and Ms. Suong Sat have returned from Bangkok as a couple since March 22, 2020, and so far their health is as normal as ever. There is nothing wrong with the times, as the village chief also comes down to check the heat at the back of the house on a regular basis.
Suong Sat is often seen in isolation from a remote house in Chong Dong commune, Baray district. She also follows consistently, does not dare to be a little careless, and always follows the news or posts on Facebook.
As for the accommodation and food of the family, Ms. Suong Sat did not have any problem, even though she wanted to go here and there during this time, she did not dare to go here to protect the safety and health of all.
According to Mr. Khorn Chanthay, local people in Baray district, especially workers from abroad, do not have any suspected symptoms of Kovid 19 infection, while village chiefs in all villages regularly monitor the health of villagers.
As a new example, when they received information from the border that there were workers coming to the Baray district, the district, commune and village authorities went to the workers' houses, urging the families to prepare a separate place. Separate and prepare for the workers who are traveling to increase the effectiveness of prevention and control of infection.
Samdech Techo's remarks after Cambodia decided not to allow more than 150 Cambodians traveling by air from Malaysia to enter Cambodia to help prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
In a press conference related to the current outbreak of Kovid 19 at the Peace Palace this morning, April 7, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked more than 150 Cambodians in Malaysia to understand the denial of entry into Cambodia due to Prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked people abroad to pay attention to the procedures in their country as well. Samdech confirmed that Samdech's decision last night was a painful decision, but there is no choice but to ask the 150 people in Malaysia who are ready to fly to Cambodia today, please understand to stay there first.
Samdech Techo also asked all 150 Malaysians, wherever you are, to stay there first, do not be lazy, because we have already seen that there are 100 people coming, about 80 people, and one Cambodian student from the United States. Immediately arrived at Chak Angre A Cambodian student from Japan arrived at Chak Angre immediately for treatment, so the situation at the moment, the transmission of disease from outside into the country is in a very important situation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "Last night, I made a difficult decision regarding 150 brothers and sisters in Malaysia. We can only ask him to stay there for the greater good of the nation. There is no other choice." "And no, I am not virtuous ... This is a difficult time, we just ask for his understanding so that he can understand the 16 million people in the country not to be infected."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his condolences to the Cambodian people who died due to Kovid 19 in foreign countries, including the United States.
This statement by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made during a press conference for about 4 hours this morning, April 7, 2020, regarding the current status of Kovid 19 disease at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "We should hold a press conference on the development of Kovid 19 once a week, in addition to the Ministry of Health issued a daily press release on this disease, setting any day to provide information from Update on Kovid 19 disease.
In addition, Samdech Techo continued, "In case of emergency of Kovid 19, the Ministry of Health can hold a press conference different from the extraordinary."
Speaking at a press conference on the current outbreak of Kovid 19 at the Peace Palace on April 7, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the declaration of a state of emergency is only if the country is at a level where it is no longer heard. .
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, although the possibility of declaring a country in a state of emergency is small, he urges that there be no legal loophole because the declaration of a state of emergency cuts Civil rights affect the economy and many more.
In the opinion of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the declaration of a state of emergency should be made by the King only, with the suggestion that the Acting Head of State may declare a state of emergency only if there is a legal interpretation. From the Constitutional Council. Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that the law on the management of the country in a state of emergency may be issued after the Khmer New Year.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this request on the occasion of his speech at a press conference on the current 19 cases of Kovid at the Peace Palace. The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia requested: "The Royal Government proposes to reduce travel to hometowns or recreational areas to avoid the transmission of germs from one place to another or to bring germs into the house or bring from "From the city to the countryside or from the countryside back to the city."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked civil servants, workers and workers to ask for understanding on this difficult decision of the Royal Government. Samdech Techo calls on workers to continue working to get money, waiting for the rest of the day to be repaid at an appropriate time. Therefore, for the budget that the Royal Government has sponsored for the traditional Khmer New Year, there is no withdrawal.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia continued that for the New Year, all Cambodians should prepare to receive the New Year angels in their homes as usual, there is no ban. However, the Royal Government prohibits the celebration of New Year and gatherings, games and trips to other areas only.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the call for people not to travel to other areas is among the measures to prevent the spread of COVID-19 virus. Therefore, the Royal Government has also announced the suspension of the upcoming New Year celebrations and will not allow public and private institutions to rest, declaring normal work and the state will reimburse at At any convenient time as well.
At the same time, Samdech Techo added that even taking a break is not a good thing because the Royal Government has banned him from going to his hometown. On the other hand, the people in the countryside are afraid that the people in the city will bring disease to the countryside, and the people in the city are also afraid to bring disease from the countryside to the city. .
