(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, April 7, 2020, held a press conference related to the latest news of Kovid 19. The press conference was held at the Peace Palace with live broadcasts on TV, Fresh News and many other Cambodian media outlets.
In today's press conference, in addition to delivering messages related to 19 cases of measles to the people, the Prime Minister also opened the media to ask questions on this topic.
It should be noted that since Cambodia contracted Kovid 19 in January 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has appeared in four conferences, including today's conference. The first conference will be held on January 30, the second conference will be held on February 24, the third conference will be held on March 30 and the fourth conference will be held on the morning of April 7.
This press conference is an important message to the Cambodian people who want to understand the measures and solutions of the Royal Government, especially of the Prime Minister himself in the face of the epidemic of Kovid 19, as well as Crisis response comes from this disease.
It should also be noted that as of April 6, 2020, Cambodia has found 114 cases of 19 cases of Kovid, of which 53 have been cured and 61 are being treated. In particular, in the last three days, there have been no new infections.
With the development of Kovid 19, it is seen as an optimal situation for Cambodia, as many countries in the world, especially developed economies such as the United States and Europe are facing a dire situation. Bad.
There is no difference between the treatment and prevention of Kovid 19 disease in both low-income and advanced health countries, as no cure has been found for the disease. No. But now, countries with advanced health care, such as the United States and Europe, are plagued by epidemics, while some countries with less-than-strong health care in Asia are less affected.
At this point, it is highly valued for measures and measures to prevent serious transmission. In the United States and Europe, it is seen that measures and measures to prevent the spread of the disease are weak, making the disease spread rapidly.
In Asia, including Cambodia, it is seen that due to the effective control and prevention of person-to-person transmission, the transmission is not as strong.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always said that overcoming Kovid 19 does not depend on rich or poor countries, countries with advanced or declining medicine, but on reliance on situation management and deployment. Measures to prevent transmission effectively.
Cambodia is seen as paying close attention to preventing the spread of disease from person to person through education and the timely introduction of measures to close meeting places. Participate in following the spirit of the Royal Government consistently.
