(Phnom Penh): A man who tied a 4-month-pregnant woman to the door of the house has been identified as 41-year-old Ou Bunthy, an official at the Phnom Penh Department of Public Works and Transport. Sreng Chheng Lin, a 61-year-old female landlord.
In connection with this issue, the governor of Por Senchey district, Mr. Hem Darith, ordered the authorities to take legal action.
"On behalf of me, as the chairman of the Po Sen Chey District Unity Command, I will urge all authorities to arrest this perpetrator and resolve it legally," he said.
According to local authorities, the suspect has now escaped, and he urged the authorities to arrest the suspect for legal action.
According to the victim's complaint, on April 5, 2020, at 1:00 pm, prior to the incident, the victim went to move the belongings of his sister, Srey Mao, who rented room A4 in Prey Tea village. Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Sen Chey.
When the victim arrived, he moved his luggage on a tricycle to bring a new rented room next to the old rented room, while the old landlord came to the scene until there was a verbal dispute by tying the victim with a scarf next to the door Once. The woman is currently giving birth at Sovannara Maternity Hospital.
