Intergovernmental Committee for the Prevention of Kovid 19 19th Meeting to Prepare a Plan to Prevent Challenges
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission on Combating Kovid 19, this morning, April 6, 2020, chaired a meeting to prepare a plan to prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19 in Cambodia, where the meeting was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Interior, relevant institutions and governors of the 25 capitals and provinces.
According to the intervention presented at the meeting, the Intergovernmental Commission on the Prevention of Kovid 19 has set up two health checkpoints at the border and at the provincial level to monitor workers from Thailand. There are four locations for the establishment of the center: the border center, the provincial level, the district level, and the home level.
Monitoring Phase 1: When workers arrive at the border, they must be inspected at the border health checkpoint, and if the temperature is below 38 degrees, they should be sent to the provincial health checkpoint for further monitoring. However, if the temperature is above 38 degrees, it should be sent to the Border Charity Center, and if the test is positive, 19 should be sent to the hospital.
Follow-up Phase 2: When sending workers to the provincial health check-up center and asymptomatic, they should be sent to the district-level medical check-up center. However, if there are any suspicious symptoms, they should be sent to the provincial chapters and if the test is positive, they should be sent to the hospital.
Follow-up phase 3: When sending workers to the district-level cadastral center and there is no suspicion, they are allowed to have cataracts at home. However, if there are any suspicious symptoms, they should be sent to the provincial chapters and if the test is positive, they should be sent to the hospital.
Phase 4 follow-up: This is a follow-up of the laboratories of each worker until they show no signs of suspected Kovid 19 infection.
