(Phnom Penh): To support the fight against Kovid-19 with the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, the leading payment technology company Pi Pay has developed a new service that makes it easy to pay and receive money from customers. Free in order to prevent the risk of infection that can be transmitted through banknotes.
The launch of this new service is meant to make it easier for all Pi Pay customers to make payments as well as receive money from customers without having to deal directly with the banknotes, as banknotes can be risky. High in transmission of Kovid-19 virus.
After successful registration, merchants can earn additional fees by providing payment services to other customers, such as: 1: Can be an agent to provide mobile top-up services and receive fees directly from customers 2: Can Be an agent to pay billing services and receive fees directly from customers 3: Can provide deposit and withdrawal services and receive direct fees from customers and many other services.
