Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Although our country is not as modern as others, we have clear measures for our people not to fall into fear of losing hope in life
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the evening of April 5, 2020, through his official Facebook page, Samdech stated, "Although we are not as modern as other countries, we have clear practical measures to solve the problem. "We can save our people from falling into the fear of losing hope in life."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement after the head of the Royal Government and Chairman of the Committee on Combating Kovid 19 committed measures to ensure the safety of the people, including food security.
To ensure local food supply, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen recently suspended rice and paddy exports and allowed only fragrant rice to be exported, as Cambodia is now fighting. And Kovid 19 Infectious Diseases. But yesterday, April 4, Samdech Techo Prime Minister issued an order to suspend the export of fish from the country.
In addition to suspending the export of fish, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also ordered the authorities to regulate the market not to raise fish prices and ban the export of fish in the current situation. This is to save for the needs of the people in the country.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister also managed the local noodle factory to produce noodles for the Royal Government to supply to the people who do not have food. At the same time, Samdech Techo has prepared for the country's pure water factory to produce bottled water to provide for the people.
"I would like to take this opportunity to call on all our citizens and all relevant institutions, local authorities and all relevant parties to continue to participate in the prevention of the transmission of the Kovid 19 virus from one person to another," she said. "And in particular, we need to cut off the transmission of the Kovid 19 virus from individuals into our community, which is very important."
She added, "These results also show that the management and prevention work in the implementation of effective measures by the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia is gradually effective. "This copy also confirms that Cambodia has done gradually, but our caution is still there because it can not be done in the short term and we do not relax."
