Another Cambodian in the US dies of Kovid 19 due to delays in medical treatment in New York City (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Another Cambodian in the US dies of Kovid 19 19 at 11:45 am, Saturday, April 4, 2020. The death was claimed to have been caused by the doctor's inattention to take the patient to the hospital.
The Cambodian who died of Kovid 19 was 54-year-old Puch Raksmey, who lives in New York City, USA.
Doctors rushed the patient to a hospital in New York City. According to Mr. Chea Huang, the doctors did not go to pick up the patient for fear of infection, requiring the family to lift the patient onto an ambulance instead.
Mr. Chea Huang said that after being taken to the hospital, his family was not allowed to come near him, and when he died, his relatives were not allowed to come near him.
Mr. Chea Huang said that Mr. Puch Raksmey's death was due to the delay of the medical team. He said that if the doctors take care and go to receive patients from the first illness is not affecting life like this.
He also stated that health services in the United States are not easy, when sick, it is not easy to call a doctor for treatment.
The United States is also a land with a large Cambodian population. But so far there are no reports or clear data on how many Cambodians are infected and how many are affected?
A brother who lives in the United States as a friend of Mr. Puch Raksmey added that Mr. Puch Raksmey's body was kept in the morgue for seven days before the family members were not allowed to report. Do not go near that. Doctors said that after seven days, doctors took the body to be cremated, requiring relatives to pay another $ 3,000 for the cremation.
The United States is struggling to fight Kovid 19 as the number of infections has risen, leading to a shortage of hospitals and medical staff. Medical use is also scarce.
According to Cambodians in the United States, 19 Kovid patients were not taken to hospital if they did not reach a critical level.
He added that according to doctors there, if anyone is diagnosed with COVID-19, they need to be treated at home because the hospital has no place to stay. Kandal Provincial Armed Forces Commander Announces Donation of 1 Million Riel Salary for 7 Months to National Commission for Combating Kovid 19
