The World Health Organization has called the Kovid 19 virus an "enemy of humanity" that requires the whole world to unite in the fight against the Kovid 19 virus.
For Cambodia, the Royal Government has put in place the necessary measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid, and the Cambodian people have been actively involved in implementing the measures in accordance with the guidelines of the health authorities. To date, there have been 19 cases of Kovid in the community, and most of them have been imported.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to increase agricultural cultivation, strengthen domestic production and establish a working group to control the prices of some commodities during the fight against Kovid 19.
At the same time, in order to protect the welfare of the Cambodian people and control the eventual outbreak of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has initiated a draft law on emergency management, which is expected to be approved by the legislature. Next week.
Although the current situation in Cambodia has not yet reached the state of emergency, as some countries have done to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that Cambodia must have this law in hand.
May this spirit of national unity remain forever in the soul of the Khmer nation and may the Khmer nation and the whole world overcome this cruel 19 Kovid virus and protect the lives of all mankind.
(Central): Mr. Tou Tres, a resident of Bahrain Krom, who was carrying 19 Kovit, was 100% cured by Cambodian doctors and was allowed to return home on April 5, 2020. Supported by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, accompanied by Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner and many other subordinates.
On this occasion, the provincial governor instructed Mr. Toutre to take good care of his health, exercise regularly, live clean, eat clean, drink clean, wash his hands often with soap or alcohol, and when you go home, please stay separate, do not be near them. Close to him for another 14 days to complete his work, because he has recovered, but must protect himself and his family again to prevent other problems.
The provincial governor also instructed Totre's family to keep a distance and protect themselves, and in particular provide him with enough vitamins and nutrients and provide him with protective equipment such as masks, alcohol, disinfectant or soap. To him so that he keeps his hygiene clean.
Mr. Tou Treh also called on all citizens not to discriminate, but instead to sympathize with each other as much as possible and to protect themselves from the spread of this disease so that it does not continue with the Royal Government of Cambodia. China vows not to restrict exports of medical equipment to other countries
