Legal Awareness: Roles and Jurisdiction of Investigating Judges
(Phnom Penh): In Cambodian courts, the criminal jurisdiction is a jurisdiction that selects a system of investigations to ensure the protection of the rights and interests of both victims and defendants in an equality before the law.
Therefore, the investigating judge stage is an important procedure in criminal proceedings because this stage is conducted with respect to the rights of the parties, whether the victim or the accused, that is, the investigating judge is the seeker. Gather evidence and exculpatory evidence to ensure equality between the parties and find out the facts before deciding whether or not to detain the accused.
Therefore, in order for the investigating judge to find out the truth, the Code of Criminal Procedure empowers as well as the important role of the investigating judge in the measures of the investigation in its investigative phase.
In order to better understand the legal awareness program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, please raise the topic "Role and Jurisdiction of the Investigating Judge" to explain and share to the people, students. All of the following:
1 * Role of the Investigating Judge:
The investigating judge also has the role of investigating the request of the prosecution, the accused, the civil party or the victim and the lawyer. In the event of a request to perform any duty, the non-binding investigating judge must investigate the request, as the investigating judge may reject the request by informing the applicant. If there is no notice of denial to the applicant, the applicant may appeal to the Parliament of Inquiry.
2 * Territorial jurisdiction of the investigating judge:
In the procedure of investigation, the investigating judge who has the territorial authority to fulfill his / her role is generally determined in the following way: * The authority of the investigating judge at the place of crime. The residence of the person suspected of committing the crime. * The authority of the investigating judge to arrest the person suspected of committing the crime.
In cases where there is a dispute between several investigating judges in different courts and all of them receive the same criminal case, the dispute is referred to the President of the Investigative Assembly for a decision. Many territorial disputes between the National Assembly are decided by the President of the Supreme Court, which closes the way for protests.
Overall, the 2007 Code of Criminal Procedure provides detailed provisions on the role and jurisdiction of investigating judges, as the investigating judge stage plays an important role in the criminal proceedings in investigating crimes. Accused by the prosecution against the accused through a subpoena that can determine whether the accused committed or did not commit the crime.
