1,000 liters of counterfeit alcohol cracked down by Chbar Ampov district authorities
(Phnom Penh): Chbar Ampov District Authority, in cooperation with officials of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud, with the approval of Mr. Sam Rithy Veasna, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, inspected and inspected a number of warehouses. In Ta Ngov village, Niroth commune, Chbar Ampov district, 1,000 liters of counterfeit alcohol were found.
The crackdown took place on the afternoon of April 4, 2020. According to the manager of the warehouse, Nguyen Van Dat, a Vietnamese national, confirmed to officials that 1,000 liters of counterfeit alcohol had been shipped through Chrey Thom checkpoint in Kandal province since April 1, 2020.
However, this unnumbered warehouse has been temporarily closed while all materials are stored in this warehouse pending further action.
Nguyen Van Dat, the Vietnamese manager of the warehouse, described that 34 cans of counterfeit alcohol, equivalent to 1,000 liters, had been imported since April 1, 2020, without seeing the owner until A joint team came down to search and test and found methanol. Mr. Kep Chuktema Visits and Educates People in Anlong Kong Thmey Community to Participate in Fighting Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Mr. KEP Chuktema, Member of Phnom Penh Constituency and Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) visited Dangkor District with the participation of Ms. Kim Nheb, Dangkor District Governor, Mr. Ch Kimsor, Deputy District Governor and local authorities. With people in Anlong Kong Thmey community in Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor.
Mr. Kep Chuktema instructed the people in this community to take care of their hygiene regularly and to avoid spending too much time washing their hands with soap. The problem is not serious, but the main problem is not going anywhere. If you have a fever, please inform the village authorities and go to the hospital immediately if you suspect that you are not comfortable, especially those from outside to report to the authorities.
He informed the people about the dangers of 19 communicable diseases that have now spread globally in almost every country in the world. In Cambodia, in particular, although the disease has not yet spread rapidly and some patients have recovered, there are no signs of remission.
Therefore, we must continue to actively participate in the fight against Kovid 19 under the guidance of the Royal Government and the medical guidelines of the Ministry of Health, such as: living a hygienic life, washing hands frequently, washing soap frequently in mutual relations must be maintained. Appropriate spacing and wearing a mask to protect the road, especially to avoid crowded gatherings, etc.
At the same time, we must unite to maintain a normal life, protect personal and family health, and protect public health in order to prevent the spread of the disease in the community, especially in the real situation of the labor movement, migrants from abroad and return. Return to his hometown village.
Mr. J Kimsor, Deputy Governor of Dangkor District and Permanent Deputy Chairman of Dangkor District Party, said that at this time, in order to participate in the hygiene and prevention of COVID-19 infection, Mr. Kep Chuktema donated scarves and rice to 120 party heads. And the budget of 70 party members. More than 16 kg of drugs and 2 suspects were cracked down by the police in Boeung Keng Kang and Toul Kork districts
(Phnom Penh): More than 16 kilograms of methamphetamine or ice and two suspects were cracked down on by the Anti-Drug Department, together with Boeung Keng Kang and Tuol Kork police. This was confirmed by a senior police officer of the Anti-Drug Department to Fresh News this morning, April 5, 2020.
The crackdown on large-scale drug cases took place under the direct leadership of General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, and Lt. Gen. Loek Vannak, Director of the Anti-Drug Department, following orders from the National Police General, Dr. Neth Savoeun .
Investigative activities leading to the crackdown on the above case were first held on April 2, 2020 at the point of Street 163, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang II, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, the specialized force of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes (A7) led by Deputy Director Soeung Nol, with the coordination of Mr. Soeun Moniroth, Deputy Prosecutor and Deputy Inspector of Tuol Kork District.
The first target arrested a suspect named Soeung Theava, 37 years old, confiscated gram powder, suspected methamphetamine (ICE) weighing about half a kilogram, and then proceeded to check the second target on April 3, 2020 at Room 33c, House 25z, Street 251, Village 16, Sangkat Boeung Salang, Khan Toul Kork, arrested another suspect, 37-year-old Oeung Dy Channa .
Police officials said that after testing and weighing, the drug methamphetamine (ICE) weighs a total of nearly 16.5 kilograms.
