(Pailin): On April 4, 2020, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by his leadership and working group, continued to visit and disseminate measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the back. Homes as well as food aid to 72 poor families in Otavao and Pailin communes, Pailin city, Pailin province, after they were affected by the Covid-19 outbreak.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, disseminated instructions to the people on hygiene to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health, such as: to wash their hands. Regularly with soap and water or use alcohol-based hand sanitizer, eat properly cooked food, reduce outings and gatherings if not necessary.
The governor said that if people go out, they should always wear a mask or a scarf and go to the doctor immediately if there are any suspicious symptoms such as fever, cough and difficulty breathing. In case of any citizens who have just returned from abroad, they must immediately report to the authorities for screening to prevent Kovid-19 infection in our community.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthulk also reminded the local authorities at all levels and the team of doctors to continue to promote education at the local level, especially in towns and public places to revive the measures. Prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly and First Vice President of the Standing Committee of the Central Working Group for Kandal Province and Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Central Working Group for Leuk Dek District on the 4th of this month. In April 2020, he met with front-line officials of the COVID 19 campaign in Leuk Dek district.
On this occasion, she instructed the front line officials of all local villages and communes in Leuk Dek to pay regular attention to integrate a clear understanding of how to protect themselves and prevent this deadly disease.
At the same time, she also stressed the need to control immigrants from abroad to monitor their health status closely, if in case of doubt, to provide information to the health department to intervene immediately. .
After further explaining the necessary measures as instructed by the Ministry of Health as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia, she also handed over materials including: 10,000 masks and 150 liters of disinfectant alcohol to be used in combat activities. Fight against the COVID-19 virus that is spreading and happening right now.
She also encouraged by donating 2 million Riels to the district team, each participant received 100,000 Riels and also donated 500,000 Riels to the troops.
It should be noted that at a time when the world as well as Cambodia is experiencing an epidemic of Kovid 19, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has called on the private sector to join the Royal Government together to fight the onslaught of this terrible disease. .
Mr. Steng Sokhom inspected and managed the fight against Kovid 19 in Kamchay Mear district
(Prey Veng): Mr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Working Group for Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, on April 4, 2020, inspected and organized the fight against 19 Kovid throughout Kamchay Mear District and Bring donations to Kamchay Mear District Administration, which is working to fight Kovid 19.
On that occasion, Mr. Steng Sokhom informed the national working group and the district administration about the situation of the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia and the important measures that the Royal Government has put in place to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. This. Mr. Steng Sokhom also expressed his appreciation to the district and commune leaders for their good work in fulfilling their duties to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
He also introduced and introduced a number of measures to prevent the spread of the disease by people from Thailand. Mr. Steung Sokhom instructed the working group to instruct the people from Thailand to stay away from their families for 14 days to avoid transmitting 19 smallpox to their families and villagers.
On the same day, Mr. Steung Sokhom and members of the working group and Kamchay Mear district leaders inspected the locations of 14 days of isolation of migrant workers in the eight communes of the district, most of which were located in Kamchay Mear district. Secondary. In each district, Mr. Steng Sokhom inspected the connection of water, electricity, accommodation, bathroom and cooking area, focusing on hygiene rules.
Mr. Steng Sokhom also requested the head of the national working group to visit all communes to provide mosquito nets, blankets, mats, pillows and food for the people who live in the center well.
