Maintaining a good situation, especially the prevention of this epidemic, is inseparable from the control and implementation of government measures.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Commander-in-Chief of the Battle of Kovid 19, has been seen to take control of the situation and set out a series of plans since Cambodia first discovered the disease in Sihanoukville. This past January.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia's Supreme Commander-in-Chief, has been hailed as one of the logistics generals who has always had an unwavering supply of military equipment, especially on the battlefield. In the battle with Kovid 19 since January, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also came out to monitor and put in place regular measures according to the disease situation.
It is remembered that the first step, when the disease did not spread, Samdech Techo Hun Sen came out to suppress the situation so that the people do not panic, only by recommending the implementation of sanitary measures. It was not until March, when the disease became more prevalent in the world and the number of cases in Cambodia increased, that Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to launch a plan to close flights with 19 Kovid countries and close borders with neighboring countries. Also side.
In addition, Samdech Techo also decided to close entertainment venues, gathering places and so on. Including programs with large crowds are also recommended to dissolve.
Not only the introduction of measures to prevent the spread of disease, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also introduced measures to maintain market price stability and food stability in Cambodia to block the export of rice and white rice to neighboring countries. Also.
Overall, through the monitoring and development of a permanent situation management plan by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, dubbed the "Strong Man of Cambodia", the crisis situation caused by Kovid 19 in Cambodia is not as bad as it used to be. Some countries in the world.
In an audio message sent to the leadership of the National Committee for Combating Diseases COVID-19 on April 4, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the order to increase the lives of doctors at the forefront At this time, seeing what all the doctors have been trying to do.
