(Pursat): The families of citizens who denounced the police force in the case of burning a car on social media yesterday came out to publicly apologize for their mistakes that caused confusion to the public.
The public apology for this mistake was made in front of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors at the Provincial Hall Forum.
Mr. Sim Chan and Ms. Vorn Phal, as well as their daughter Sem Sovann, who lives in Rovieng village, Samrong commune, Phnom Kravanh district, confirmed that the live video was due to incitement by his son-in-law and caused a moment of confusion. Forget to consider. In fact, his son-in-law, who was divorced from his daughter, cheated on him by plotting to notify the authorities and ask the media to come down for such a confusing interview.
Ms. Vorn Phal added that during the crackdown operation by the district military base on April 1, 2020, her son-in-law reported and asked a friend who was a journalist to interview her as the owner of the RV. That's why the video that was live yesterday, April 2, 2020, exploded and was shared by other media and posted, "I really feel sorry for him, why did he burn his car?" What good is a business if it simply "blends in" with everything else out there?
"I know I was wrong," Von Phal said. Because of my negligence for a while, because I did not check carefully after I found out so that there will be no more misunderstandings, so I publicly apologize to the police and hope not Hold on to me. ” Colonel Hor Chea announces donation of 810,000 Riels per month for 6 months to the National Commission for Combating Kovid 19
