Many Families in Lumhach Commune, Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province Complain to Keo Moniroth Company for Failing Documents
(Kandal): Many families in Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province, have filed a lawsuit against Keo Moniroth Company for forging documents and refusing to pay them land in Andong Teuk village, Lumhach commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
It should be noted that in the past, Mr. Keo Moniroth, the president of this company, was also arrested by the Kandal Provincial Armed Forces through a lawsuit filed by a lawyer named Jai Ho Ming because the president of this company swindled the sale of land worth more than 2 million dollars. To the lawyer in Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province.
Separately, people in Andong Teuk village, Lumhach commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province also protested because they sold the land to Mr. Keo Moniroth's company but did not receive the full amount and the company intends to pour the land. Another breach of contract. But now the company, represented by Mr. Leng Seng Rang, has come out to settle some of the installments, the rest are filing lawsuits to protest.
According to some documents obtained by Fresh News on April 4, 2020, it is clear that people who have not yet received payment from the company because the documents have to be used to pay taxes have been stolen. Or scratching, distorting, damaging in order to freeze the people's money, which is why the people can no longer decide to go to court to get their land back.
The remaining 7 families have not yet paid their installments for various reasons, some of which have expired sales contracts, their lands have been returned to them, and some of them have deliberately damaged documents by local officials or company representatives. Order from Mr. Keo Moniroth directly.
