Parents of private students request some discounts for online classes
(Phnom Penh): Some private schools, even if they only teach online, they still charge the full price, which makes some parents unhappy.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, has ordered schools across the country to suspend their studies until the situation of Kovid 19 changes again.
Even though schools are closed, many private schools continue to find ways to educate their students by teaching online or sharing lessons on social media.
Due to the incomplete provision of education and the perception that parents are all helping with the economic problems caused by Kovid 19, some private schools have decided to reduce tuition fees, but others have not.
She asked the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to facilitate the school to help reduce some tuition fees, because the provision of education is not as full as when going to school, and in the meantime, all Cambodian families have problems in life.
Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that in principle, the Ministry of Education does not have the right to order private schools regarding tuition fees. However, he encouraged the school and the parents to talk because during this time, both the school and the parents are in a difficult situation together.
