The birthday chosen during the entry into the jungle, the struggle to change from a civilian to a warrior, was also decided by Samdech Techo to this day.
This year marks the 50th anniversary of my use of April 4 as a birthday, an appropriate time for interpretation to address the questions of some who have always wondered why Hun Sen has two birthdays and which one is his real birthday. ?.
Fifty years ago, on April 4, 1970, I entered the Margi forest to fight against the call of King Norodom Sihanouk to fight against illegal coup d'etats and foreign aggression. Upon entering the camp in the deep forest, the leader asked about 300 of us to make a resume. I do not remember the date of birth, so I took April 4, the day I joined the struggle as a birthday, April 4, 1952.
I was appointed Minister of Foreign Affairs at the age of 27. The transition from 1952 to 1951 had two reasons: first, the typist had mistyped it and had already broadcast it on the radio. Secondly, I refuse to make any adjustments because I am too young to be over 26 years old compared to other ministers who are all over 40 or over 50 years old.
This is to clarify the history of April 4, which I keep today as an official birthday, because it is the day I decided to join the army at the call of the Father of the Nation, Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk.
