(Phnom Penh): On April 3, 2020, WB Finance, one of the largest deposit-taking microfinance institutions in Cambodia and a subsidiary of Uri Bank in South Korea, donated US $ 10,000. To the Ministry of Health of Cambodia to help fight and prevent the spread of COVID-19.
WB Finance also donated some other essential medical equipment to the Cambodian community in need, including: 1,250 bottles of hand wash gel, 390 liters of alcohol and 9,500 masks. This donation will be an important part of supporting and encouraging the team that is carrying out operations to fight this communicable disease, as well as providing assistance to communities in this difficult time.
In order to ensure the protection of its employees and customers from infectious diseases, COVID-19 WB Finance has been implementing various safety measures for all customers and staff, such as temperature monitoring before entering the building. Or the office, washing hands often with gel or alcohol, washing hands, wearing masks and keeping away from various interactions.
