Noodles bring sanitation materials and noodles to orphanages
(Phnom Penh): Mi Cheat distributed 120 cases of thermometers, alcohol, hand soap, mask and noodles to distribute to the Cambodian Social Welfare Organization, an orphanage and poor children in Phnom Penh on April 3, 2020.
In addition to bringing the above gifts, the Mey Cheat team also showed how to wear a mask and how to wash their hands properly to protect themselves from infections to the children's representatives in the organization.
Chun Heang Thav Sithy, Marketing Manager of Mey Cheat, said: “Mey Cheat brings these donations because Mey Cheat wants to contribute to help prevent the spread of 19 Kovid virus in Cambodia in this situation, especially children in the nursery. Orphans and poor children who are in need of these assistance. ”
Mr. Ny Sakal, Director General of the Social Welfare Organization, said, "Donations from the National Association at this time are what the organization needs and is already looking for donors, and this contribution really shows the goodwill of the National Association. To all the children who are staying in the organization. ”
Currently, a total of 58 children, including 25 girls and 33 boys, are living in the social welfare organization, receiving food, shelter, clothing and school supplies.
This is not the first time that Mi Cheat has participated in social activities. In the past, Mi Cheat has also donated to the poor people in Phnom Penh and in Koh Sotin district, donated to various charity programs Donate blood voluntarily as well.
