Khmer Breweries Donates Cambodian Pure Water and Fruit Juice to Prey Veng Provincial Hall for Kovid 19 Prevention Campaign
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries Company has donated 1,000 cases of Cambodian pure water and 200 cases of fruit juice to Prey Veng Provincial Hall for use in the campaign against 19 Kovid in this province.
The handing over ceremony of Cambodian pure water and fruit juice was held at Prey Veng Provincial Hall on the morning of April 3, 2020. Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province, handed over a letter of thanks to Khmer Breweries, which has always been actively involved in social and charitable activities in the past.
At the end of March, Khmer Breweries donated 3,000 cases of Cambodian pure water to the Ministry of Health for use in the campaign against Kovid 19. Chip Mong, the parent company of Khmer Breweries, donated $ 500,000 to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the same campaign.
For customers who always support and buy Cambodian pure water, it means that they have been significantly involved with Khmer Breweries in social activities and charitable activities as well.
