JICA Japan provides equipment and equipment for surveillance cameras to Cambodian customs
(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has provided equipment and camera systems for inspection of goods to the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia to contribute to the inspection of goods entering and leaving Cambodia.
It should be noted that the Customs Surveillance Camera System project is part of the Customs Reform and Modernization Program to strengthen the control of export-import control of goods and means of transportation in accordance with the Customs Law and related regulations in force. With the main function of sending images from some branches of the Office of Customs and Excise to the Central Center of the General Department of Customs and Excise.
On that occasion, Dr. Kun Nhim, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, also thanked JICA for always cooperating and supporting the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Sends a Letter of Thanks to Pann Serey Vuth and Long Sopha for Donating 1 Million Riels to the Royal Government for Fighting Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has sent a letter of thanks to Pastor Panh Serey Vuth and his disciple Long Sopha for donating 1 million Riels to the Royal Government of Cambodia for anti-epidemic activities. Kovid 19, which is endangering the health and lives of the Cambodian people. This is according to the letter of thanks received by Fresh News on the afternoon of April 3.
In his letter of thanks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "I would like to express my deep gratitude and sincere appreciation to the wedding teacher Panh Sereyvuth and his disciple Long Sopha for donating 1 million Riels to join the Royal Family." The government is fighting the epidemic Kovid-19 (COVID-19), which is threatening the health of our Cambodian people. ”
