In fact, on April 2, 2020, the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled received a charitable donation of food and 7 million Riels from a philanthropist named Seav Mey. Ms. Sieu Mey also donated 2 tons of Angkor food, 5 kg of dried fish, 5 kg of sausage, 60 boxes of noodles, 100 bottles of hand washing alcohol.
Ms. Nhem Morakot, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Women's Affairs, thanked the benefactors for sharing what they have and giving to people with disabilities in the circumstances that Cambodia is infected with COVID-19. She said that in the meantime, no one is afraid to leave their homes to protect themselves, instead philanthropists have spent time and resources as well as food to share with people with disabilities, which is a respectable activity.
Ms. Nhem Morakot, Member of the Disability Action Council and Honorary President of the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled, continued, Samneang Music Association for the Disabled directly. We welcome philanthropists, how can we help each other in this difficult situation, because we say we are physically fit and still difficult, how difficult is it for each other? ”
For her part, Sia Mey said that the reason she contributed was because she saw the plight of people with disabilities in the circumstances that COVID-19 virus was spreading, which made them unemployed and affect their livelihoods. Speaking at the beginning, Xiaomei also appealed that in the difficult circumstances of people with disabilities, now only the help of philanthropists, so please all philanthropists to help people with disabilities as much as possible.
The Samneang Music Association for the Disabled was founded in 2013 by Mr. Chap To, a blind man. The association is located in Chumral village, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, and is also recognized by the Ministry of Interior. Fighting Kovid 19
