(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on April 3, 2020 issued guidelines on measures to promote agricultural production in the rainy season of 2020, which will come soon.
B: General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production:
C: Fisheries Administration:
D: Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Capital-Province: 1: To advise farmers and all stakeholders in the agricultural production chain to be ready to grow crops in the coming rainy season to increase food production of all kinds. Quality and safety.
2. To coordinate with the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology and local authorities to inspect and identify areas with water sources or areas with favorable conditions in their localities, especially to coordinate the search for water supply to promote crop production at the beginning of the rainy season. As fast as possible.
3. To be an active and effective intermediary in liaising between producers and collectors through contract agricultural production mechanisms to ensure the supply and fair prices of agricultural products.
E: Agricultural Development Project Implementation Unit and related specialized units under the Ministry: 1: To promote the implementation of the approved action plan to increase food production (vegetables, fruits, fish, meat) to supply the country's food needs adequately in the disease environment. This Kovid-19.2: Must regularly report to the Ministry on the results achieved so that the Ministry has appropriate measures to continue.
The Ministry of Agriculture emphasizes that the relevant units under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Capital, Provincial Departments of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries must cooperate well with sub-national administrations, the private sector and development partners to implement this guideline effectively. And succeed. Mr. Luy David announced to donate 1 million Riel for 6 months to the National Commission for Combating Kovid 19
