(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia in the war to fight against Kovid 19, Metfone has established a charity fund called "Metfone Kovid 19 Foundation".
This program is free of charge and everyone can easily donate to join us in this difficult situation as well. The fund is expected to reach millions of people and hundreds of thousands of dollars will be handed over to the authorities at the end of the program.
All registered and activated accounts will be automatically donated 1,000 Riels to Metfone Coverage 19 Foundation and the program starts from today until the end of May.
Funds raised from all funds will be donated to the authorities to accommodate 19 Kovid patients, front-line doctors and the needs of the population. There is no charge during the implementation of this program.
This action underscores that Metfone has always adhered to its "Highly Careful and Innovative" vision with the aim of contributing to the fight against this deadly disease with high efficiency.
Nhong Dinthon, Deputy General Manager of Metfone, said: “The reason for choosing Mocha and eMoney to raise funds is because Metfone complies with government guidelines in response to the Kovid 19 outbreak and encourages All customers stay at home, keep away from society, but still be able to enjoy various online entertainment, shopping and some essentials.
Mocha is a world-class online entertainment program that provides up-to-date information, watch copyrighted movies and blogs without annoying ads, and all customers can listen to music and chat together for free. . EMoney is a digital wallet app that allows you to top up your mobile phone, pay bills and transfer money at home for free.
He added: "In addition to this program, Metfone has updated the latest information on Kovid 19, including instructions from the Ministry of Health and relevant authorities. All customers can follow the latest information on the status of the epidemic. "Find videos to protect yourself and the latest information from the authorities."
Since the outbreak of Kovid 19, Metfone has been actively involved with the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, especially in the field of education and the implementation of a number of strategies, including sponsoring online education, video conferencing solutions, and providing free telecommunications infrastructure. And provide many other services as well.
