Russey Keo District Governor Continues to Receive Disinfectant Equipment, Massage and Hand Wash from Two Companies to Prevent Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Pisey, Governor of Russey Keo District and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continues to receive equipment such as antiseptic mask and hand sanitizer from two companies, Ganzberg Beer Company and DF Company. I Lucky to join the Royal Government of Cambodia to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
The handover ceremony of antiseptic equipment, mask and hand wash from these two companies with the participation of Mr. Deputy Governor, Khan Administration Director and other relevant government officials at Russey Keo District Hall on April 2. 2020.
In addition, the Governor of Russey Keo District is committed and strives to pay attention to the whole body, mind and body in inspiring to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 disease all over the world according to the instructions of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Director Minister and Minister of Interior and in accordance with the spirit of the High Directive of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be informed that for Ganzberg Beer Company, which has sponsored Russey Keo District Hall now, it includes: 10 equipment for spraying disinfectants and 2 cans of disinfectant. Separately for DFI Lucky, which has donated to Russey Keo district now, including: 2,500 masks and 50 bottles of antiseptic hand wash.
