BEIJING (Reuters) - China will hold a nationwide mourning ceremony this Saturday for doctors, police and civil servants at all levels who have sacrificed their lives in the fight against COVID-19. Thousands of other Chinese died of the disease. This was quoted from the Xinhua news agency on Friday afternoon, April 3, 2020.
According to a statement from the Chinese government during the mourning tomorrow, all flags across China will be flown at half-mast, and all Chinese embassies and consulates abroad will do the same. .
Fun activities in the country will be suspended. At 10:00 a.m. Saturday, Chinese people across the country will hold a three-minute mourning ceremony to mourn those who lost their lives, as sirens will be heard in mourning.
