(Phnom Penh): Since the outbreak of the Covid-19 virus, Metfone has been working hard to support the government and the people, especially in the field of education through various practical means, including support for online learning, solutions through video conferencing. Provides free telecommunications infrastructure and much more.
Since the Covid-19 pandemic has affected many countries in the world, including Cambodia, keeping away from society has been encouraged as a precaution against the virus.
Since the end of March, all schools across the country have been closed to prevent the spread of the virus to all future students of the nation.
Seeing these situations, Metfone immediately contributed with all the resources it has, implementing and providing solutions to the government and the people to overcome this situation in order to maintain effective education. Online study period.
Metfone is also offering a 50% discount until the end of April 2020 for the first internet connection to all parents after schools across the country closed during the Covid-19 virus outbreak.
At the same time, the Ministry also achieves real work efficiency and high quality in communicating with subordinates more easily than ever before. All this took place during the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between Metfone and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to improve telecommunications and ICT programs for all ministries and schools across the country on March 25. 2020.
