(Phnom Penh-Kandal): Two methanol storage sites for alcohol production were searched by a joint police force and raided at 4:30 pm on April 2, 2020.
Tens of thousands of liters of methanol were confiscated and it was learned that the illegal importers were Chinese and escaped before the coalition forces arrived.
According to sources from the police, at the first location in Phnom Penh, led by Mr. Seng Heang, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, with the participation of Mr. Khim Sun Soda, Governor of Kampol District, Mr. Phan Liva, Clerk, Mr. Nget Banana, General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (Camcontrol) of the Ministry of Commerce.
At the same time, the force confiscated 102 barrels of unused methanol and 81 barrels of used methanol, each with a capacity of 200 liters and about 100 gallons of alcohol per gallon of 60 liters.
The authorities further confirmed that the experts immediately conducted an experiment and found that the methanol and alcohol produced can cause serious harm to the health of consumers.
