JICA Signs $ 50 Million Loan Agreement with Hattha Kaksekar Microfinance Limited
(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) has signed a $ 50 million loan agreement with Hattha Kaksekar Limited, one of Cambodia's leading deposit-taking microfinance institutions, to provide funding. To micro, small and medium enterprises in various regions of the country.
This lending agreement demonstrates the high level of confidence and trustworthiness of HKL in making a significant contribution to the broader lending of micro, small and medium enterprises in rural areas. Than before.
According to JICA, the loan is designed to support the growth of micro, small and medium enterprises, create job opportunities and improve the financial environment for small and medium enterprises. Rural areas, as well as reducing poverty and differences in living standards in different parts of Cambodia.
Most importantly, the growth of micro, small and medium enterprises is an important part of promoting women. Therefore, this loan not only contributes to sustainable economic growth, but also supports the Sustainable Development Goals 8, 9 and 17.
