(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on April 2, 2020, emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia considers the development of the digital economy as an important priority area to promote the country's development.
This emphasis was made on the occasion of the official inauguration of the new Minister of Posts and Telecommunications by Mr. Chea Vandeth, replacing Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, Mr. Techo Hun Sen.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, has considered the development of the digital economy as one of the most important priority areas for promoting the country's development, as defined in the Rectangular Strategy - Phase IV.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also highlighted some important priorities for the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications to focus on in the medium and long term as follows:
3. Continuing to reform, enhance institutional capacity and strengthen work efficiency. Promote the preparation of legal documents set out in the Ministry's work program. Examine, amend or amend as appropriate some laws, documents, regulations in force to be in line with the development of ICT.
4: For the postal sector, continue to pay attention to improve the study of investment in equipping new technologies and promote the introduction of technology and information (E-Commerce). Increasing the volume of domestic delivery and promoting the operation of the international postal network.
5. In the field of telecommunications and ICT, continuing to strengthen and expand the telecommunication infrastructure with modern quality and providing nationwide coverage in the era of digitalization is having a positive impact on all major sectors of the national economy.
