(Phnom Penh): After the reshuffle of the new cabinet in the middle of this term, there are two of the four new ministers who are most interested, Mr. Chea Vandeth and Mr. Keut Rith, a new blood, an old intellectual who came out. From scholarship students to study abroad.
Chea Vandeth received a scholarship to study in Russia in 1990. He received a Master's degree in Economics in 1994 and a PhD in Economics in 1997. After returning to the country, he worked as a part-time professor of economics at several universities in Phnom Penh at the same time as the government under the leadership of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An as the Chief of Staff at the Council of Ministers.
Believing in his ability, Mr. Chea Van Det was appointed as the Head of the Economic Office of the Department of International Relations at the Office of the Council of Ministers, then as the Deputy Director of the Department and as the Director of the Cabinet, HE Sok An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
In terms of state affairs, he led the Royal Government's White Paper compilation team and was the personal secretary of the Preah Vihear Temple Working Group in the country when Deputy Prime Minister Sok An went on a mission to find a solution. Abroad.
Until 2018, after being appointed as the Chairman of the Third Committee of the National Assembly and as a member of the Standing Committee of the National Assembly, he has done a lot of outstanding work. These actions may be an additional factor that led to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision to appoint him Minister of Posts and Telecommunications by saying that he needed a wise, active and agile in his deep reform work.
Regarding his role in the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, Dr. Chea Vandeth has previously worked for Telecom Cambodia and Cambodia Reinsurance Company as a board member.
Speaking at the inauguration of the new Minister on Thursday morning, Mr. Chea Vandeth outlined nine priority tasks, especially the strengthening of human resources of civil servants in the Ministry of Labor Efficiency and Modernization and the speedy completion of government policies. Digital.
Along with those priorities, Mr. Chea Vandeth also asked for understanding from the leadership and civil servants in the Ministry of the reform plan, which may have some conflict, but must be done to ensure efficiency and success, especially for the Royal Government. By Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
However, the public will be waiting to see if Chea Vandeth can carry out in-depth reforms in the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
