(Phnom Penh): The new Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, Mr. Chea Vandeth, who was officially inaugurated this morning, April 2, 2020, is determined to make the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications one of the model ministries. More of the Royal Government.
Such a commitment was made on the occasion of Mr. Chea Van Det's participation in the inauguration ceremony of the Minister of Posts and Telecommunications this morning, April 2, 2020.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and was represented by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
At the inauguration ceremony, Mr. Chea Van Det committed to strengthen the administration of the Ministry to effectively perform its functions and save the state budget to the maximum.
In response to the trust of the Head of the Royal Government as well as the National Assembly of Cambodia and to testify in this significant event, Mr. Chea Vandeth made further commitments to the whole ceremony as follows:
* First: Commitment to respect the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia
* Second: Respect and loyal commitment to the nation, religion, the King
* Third, strive to implement the Rectangular Policy and Strategy Program, Phase 4 of the Royal Government, the 6th Legislature of the National Assembly, on the program of in-depth reform and development of the post, telecommunications, information and communication technology sector, to be able to expand the scope of telecommunication infrastructure to cover rural areas. Lack of services or insufficient telecommunications services and rural areas with economic and tourism potential.
* Fourth: Continue to promote and provide public services related to the postal, telecommunication, communication and information technology so that civil servants and people at all localities continue to support the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister for the sixth term. Subsequent pity.
* Fifth: Strengthen the internal unity and solidarity of the leaders at all levels at all levels of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
It should be noted that Mr. Chea Vandeth was appointed by the King in a Royal Decree to be the Minister of Posts and Telecommunications on March 30, 2020, after the National Assembly voted to approve the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Van Det was born in 1971. In 2017, he was the MP for Takeo constituency, replacing Sok An. He is also the Chairman of the Committee on Investment Planning, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources (Third Committee) of the National Assembly and the founder of the American University of Phnom Penh (AUPP).
On his first day as the new Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, Chea Vandeth also announced his six-month salary contribution to the National Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19.
