This draft law was unanimously approved by the Senate by a vote of 49 to 49 in the Extraordinary Session of the 4th Senate this morning, April 2, after being fully approved by the National Assembly in the morning of the 26th morning. March 2020 with 109 votes in favor.
Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of Cambodia to the Royal Group Investment Co., Ltd. for the Investment Project for the Construction of a 700 MW Coal-Fired Power Plant in Koh Kong Province is the First Agenda Approved The last one.
Royal Group Investment Group Co., Ltd. has received a concession to implement a project to build a 700-megawatt imported coal-fired power plant in Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province, with the following key conditions:
The plant has an installed capacity of 700 megawatts and a net power of 680 megawatts. Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) guarantees to buy energy from the project 80% per year. Total investment is 1,344.20 million US dollars, of which 30% is direct capital and 70% is bank loan.
The commissioning of the power plant is in line with the master plan for the development of the electricity sector, with the first 350-megawatt engine to be commissioned in 2023 and the second 350-megawatt generator to be commissioned in 2024. The concession period is 38 years, including the construction period of 3 years and the operation period of 35 years, while the selling price of electricity is 0.07292 US dollars per kilowatt hour.
For this power plant project, the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided some incentives such as:
* Exemption from import tax on machinery, machinery, equipment and materials of the project during construction * Value Added Tax (VAT) and special tax owed by the state * Exemption from income tax for 9 years from the date of operation First business * Exemption of royalties and other financial obligations on the use of water and construction resources (gravel, sand, soil) for project construction.
However, the company has to clear mines and unexploded ordnance at the necessary locations. The company must strictly and effectively implement measures to prevent and reduce environmental impact. The company must also provide funding to support and reduce environmental impacts, and the company must support EDC for human resource training programs and capacity building in the Cambodian energy sector.
