New Minister of Justice Keut Rith bursts into tears while commemorating the virtues and merits of the former Minister of Justice (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The new Minister of Justice, Keut Rith, burst into tears unknowingly In commemoration of the virtues and merits of the training, as well as the memories of working under the guidance of Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, former Minister of Justice for 13 years.
During his inauguration ceremony on the afternoon of April 1, 2020, Mr. Keut Rith reminded that while he was the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice under the supervision of Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, he received education, training and Lots of work experience from Mr. Ang Vong Vathana.
Reminiscing about the memories and merits of his former boss, Mr. Keut Rith was emotional and pushed the tears out until he no longer wanted to leave.
Through tears led to the evaluation and conclusion of the deep feelings between Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, the former Minister and Mr. Keut Rith, the Minister. From what has emerged, there is also an assessment of Keut Rith's personality and qualities as a person who values virtue.
It should be noted that Mr. Keut Rith, 41 years old, was elected by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Minister of Justice to replace Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, who held this ministry for 16 years. Mr. Keut Rith was entrusted by the National Assembly on March 30, 2020.
Mr. Keut Rith, 41 years old, was born on January 2, 1979 and was born in Prey Toteung Village, Prey Chhor District, Kampong Cham Province. He was a hard-working student, although his family life was not very good, but he still worked hard to support his family and study hard until he received a scholarship to study law in France in 1999.
Seeing his work and efforts, especially his extensive legal knowledge, on September 27, 2007, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni issued a Royal Decree appointing Keut Rith as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Justice. Request from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. On September 24, 2013, as Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice, until March 30, 2020, Samdech Techo decided to be appointed Minister of Justice.
