Nearly 300 Chinese troops return home after Golden Dragon exercise with Cambodian troops
(Phnom Penh): 265 Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) returned to their home country this morning, March 30, 2020, after successfully completing the 2020 Golden Dragon exercise with the Cambodian army.
The Chinese Army Retirement took place at Phnom Penh International Airport, accompanied by Cambodian troops.
It should be noted that the 4th Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army took place for 15 days from March 15 to 30 at the 70th Infantry Regiment Techo Sen Chum Kiri Real Shooting Range. In O village, Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province.
The fourth Golden Dragon exercise was held under the theme "Together against terrorism and humanitarian work" and also took shape over the years.
For the 2020 Golden Dragon Exercise, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has sent 2,746 participants, including 27 general managers, 463 training troops, and the rest for the opening and closing ceremonies.
The 2020 Golden Dragon Exercise involves more than 3,000 Cambodian-Chinese troops, accompanied by heavy weapons, tanks, armored vehicles, helicopters, along with automatic rifles, reconnaissance equipment, demining equipment, and chemical decontamination equipment. . It is noteworthy that the Cambodia-China 2020 exercise was held on a larger scale than in previous years under the theme "Together against terrorism and humanitarian work."
General Ith Sarath, Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, said that the 2020 Golden Dragon Exercise is to measure the quality of the Cambodian and Chinese armies in a sense to increase the quality capacity of the Cambodian Armed Forces. Make the Cambodian army more profitable by gaining a lot of experience from the Chinese People's Liberation Army on counter-terrorism, disaster relief and more.
For the 2020 Golden Dragon exercise, the Chinese military has sent five helicopters, 122 mm artillery, three mobile D-30s, nine armored vehicles, along with 28 other vehicles for the 2020 Golden Dragon exercise, as well as weapons and equipment. More tools to shoot together in 15 days.
The fourth Golden Dragon exercise was considered a great success and also contributed to strengthening military ties and cooperation between the two countries.
Wang Wintian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, described the 2020 Golden Dragon Exercise as a practical strategy to implement the two countries 'military leaders' agreement to further deepen military cooperation and participation. Promote the capacity of the two countries to move forward further.
