Ministry of Public Works Issues on Guidelines for Prevention and Control of 19 Kovid Diseases at Vehicle Technical Inspection Centers
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has issued guidelines on the implementation of measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in all vehicle technical inspection centers and passenger transport companies in the Kingdom of Cambodia for the purpose of implementation. Measures to prevent and control the risk of the spread of Kovid 19.
In the instruction of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which was received by Fresh News this morning, April 1, 2020, stated that in order to implement measures to prevent and prevent the risk of the spread of Kovid 19, the General Department of Transport Road Transport would like to introduce the following to the Director of Kbodime Motor VHickel Investment Company and the Director of HK Car Investment Co., Ltd. to implement the following measures:
* First, arrange hand soap or alcohol at the entrance of the vehicle technical inspection center for staff or customers to wash their hands before entering the vehicle technical inspection center.
* Second: Provide sufficient masks and protective gloves for the company staff in the vehicle technical inspection center.
* Third: Arrange for temperature measurement for all staff before entering the vehicle technical inspection center twice a day, once in the morning and once in the afternoon. Employees with a temperature above 37.2 degrees are allowed to take time off from work and are required to go for personal check-ups with high responsibility.
Fourth, instruct all employees to maintain hygiene and increase vigilance at all times with a safety distance of at least 1.5 meters apart when working with clients or colleagues.
* 5: Remind staff when coughing, sneeze, cover mouth, nose with toilet paper and throw in the trash properly, then wash hands with soap or alcohol.
* Sixth: Employees should be instructed to practice greeting each other by saluting in the traditional way to avoid shaking hands.
* 7th: Instruct the administrative staff to receive documents, to wear masks and protective gloves when touching documents, and to wash hands with soap or alcohol before and after receiving documents.
* Eighth: Instruct the staff to ask all vehicle owners to measure the temperature and not to sit inside the vehicle with the inspection staff during the inspection of vehicle specifications, by having the vehicle owners to the waiting area and take Carry valuables stored in the vehicle, such as jewelry, bags, phones, etc.
9th: Instruct the inspection staff to wear masks and protective gloves while driving and wash their hands with soap or alcohol before and after the technical inspection of the vehicle.
10th: Sanitary measures to disinfect using soap or alcohol must be carried out thoroughly and regularly by cleaning all equipment and equipment used in the vehicle technical inspection center.
