Health message from the Ministry of Health: Stop the spread of Kovid 19 and live far away (social gap) to keep yourself and your family safe
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on March 31, 2020 released a new educational message urging people to protect themselves and practice living apart (social gap) for themselves and their families to stop safely Outbreaks of Kovid 19.
The education message of the Ministry of Health provides the following 6 points of advice:
1: Avoid close contact with people with respiratory diseases such as fever, cough, sneeze or cold.
2: Avoid using unnecessary public transportation. Change travel times to avoid rush hour.
4: Avoid social gatherings and gatherings such as pubs, cinemas, restaurants, cafes, bars, clubs.
5: Avoid meeting friends and family. Keep in touch using mobile phones, internet and social media.
6: Greetings instead of handshakes and hugs. Keep a distance of at least 1.5 meters from each other.
