(Phnom Penh): The report of the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, stated that in the first three months of 2020, Cambodia exported nearly 3 million tons of agricultural products to international markets, both formal and informal.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, the official export figures for the first three months were 1,638,338 tonnes by the General Department of Agriculture and 1,298,654 tonnes by the Ministry of Agriculture.
Unofficial exports of cassava and rice to Vietnam amounted to 1,298,654 tons.
The markets for Cambodia's agricultural products are China, Europe, the United States, Vietnam, Thailand, Japan, Russia, India, ASEAN member countries and others.
