(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, March 31, 2020, chaired a meeting of the Standing Committee of the Council of Ministers to review the draft law on emergency management.
The statement added that the draft law would provide a legal basis to ensure the implementation of the new Article 22 of the Constitution and a legal basis for the Royal Government's authority to take the necessary measures to respond. The country's state of emergency aims to protect security, public order, protect the lives and health of the people, as well as protect property and the environment.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced at a press conference on March 30 yesterday that the decision to draft a law on governing the country is a state of emergency. Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that Cambodia does not yet have the law to govern the country in times of emergency. Therefore, the creation of this law to be a legal tool to manage the country in an emergency.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on the people and civil society organizations not to worry about this law because it is not designed to restrict the freedom of the people and freedom of expression.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed the expectation that the National Assembly will expedite the review and approval of this draft law.
