(Phnom Penh): Colonel Thi Visal, Deputy Director of the Traffic Police Department, stated that the new Sub-Decree No. 39 on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Road Traffic Law will contribute significantly to the prevention of traffic accidents while the new sub-decree Used by other countries in the world to reduce traffic accidents.
He said that the new sub-decree No. 39 on the penalty for violations of the law on road traffic, in general, all the crimes that occur by drivers in all sub-decrees.
He added that this sub-decree was amended from the old sub-decree that was implemented last year and has five main points that are different from the old sub-decree, including:
1: The amount of the fine to be fined in this sub-decree is increased between 3-5 times.
2. In this sub-decree, there is a distinction between offenses committed by motorcyclists and offenses committed by motorists.
3. Owners of all types of vehicles shall also be penalized for failing to complete the vehicle registration (license plate) registration form before handing it over to the buyer, which was not stated in the previous sub-decree.
4: In relation to crimes committed by a minor under the age of 15, it is not punishable by just educating, but if the minor is between the ages of 15 and 18, the parent or guardian is responsible and pays. Replacement penalty.
5. In case of non-payment of the 15-day interim fine, the amount shall be increased twice, but if it exceeds 30 days, it shall be increased 3 times and beyond 60 days, the case shall be sent to court for trial according to the law. According to the old law, it is left for 30-90 days.
Lt. Col. Thi Visal stated that the number of drivers who do not wear a helmet has been increased four times. Drivers must wear helmets when riding a motorcycle to protect their own safety.
"According to the study experience in ASEAN countries and neighboring countries as well as European countries, the implementation of this new sub-decree is effective and successful, making people have a negative attitude to positive," he said. "Back."
He said the purpose of the new sub-decree was to protect the lives of road users, so if people obeyed all traffic laws, they would not have to spend money on fines and protect their lives. Kampong Speu Provincial Governor Tells Pharmacy Owners, Vendors and Citizens Not to Buy and Sell COVID-19 Test Equipment
