(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has called on the Rice Federation, millers and traders to work with the Ministry of Commerce's Green Trade Company and the Rural Development Bank to obtain information on credit and food security in Cambodia while Cambodia is Risk of the spread of Kovid 19 infection.
In a statement issued on March 30, 2020, the Ministry claimed that this was done to ensure the normalization of the rice trade in Cambodia.
The call for the Rice Federation, millers and traders to work with the Ministry of Commerce's Green Trade and the Rural Development Bank came after the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued an order banning the sale of white rice and paddy. To neighboring countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during a press conference at the National Assembly building this morning, March 30, 2020, announced the suspension of rice and paddy exports from April 5, 2020 until further notice. Again to save local supply.
Samdech Techo stated that most of Cambodia's white rice and paddy is exported to neighboring countries such as Vietnam and Thailand. However, in order to ensure domestic supply, Cambodia needs to store rice and white rice, which are in high demand locally, and for fragrant rice, which is small in quantity and low in domestic demand, is still allowed to be exported as usual.
