Thirteen people arrested in connection with the production and sale of counterfeit Kovid 19 virus testing and protection equipment
(Phnom Penh): At least 13 people, including five foreigners and eight Cambodians, were arrested in connection with the production and sale of counterfeit devices for testing and preventing 19 Kovid virus in two days. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News on the night of March 30, 2020.
The general confirmed that the nine people were arrested during the police operation in 12 cases across the country, including 9 cases in Phnom Penh, 2 cases in Sihanoukville and 1 case in Siem Reap, however. Of the 13 people arrested, four were educated and allowed to go home and nine are in the process of being investigated.
"Those who are educated and allowed to go home are online sellers who do not have products," the spokesman said. According to Mr. Chhay Kim Khoeun, today, the police confiscated some fake equipment, including 21 blood test needles, 13 emergency test kits (in Phnom Penh) and 48 packages (in Sihanoukville), 400 fake clothes and 191,500 fake masks.
(Kampot): Joint military exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army, entitled "Golden Dragon Exercise 2020" on the theme of joint anti-terrorism and humanitarian work, which began on March 15 at the shooting range In fact, Techo Sen Chum Kiri of the 70th Infantry Brigade in O village, Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province, closed on March 30, 2020.
The closing ceremony was presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, and Mr. Wang Vinthean, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia.
At the same time, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Wintian considered the 2020 Golden Dragon Exercise as a practical strategy to implement the agreement reached by the two countries' military leaders to further deepen cooperation in the field. The military will participate in promoting the capabilities of both countries to move forward further.
It should be noted that this year is the fourth time that the Cambodian and Chinese armies have held joint exercises in Cambodia, with the first in 2016, the second in 2018, and the third in 2019. .
