Six Families from Samaki Meanchey District Come to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court to Request to Return 3 Bulldozers for Livelihood
(Kampong Chhnang): On the afternoon of March 30, 2020, six families in Samaki Meanchey district came to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court to request for their three bulldozers to be seized by the Provincial Gendarmerie. Kampong Chhnang was arrested and kept at the district inspectorate in the past in a land dispute.
Mr. Ek Mony, representing the above 6 families, said that today they came to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court to ask for information related to the problems of their three bulldozers. Prosecutors ordered the arrest on March 6, 2020.
After arranging for the release of the four of them to return home, the three bulldozers were required by the King to obtain proper documents from the village and commune authorities before they were allowed to take the bulldozers. Those and materials are reusable.
He added that the relevant documents and bulldozers and equipment seized by him were prepared by the local authority in accordance with the law, with the recognition of the village and commune authorities, and also submitted to the institution. The court has been working since March 16, 2020, and it has been half a month since today, but there has been no response from the court so that they can take the materials back to business.
After missing for several days, today they came to the court to ask for information. He asked the clerk, who accepted the documents from them, but the clerk told him that the documents had been handed over to him. The administration has already done so, but the administration has replied that he has not yet seen the document in their hands, however, the administration will help expedite this work for them as well.
They also asked the court to expedite the settlement for them as soon as possible so that they can use the bulldozers and equipment to make a living as the farming season is approaching.
