Ministry of Commerce announces legal action against those who continue to increase the price of Kovid 19 mask and protective equipment
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has announced that it will take legal action against vendors who continue to increase the price of masks and protective equipment for Kovid 19.
The Ministry of Commerce has appealed to all traders, companies, enterprises and individuals who do business and provide e-commerce services to sell products and equipment to prevent and prevent the spread of diseases such as masks, soaps, hand sanitizers and alcohol. And thermometers, etc., at an acceptable price, and strictly prohibiting unfortunate advertising to raise product prices.
The Ministry warns that in the event that the Ministry still sees that traders, companies, enterprises and individuals doing business and providing e-commerce services are still taking the opportunity to raise prices while Cambodia is experiencing a global pandemic (Kovid) 19) The Ministry of Commerce will take legal action. APSARA Authority is preparing to irrigate the grass in Angkor Wat
(Siem Reap): A team from the Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority is busy installing pipes to prepare a water system for irrigating grass in the Angkor Wat temple area of nearly 12 hectares.
Phoeun Sokhim, Deputy Director of the Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority, said that the process of preparing the irrigation system in the Angkor Wat temple area took two months to complete. The installation of pipes from one row to another is 20 meters apart.
The source of water for watering the grass is from the water well that surrounds the temple and watered in the evening to save water and not disturb tourists.
After finishing his work, he believes that the grass in the Angkor Wat temple complex will be green in both the dry season and the rainy season, especially to attract more tourists to visit this sacred monument.
In addition to weeding, the team will also prepare walkways in the Angkor Wat temple area as planned, and the arrangement of this weed irrigation system will also ensure the filling of water in the northern and southern ponds to have enough water in all seasons. The Governor of Kampong Thom Province continues to distribute donations and educate citizens to understand the COVID-19 virus measures.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, visited Srayov Sangkat, Stung Sen City to distribute gifts to the people and educate them to understand the COVID-19 virus measures and tell them not to believe the false information that makes Confused and urged local authorities to increase awareness to all citizens, especially to advise people who have just come from Thailand and other countries to stay separately for 14 days.
Speaking to Fresh News Agency in Kampong Thom province on March 30, 2020, Mr. Sok Loo urged the nine municipal authorities to continue to disseminate and deepen awareness to all citizens, especially to introduce newcomers from Thailand and other countries. Please stay separate for 14 days, especially if you have good hygiene by wearing a mask, use alcohol, wash your hands when handling objects.
The governor also advised the people not to believe the voicemail on Chat, do not believe false news, polluting information, inciting unrest, especially do not believe word of mouth, because all of them have no basis to believe. But please believe only in the Ministry of Health, because they provide real information, specific information and the most accurate information.
Police find more than 20 kilograms of drugs floating in the sea in Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): On March 30, 2020, the Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner held a press conference to show the drugs found by the authorities floating at Koh Kong point outside the 5th coconut plantation, Alatan village, Chroy Pros commune, Koh Kong district, Koh Kong province.
The press conference was held in the presence of Ms. Mithona Phu Thong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, Mr. Ros Saram, Prosecutor of Koh Kong Provincial Court, Major General Sam Khit Vien, Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner and General Min Raksmey, Deputy Commissioner. Anti-drug crime plan includes many experts.
Major General Samkhit Vien said that the fishermen provided information to the authorities to implement and search for the target on March 28, 2020, when they found a strange object on the beach.
Major General Samkhit Vien continued that with the order from the provincial governor, he ordered General Min Raksmey to lead professional officers to inspect the sea in the middle of the night. After inspecting for drugs, the police kept it at the provincial police commissioner for a thorough inspection.
He added that after checking and found that the drug is a type of ice, there are 20 large packages, each package weighs 1,020 grams. After inspecting all these drugs, the authorities will send them to the provincial court for further action in accordance with the law.
On this occasion, Ms. Mithona Phu Thong thanked the authorities at all levels for keeping the people safe, no matter what the circumstances, and always striving to fulfill their duties regardless of fatigue and Moral framework as a authority to serve the people and the nation.
