The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) recently issued a new directive to banking and financial institutions to restructure their loans to ease the burden on borrowers facing declining revenues. Mainly and difficult to compensate for due to the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
Through the Circular on "Credit Restructuring During the Impact of Kovid 19 Outbreak" signed by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia on March 27, 2020, introduced to the Banking and Financial Institutions Pay attention to the actual affected customers from four sectors, including:
The circular also recommends that the reorganization of loans be to ensure that the client is experiencing financial difficulties before granting a concession.
The circular recommends that this loan restructuring be provided to customers whose interest and / or principal payments are not overdue for more than 30 days (type of loan is processed) and that the client is expected to experience financial difficulties. And payments are only temporary and valid until December 31, 2020.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth tells the General Department of Customs to take action to suspend the export of rice and white rice in accordance with the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen from April 5
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, this morning, March 30, 2020, issued an official letter to the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia to take action to suspend exports. Rice and white rice according to the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen from April 5, 2020 onwards until a new notification.
The Ministry of Economy's introduction to the General Department of Customs came after the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this morning, March 30, issued an order to suspend the export of white rice and rice from 23:00: 59 mins, March 5, 2020, to ensure Cambodia's food security in the face of the Kovid 19 crisis.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, said, "I have issued an order to suspend the export of white rice and rice, but allow the export of fragrant rice until there is a new order to keep the local supply and effective from April 5. 2020 onwards.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the ban on the export of rice is only white rice and rice for fragrant rice is allowed to export normally.
(Phnom Penh): While some people are suffering, Wing agents in the provinces and in Phnom Penh have volunteered to distribute rice, water, alcohol, hand wash, cola oil and some personal funds to distribute to people who are Deficiency to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
Ms. Eng Buntha, the owner of Wing BlueI, located on Street 430 near the Residence Hotel in Phnom Penh, said that seeing the rate of 19 cases of Kovid virus infection continuing daily, she donated 300 kilograms of Angkor alcohol. Wash your hands and distribute cola oil to those in need.
"Some scavengers and motodup drivers cannot buy alcohol to protect themselves from the 19-virus virus," she said. During this difficult time, they could not earn a decent living to support themselves. Therefore, my family donated 300 kilograms of rice to distribute to them.
Seeing her kindness, her neighbors also donated cola oil, water, hand wash to distribute to those in need. As of March 28, more than 100 siblings have received generous gifts from her family and neighbors.
Mrs. Kong Mony Pheakdey, the owner of Wing Ratanak Rainsy in Chhouk Meas Market, Phnom Penh, regularly distributes hand gel to her passengers and customers. "I distribute their gels at all four of my Wing outlets, one day at a time. At each store, I distribute about 100 bottles," she said. In addition, I donate money to various associations to help the poor as well.
Separately, in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, Wing agents with the brand name Nguon Sitha shared a lot of alcohol, hand washing and masks for free to customers and travelers.
Not to mention that the Wing agents in Phnom Penh, even the Wing agents in the provinces, also participated in preventing 19 Kovids. For example, the family of Mr. Khin Ly Hak, the owner of Wing Agent and his family also donated 4 million Riels to help the needy people in Sral village, Treng Trayeung commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province through the village chief. Families can request this budget for 100,000 Riels.
In addition, there are WING agents in other places in Cambodia who have volunteered to donate their own money to support the needy Cambodians.
