(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has confirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia will prepare a draft law governing the country in case of an outbreak of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the remarks at a press conference at the National Assembly this morning, March 30, 2020, after the National Assembly voted to support the appointment and revision of the new composition of the Royal Government. Cambodia, 6th mandate.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "We have already drafted this law, including the statement. "We will have a division of what to do, what not to do, and then put in place measures to close any public and private places that are necessary to respond."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has not yet confirmed the content of the draft law, stating that the content will be revealed at the next cabinet meeting on Friday. Samdech Techo further stated that the draft law governing the country in case of emergency was prepared by Mr. Keut Rith, the new Minister of Justice, and also sent to all Deputy Prime Ministers.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen had sent a message to his compatriots about the consideration to ask the King for permission to put Cambodia "in a state of emergency" as the situation of Kovid 19 spread more and more people. More than 100 people were infected.
Under the current constitution, declaring a country in a state of emergency is an application under Article 22 when the nation is in unpredictable danger. However, the Cambodian Constitution does not clearly state the meaning or actions of putting the country in a state of emergency.
The new Article 22 states, "When the nation is in danger, the King shall publicly declare the nation in a state of emergency after the approval of the Prime Minister, the President of the National Assembly and the President of the Senate."
Prasat Chrung dedicated to the bodhisattva Lokesvara
(Siem Reap): Prasat Chrung is a small temple located within the outer walls of the Bayon temple at the corner of the Om River (southwest of the walls of Nokor Thom). At the entrance to the south side of Angkor Thom and turn left, travel along the river Om to the west to the corner of the temple wall, we will see a small temple there is a corner temple. Prasat Chrung is a place where you can see the sacred and interesting sunset.
Prasat Chrung is a pavilion or library measuring about 15m x 10m and about 570 cm high facing east, which houses important inscriptions and rules that describe the construction in detail. The Great Wall of Kasin, the surrounding water and the entrance to Angkor Thom during the reign of King Jayavarman VII.
Prasat Chrung was built during the reign of Jayavarman VII, built in the late 12th century to be dedicated to the Bodhisattva Lokesvara and in the Bayon style. Currently, there is a lot of damage and damage ....
