(Phnom Penh): March 30, 2020 A new international hospital was announced to open this Monday to provide health care and treatment services to Cambodians without having to travel to neighboring countries.
The Presbyterian Hospital is an international hospital run by one of the top international healthcare leaders from Singapore, along with doctors and specialists from Singapore, France and the United States.
"The services and standards we bring to Cambodia are world-class and Singapore-based health care by the best doctors, nurses and professionals with the latest technology," said Dr. Thay Christopher, Executive Director of The Prestige Hospital. .
"Our hospital is more affordable than the hospital in Singapore," he said. He added: "Our vision is to be your health care partner forever. "Our mission is to provide effective treatment with the latest health technology in accordance with international medical methods and with high ethics."
Cambodians who are experiencing health problems or in need of highly skilled health care do not need to travel abroad anymore, as The Presbyterian Hospital offers the same standard of service as Singapore and other international hospitals.
The Presbyterian Hospital is ready to examine and care for patients through services such as laboratory imaging, ultrasound imaging, X-rays, CT scans, breast examinations, gastric examinations, colonoscopies, obstetrics. Pediatric gynecology and general surgery.
In the coming months, our hospital will add some services such as ear, nose, throat, men and eye health, and medical equipment is modern and the latest equipment from the United States, Germany and Japan.
Dr. Thai Christopher said, "In addition to providing care and treatment services in Cambodia, we will work closely with health partners and the Ministry of Health to raise the standard of health care." More.
All in all, The Presbyterian Hospital does not treat Kovid patients, but we will work with hospitals designated by the Ministry of Health and other institutions involved in Kovid cases.
In the first phase, The Presbyterian Hospital will be open from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. Our hospital welcomes all guests, but we urge you to make an appointment in advance to make it easier.
Executive Director:
Dr. Theay added, "Although the standard of health care here is good, I would like to take this opportunity to share my experience to help improve the healthcare sector in Cambodia." Holds Singaporean and international standards. ”
