Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced, "I am just signaling that there will be a reshuffle of the Council of Ministers shortly after the law on the establishment of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation takes place, then we will have a ministerial election." That minister is still Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, but there may be some ministries to adjust.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further explained that it is normal for the cabinet to be reshuffled, that in some countries it is changed more quickly, and that the amendment is not so strong as to dissolve the government, only to find that there is numbness in place. In some places, it is less effective and does not meet the wishes of the Royal Government.
It should be noted that the Council of Ministers of the 6th Mandate, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was established in September 2018 after the Cambodian People's Party won the National Assembly Election of the 6th Mandate by winning all the seats in National Assembly. The new cabinet is made up of the prime minister, deputy prime ministers, senior ministers and ministers.
