On the morning of March 29, 2020, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia also issued a call to people not to use the rapid test kits to detect 19 Kovid on their own.
In a press release on the morning of March 29, 2020, the Ministry of Health confirmed that there is currently a large number of rapid test kits, but so far no 19 kovid test kits are available. Accreditation by the World Health Organization is still valid and effective.
The ministry added that the effectiveness of such rapid tests is still very low and there are many uncertain results, such as those who do not have the virus turn out to be positive and those who do have the virus turn out to be negative. Instead.
The Ministry states that only the National Institutes of Public Research and the Institut Pasteur du Cambodge, which are operating in accordance with the World Health Organization's standards and operating principles, have issued valid results.
The Ministry of Health has warned that anyone who uses the Kovid 19 virus test kit to publish it without the Ministry of Health's permission will be prosecuted.
The ministry also called on the relevant authorities to take the strictest legal action against any person or company that publishes the Kovid 19 rapid test kit without the permission of the Ministry of Health.
