Important messages of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the press conference from the National Assembly
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, March 30, 2020, the National Assembly convened to vote on the appointment and reshuffle of the Royal Government of Cambodia. The plenary session of the National Assembly was also in the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
After the National Assembly closed its session to vote on the appointment and reshuffle of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen held a special press conference, delivering a message to his compatriots.
The following are the main messages of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the closure of all casinos nationwide from April 1, 2020
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people not to believe the propaganda in Cambodia that there is a cure for Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen bans the export of white rice and paddy to ensure domestic supply, effective from April 5, 2020 until further notice
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns to arrest Mr. Am Sam Ath, who supports the illegal process of selling counterfeit products related to Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen orders the authorities to cooperate with the prosecutor to arrest and confiscate 19 Kovid test equipment to the seller and advertiser's house
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people to turn their fears into self-defense by following the measures of the Ministry of Health
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the media and all the singers and songwriters who helped with the campaign against Kovid 19 and educated the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has instructed more than 50,000 Cambodian workers from Thailand to be isolated for 14 days and their families must be notified in front of their houses to prevent Kovid 19 infection
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 19 Kovid diseases found in Cambodia so far are imported diseases
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all people from Thailand must be careful not to become a carrier of Kovid 19 virus to their families and communities.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if any workers suspected that they had Kovid 19 virus, they should immediately seek medical attention.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns not to tolerate people who insult the Khmer medical certificate
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen encourages all shops to have alcohol to wash their hands
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is not a place for drug testing
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the private sector to do business with mutual understanding
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the owners of locations that are rented out to other businesses to be understanding, which can delay payment or lower prices during the Kovid 19
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says the state is considering disbursing $ 500 million to $ 600 million for low-interest loans to banks and microfinance institutions
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen: So far, philanthropists have contributed more than 10 million US dollars to support the 19 Kovid battle campaign in Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has ordered about 3 million masks from abroad due to our shortage
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the ministers who have changed now are all capable, but due to their age, they have to change.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that the Royal Government has already prepared a draft law related to placing the country under a state of emergency.
* Samdech revealed that the new Minister of Justice, Mr. Keut Rith, was the one who drafted the law to put the country in a state of emergency.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen will request the Supreme Constitutional Council to interpret Article 86 and Article 102 of the Constitution regarding the powers of the National Assembly and the Senate in the country in a state of emergency.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Weak or strong country, health is now measured by the number of people who died due to Kovid.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has taken central measures without closing the country, but put in place other measures
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that customs revenue decreased but tax revenue increased, which was about $ 700 million
