(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the National Working Group to Assist Oddar Meanchey Province on Sunday, March 29, 2020, will continue to bring food, food, budget and krama to distribute to people in need due to Effects of Kovid 19.
Oddar Meanchey is a province bordering Thailand, and many people often do business by crossing the border between the two countries. Due to the effects of Kovid 19, the two countries temporarily closed their borders to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The closure of the border causes people to lose their jobs and the income they used to earn on a daily basis and also affect their livelihoods. Senior Minister Kun Kim said that there are more than 10,000 families in Oddar Meanchey province.
To solve the hardships of the people, the Senior Minister, who is the chairman of the national working group to help this province bordering Thailand, and the working group has mobilized various charitable donations, especially food to distribute to those in need in this life to Solve their difficulties.
On the occasion of delivering food to these disadvantaged people, Senior Minister Kun Kim explained the hardships of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the whole world due to the effects of Kovid 19.
The Senior Minister also informed the people about the consideration and attention from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and instructed all national working groups to bring food to the people in rural areas.
"This is the problem of our nation and not only our nation but the world is suffering because of the spread of Kovid 19 disease. However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen are very careful in solving the problems of the whole nation and our people. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim when he visited the backs of people's houses.
However, Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Assistance Team, is determined to address all the difficulties of the people of Oddar Meanchey. The senior minister asked people to contact local authorities when they encounter problems so that the relevant authorities can find a solution.
During the visit to the backyards of the people providing food, Senior Minister Kun Kim also instructed the people to follow the hygiene rules of the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread and infection of Kovid 19.
The hygiene rules that the senior minister introduced to the people include washing their hands thoroughly with soap before and after eating or when returning from outside the house, etc. When going out or gathering places, wear or use a mask. For example, food must be cooked well, reduce the number of gatherings. Especially when there is a health problem, contact the local authority or health officer at the health center or the phone number shown.
