In this situation, the Ministry of Commerce would like to make the following calls:
1. The public is kindly requested to maintain that status, not to be overly disturbed, leading opportunists to take advantage of unreasonable price increases.
2: Let all shop owners, traders and online sellers adhere to the spirit of Khmer national unity, do not take the opportunity to increase the price of goods for excessive profit.
3. All shopkeepers and traders are required to affix the riel price tag on the goods circulating in the market in order to ensure a free market economy mechanism, fair competition and promote local currency circulation in order to serve the interests. The general population.
In the case of face masks, hand rubs, alcohol, hand jelly and alcohol thermometers, the seller must raise the price tag in large riel so that the public can see clearly from a distance.
The Ministry of Commerce emphasizes that it will send professional officers to cooperate with relevant authorities to investigate, inspect the quality, safety and price of goods, and to implement legal measures in case of finding crooks who take the opportunity to sell goods at exorbitant prices. .
The Ministry sincerely hopes that the public, shopkeepers, traders and online sellers will all comply with this call to enforce the law and show the spirit of Khmer national unity under the umbrella of peace that we are receiving.
