Faced with the COVID-19 crisis, many countries have taken measures to close the whole country, some partially shut down, others declared a state of emergency, and some have taken drastic measures to combat this global pandemic. These countries include:
South Africa: On Thursday, March 26, 2020, South Africa announced a 21-day nationwide shutdown, with only key businesses and services resumed.
New Zealand announced the closure of the entire country on Wednesday, March 25, 2020. The closure will be eased after a month.
Colombia: Introduces separate accommodation measures nationwide, requiring people aged 70 and over to stay indoors until May, when the measure lasts 19 days.
* United Kingdom: Closed nationwide on Monday, March 23, 2020 for 3 weeks. Letting go of the house until there is a necessary job.
Australia: Australian authorities on Monday, March 23, 2020, temporarily closed bars, clubs, gyms, cinemas and religious venues, as well as all non-essential services.
* Argentina: Close the country by requiring people to go out to find only essential services. The measure was implemented from March 21 to March 31.
Israel: On March 19, 2020, the country was temporarily closed to foreigners.
Belgium: Closed on March 17, 2020, and the measure could last for eight weeks.
Norway: Closed for two weeks on March 12, and on Tuesday, March 24, 2020, the Norwegian government announced the implementation of this measure until April 12.
* Denmark: Closed measures were announced on March 11 and extended until April 13.
* Belgium: Requires its people to implement isolated measures across the country until April 5. Can go out of the house for urgent tasks or urgent services.
United States: Declared a state of emergency on March 13.
Malaysia: Measures to close the whole country first expire on March 31, but the Kuala Lumpur government has decided to extend it until April 14, 2020.
Philippines: Manila government imposes partial closure measures until April 13, 2020.
Indonesia: Declared a state of emergency in Jakarta on Monday, March 23, 2020.
South Korea declares health emergency on Sunday, February 23, 2020.
