This statement by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng was made this morning, March 27, 2020, on the occasion of presiding over the dissemination ceremony of Sub-Decree No. 39 on the revision of Sub-Decree No. 44 on the Transaction Penalty. Violation of the law on road traffic.
On March 17, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issued a new sub-decree amending the sub-decree on transitional penalties for violations of the road traffic law. This new sub-decree amended some articles such as Article 6, Article 7, Article 10, Article 11, Article 12, Article 13, Article 14 and Article 15 of Chapter 3 regarding the offenses and the amount of fines of Sub-Decree No. 44 dated March 21, 2017.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also appealed and issued a number of regulations to improve road traffic safety in Cambodia, while 2020 is the year of tightening road traffic laws, including:
* First, all road users, please understand the strict legal measures for road traffic offenses. In order to avoid legal challenges, please strictly abide by the law on road traffic to protect your own life, for the harmony of the family, to protect your property and to jointly promote the honor and dignity of the nation. We.
* Second, the relevant ministries, institutions, authorities, competent forces at all levels, national and international organizations and the media should continue to educate and disseminate the law on road traffic and the level of interim penalties for violations of the law on road traffic. And stick to it regularly.
* Third: I would like to issue an order to the leaders and officers of the traffic police throughout the country to strictly enforce the law on road traffic with strict strictness, not to understand and to properly implement all legal procedures. Violation of road traffic in a transparent, fair and non-discriminatory manner and must cooperate in the search and arrest of the perpetrators of road traffic accidents who have escaped and bring them to justice.
* Fourth, the traffic police leadership must prepare an action plan and organize a force to monitor, monitor and support the law enforcement operations of the traffic police officers under their supervision to ensure the correct implementation of the law by all traffic police officers, and must Strengthen attitudes, morals and discipline to be worthy of law enforcement officers with virtue and professional conscience.
Provides state-mandated bonuses with commendation of competent units and officials, and severe disciplinary action against inactive or unethical officials.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng strongly believes that the leaders and officers of the land traffic police throughout the country will continue to work hard to fulfill their duties and responsibilities in enforcing the law on road traffic with a high sense of responsibility. To jointly reduce road traffic accidents to a maximum.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng requested all road users and all citizens to strictly abide by the law on road traffic in order to maintain better order and safety of road traffic.
