The Cambodian Association of Banks and Microfinance is committed to providing services to the people despite the situation of Covid-19 disease
(Phnom Penh): The Banking Association and the Cambodian Microfinance Association have issued a joint statement expressing their high commitment to continue to provide banking and financial services to clients and the public at all times and in all circumstances.
The joint announcement by the Association of Banks and the Cambodian Microfinance Association comes after some citizens and the public were concerned about the bank's services as the world and Cambodia spread the Covid-19 disease.
According to the announcement, the banking and microfinance institution provides banking and financial services to customers and the public through four infrastructures:
1: Branches and offices of banking and microfinance institutions are open to customers and the public at all business hours throughout the country from Monday to Friday. Some commercial banks also offer additional services until Saturday morning.
2: Electronic banking services have ATMs and POS machines that are available to customers 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.
3: Internet Banking: Customers and the public can use the Internet banking services themselves anytime and anywhere.
4: Digital Mobile Banking: Customers and the public can use digital mobile banking by themselves anytime and anywhere.
