(Oddar Meanchey): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, confirmed that from March 22 to 26, 2020, local authorities across the country will control the number of people returning from Thailand to their hometowns. More than 40,000 people.
This confirmation by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng was made on March 26, 2020, on the occasion that Samdech had a face-to-face meeting with officials of various units and institutions working at the gates. The Cambodian-Thai border is located in Oddar Meanchey province, where the meeting took place at the O'Smach International Gate Police Station.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that on behalf of the Royal Government and Samdech Techo, he commended the provincial administration, districts, communes, sangkats, villages and the national working group for working together with the border authorities and the people in border protection to manage the border. Border gates and the entry and exit of citizens on both sides, in the past and especially in the fight against the deadly 19 Kovid disease.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that in the face of this epidemic, some of our Cambodian citizens have rushed back from Thailand to Cambodia, so all border guards must be ready to welcome the people well. Further, there must be strict measures in accordance with health regulations.
On that occasion, the provincial governor said that the people who crossed the border into the country from March 23 to 25, as of 4:30 pm, more than 1,200 people, of which more than 400 people. Citizens of Oddar Meanchey province, and most of the authorities have captured the identity.
