Spokesman Jin Malin: The Ministry of Justice is considering using mobile courts to reduce case congestion (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Justice Chin Malin Apparently congested, the Minister of Justice is considering using a six-month trial mobile tribunal to clear the remaining cases, which is also a factor in facilitating inmates in prisons.
In a press conference on the progress and work direction of the Ministry of Justice organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of March 26, 2020, Mr. Jean Malin confirmed that the mechanism is set to be used in case of stalemate. In court, but the Ministry of Justice has never used it, so the future is a time of testing.
According to Mr. Chin Malin, this mobile court means that both mobile judges, mobile cases and mobile courts, in the case of judges in any provincial court are free to go to work in other provinces and take the remaining cases to clear and Take any of the same vacant courtroom locations for adjudication.
Spokesman Jin Malin said: "We are considering a mobile court that is governed by the law. This mobile court is mobile, both the case judges, the jurisdiction and the mobile court. "Therefore, this mobile court is under consideration to release the congestion of court cases for a long time."
In addition, Mr. Jean Malin explained that the reason for the congestion in the court case is due to the lack of human resources compared to the case that the court receives every day.
He asserted that the ministry will continue to expand its physical infrastructure, including two frameworks, including the expansion of the courtroom, the expansion of the court building and the implementation of the law enforcement of mobile courts. Both of these points the Ministry is considering going forward to address the current challenges.
But for the question of when the mobile court is planned to be implemented? Mr. Jean Malin has not yet been able to confirm that he will have to wait for the next decision of the Minister of Justice, but he only revealed that he will start the trial first at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, considering that if the Phnom Penh Municipal Court is removed As can be removed in court across the country.
