Ministry of Agriculture Introduces Immediate Response to Programs and Development Projects in the Context of the Global Outbreak of Kovid 19
According to a guideline obtained by Fresh News today, the rapid spread of 19 Kovid cases worldwide and in the region could have a devastating effect on the lives of people, especially the population. Farmers in the countryside.
In response to this, the Ministry of Agriculture would like to advise you, the Director of Programs or Development Projects, the Head of the Sub-Unit and the Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to immediately implement the following necessary measures:
1. Implement necessary actions in an emergency in response to increase food production with quality and safety in order to contribute to increase employment opportunities and income for rural people as well as workers who have just returned from abroad.
In this regard, it is necessary to examine the emergency response activities in the project to solve water problems by using water-saving systems, digging and restoring ponds, ponds and wells, etc. Financing farmers in all forms refers to the establishment of new farms as well as supporting and expanding the production of fast-growing food, etc.
2. Examine the budget that can be used to implement immediate response activities, expedite the implementation of programs and budget payment activities in a timely manner and reduce any unnecessary expenses.
3. Request a relaxation of the requirements of the project advance budget request, streamline procurement procedures and budget allocation to be able to fully implement the work that is needed.
4. Encourage units and stakeholders who have received project financing to take measures to promote and expand the market for more active and strong products.
The Ministry of Agriculture also stated that, after receiving this instruction, the Director of the program or development project, the head of the subordinate unit and the director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital and Provinces must cooperate to implement it effectively.
