(Battambang): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the afternoon of March 25, 2020, met with officials of various units and institutions working at the border gates of Battambang province. And Pailin Province. The meeting was held at Kamrieng District Hall, Battambang Province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Senator, National Assembly, senior leaders of the Ministry of Interior, Battambang and Pailin Provincial Working Group, Provincial Council of Governors, as well as government officials and forces under the administration of Battambang and Pailin, especially civil servants. And forces serving in the Cambodian-Thai border gate units.
Speaking on that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the presence of Samdech and other leaders in this meeting is a contribution to encourage all officials who are working in the units at the border - Thailand, both in Battambang and Pailin, in a context where the world is facing the epidemic of Kovid 19, which has now become a global crisis.
Regarding the deployment of the Thai government during a state of emergency, the prince stated that if any Cambodians continued to return to the country, the Royal Government could not prevent the citizens from returning. The prince advised to be ready to welcome them with a dignified, polite and gentle attitude, but to take strict measures according to health rules to ensure the safety of them and their families in their hometown.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng instructed the authorities at the border gate to clearly record the identities of citizens who have returned to the country to ensure that they are tracked down if there are any problems, and at the same time to make efforts to discuss with the Thai side to avoid Permission to cross the corridor, which makes it difficult to get medical check-ups and identify them, that is, clear gates for Cambodians to return to the country.
The prince also advised to be ready to provide masks to those who come from Thailand without masks and to ask them to cooperate in checking the heat and invite them to the place where the identity is to be recorded first. In case there is an emergency patient and the patient is not a Kovid 19 patient, the prince also advised the governors of Battambang and Pailin to ask for cooperation to allow the patient to receive treatment in Thailand.
Samdech believes that both Cambodia and Thailand will consider bilateral relations to protect the mutual interests between the two countries and peoples. Apparently, such as the closure of human-to-human traffic between Cambodia, Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam, where both sides continue to allow the entry and exit of goods under strict security conditions when transporting across the border.
Regarding the work of educating the people about measures to protect themselves and prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Prince Sar Kheng also commended all local authorities for organizing the broadcast of mobile educational messages in all villages and communes to the people. Citizens.
Before concluding, Samdech expressed his hope that the leaders, civil servants and forces under the provincial administration and are working in the Cambodian-Thai border units in Battambang and Pailin will continue to work hard to fulfill their roles and responsibilities. Good and careful to avoid Kovid 19 infection.
