This morning's meeting was broadcast live on TV and on Fresh News. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's meeting with a group of volunteer doctors today is to give advice and encouragement to the group of doctors who have volunteered to leave their families and loved ones in the face of illness to be saved. Human life.
To date, Cambodia has been taking action and introducing a number of measures to combat and prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The Ministry of Health recently called on medical professionals as well as medical students to help fight Kovid 19.
After the appeal, the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association (TYDA), with Mr. Hun Manet as Chairman and Ms. Pech Chanmony as Vice Chairman, also appealed.
Through this call, medical professionals, students and alumni have also applied for a series of activities to fight Kovid 19. After receiving the volunteers, the Samdech Techo Young Volunteer Doctors Association also opened training courses and provided additional technical training on the prevention and control of Kovid 19 transmission.
Ms. Pech Chanmony considered the participation of 19 volunteer doctors to fight Kovid as the first line for the society and the family, and this participation is very courageous. She considers these volunteer doctors to be the nation's true heroes in times of emergency.
When a nation is at war, it takes courage to enter the battlefield to defend its homeland. In the event that society is facing an epidemic, it needs a team of brave and courageous doctors to save lives.
Kovid 19, which has claimed the lives of more than 16,000 people, including doctors, is considered one of the worst diseases in the world today. Many people are scared and want to avoid this disease. On the contrary, the Cambodian medical team, as well as this group of volunteer doctors, are determined to overcome the prohibitions of parents, husbands, wives, children and Family to fight this disease.
The dedication of the Cambodian medical team is considered to be one of the most courageous and awe-inspiring epics for the cause of the Cambodian society and people. TOP NEWS: Today, the Ministry of Health found 4 new 19 cases of Kovid, increasing the total number of infections to 91, while 4 people were cured
