(Phnom Penh): Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Wentian said that China-Cambodia is a community that shares the same destiny in the most difficult times in the fight against the disease and the spread from China to Cambodia. The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia will closely monitor and maintain close ties with the Cambodian Ministry of Health to jointly combat the spread of the epidemic in Cambodia.
According to Wang Wentian, in line with the need for pandemic prevention in Cambodia, China will continue to provide the necessary material assistance and medical support in the future, and all these measures will enhance Cambodia's ability to prevent And control the spread of the disease.
Ai Xiang, head of the Chinese Medical Aid Team in Cambodia, said the main task of the Chinese medical team was to share and exchange experiences, as well as to guide the prevention and control of epidemics, to treat patients with mild and moderate illnesses. And laboratory work, as well as providing guidance and other medical assistance to the Chinese Embassy, enterprises, students and all Chinese in Cambodia.
Professor Mam Bunheng also said that this is a demonstration of the friendship between Cambodia and China with solidarity and brotherhood. China has experience in fighting this new pneumonia epidemic, so Cambodian medical staff will learn from Chinese experts. On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, he also expressed his deep gratitude to the Chinese medical experts who came to Cambodia.
The Chinese experts, set up by the National Committee for Health and Welfare of China, will be selected by the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region Health and Health Committee, which covers the following areas: prevention and control. Diagnosis and laboratory tests.
