(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia on the morning of March 24, 2020 issued a joint press release on the signing ceremony of the financing of a number of projects. Five, worth nearly $ 600 million.
The signing ceremony of financing for five projects, including five exchange letters and two concessional loan agreements, was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
1: Water supply system expansion project in Takhmao city (amounting to 3,421 million yen (approximately 30.7 million US dollars))
2: Integrated Mine Clearance and Relief Project (1 billion yen (approximately US $ 8.97 million)
3: Economic and Social Development Program by providing vehicles and equipment to Cambodia for the ASEAN Summit 2022 (300 million yen (approximately 2.7 million US dollars)
4: The project to improve National Road No. 5 (from Prek Kdam Bridge - Thla Mam, Pursat Province), the third phase, with the amount of 11,715 million yen, approximately 108 million US dollars.
5: The project to upgrade National Road No. 5 (from Thla Mam, Pursat Province, Battambang City and from Serei Sophorn City - Poipet City), the second phase, with the amount of 17,702 million yen, approximately 162 million US dollars.
B: Signing between: General Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. SUGANO Yuichi, President of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia, on two Concessional Loan Agreements $ 270 million. These two concessional loan agreements are additional credit packages for both projects, including:
1: Project to improve National Road No. 5 (from Prek Kdam Bridge - Thla Mam, Pursat Province), Phase 3, amounting to 11,715 million yen (approximately 108 million US dollars)
2: The project to upgrade National Road No. 5 (from Thla Mam, Pursat Province, Battambang City and from Serei Sophorn City - Poipet City), the second phase, with the amount of 17,702 million yen, approximately 162 million US dollars.
Due to the large demand for financing for each sector, the provision of credit for each sector took place in stages as the project progressed. In total, the section of National Road No. 5 (from Prek Kdam Bridge - Poipet City) with a total length of 366 km requires a concessional loan from the Government of Japan totaling about 840 million US dollars.
