Mr. Dmitry Schwartzkov's declaration of support for Cambodia was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong allowed him to pay a courtesy call this morning, March 23, 2020 at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
The Russian ambassador praised Cambodia's development in all areas, with economic growth of around 7% over the years, even though Cambodia is not an oil and gas producer like other countries. In addition, he was pleased that during his mission, 51 agreements and memoranda of understanding were signed between Cambodia and Russia, deepening our cooperation.
He hopes that the Russian President will attend the upcoming 13th Asia-Europe Summit in Cambodia.
