In less than two years, after transforming from a microfinance institution into a commercial bank, Prince Bank has focused its efforts on becoming an "employer of first choice," he said. "
"We want to create a work environment with clear human resource coordination procedures, adequate opportunities for employees to receive training and personal development, a work culture based on values and responsibilities," he added. "Encouragement for open and honest communication."
He added that in terms of recruitment, the bank has encouraged the participation of young people in Cambodia by participating in job fairs at universities and disseminated to provincial educational institutions.
Prince Bank has also developed an internship program, giving university students the opportunity to intern as frontline staff as well as head office staff. This program allows young people to gain hands-on experience working as a full-time employee at Prince Bank.
In addition, in line with its goal of becoming one of the fastest growing digital banks in Cambodia, Prince Bank is leveraging the potential of digital technology to serve the rapidly growing workforce.
The bank has launched an HR system that includes mobile applications that allow employees to manage leave, payroll, employee data and other HR administration functions from their smartphones. This program makes the human resource management process more efficient by reducing the time to respond to administrative work, reducing the use of paper and contributing to environmental solutions.
Digital technology also helps to train the bank's staff. The Bank has launched a digital training management system to make it easier for employees to learn subjects to complete their courses at their own pace.
This e-learning program complements in-class courses that include the technical and management skills training needed to succeed in staff work and customer service.
These strategies, along with core values such as professionalism, responsibility, integrity, dignity, commitment and self-esteem, aim to create a professional workplace that allows employees to succeed in the company and the bank has We believe that this strategy will continue to attract and retain highly committed and capable employees.
In the last two years, Prince Bank has almost doubled the number of employees to more than 1,000. Prince Bank is proud to have been named the World's Best Employer Award in the first quarter of this new year.
Prince Bank will continue to develop and improve the Bank's human resource management program to ensure that our employees can achieve strategic goals for the present, as well as be ready to become future leaders and be ready to push Prince Bank to become A digital bank that offers the best customer experience.
