Legal Awareness: Mandate
(Phnom Penh): Most people often hear the word "mandate" and think that this word is used only for the framework of civil servants, diplomats or MPs. But in addition to the use of words in the above sense, this mandate is also some of the daily activities of the people.
Therefore, in order to better understand the legal awareness program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, please explain the following topics related to the "mandate" to the people:
According to the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Article 637 defines a mandate as a contract in which one party is called a successor (delegated authority) and delegates authority to the other party, called an executive mandate. Assignments) Assign tasks to the successor mandate.
This mandate contract is made only with the consent of the parties, that is, it can be made orally or in writing and can be paid or not charged. Whether the contract is in the form of a fee or a non-fee, the manager must carefully manage the mandate as an honest manager based on the meaning of the mandate.
For the receipt of money and other items according to the assignment of the mandate, the assignment manager must hand over the money and other items to the delegate. In addition, the supervisor must also hand over the harvest to the delegate. In particular, the rights that the manager receives in his name so that the delegate can delegate that authority to the delegate.
In particular, in relation to the claim of the manager, the manager can not claim the fee for the mandate in the case that is not specified in the contract. In the case of contract for which the fee is paid, the manager may not claim the fee if the performance of the duties specified in the mandate is not completed, but if the fee is determined during that period, the fee can be claimed after that period. Passed.
At the same time, if the mandate contract is terminated in the middle due to non-responsibility of the manager, the manager may claim a fee in proportion to the portion already applied. You delegate the right to pay the costs in advance at the request of the manager in case there is a need for the expenses for the management of the mandate.
In addition, the manager may also demand that the delegate reimburse the costs and interest from the date after which the expenses were paid, if any payments were recognized as necessary for the management of the mandate or The Task Manager may authorize you to repay the obligation on your behalf if you have been assigned an obligation that is deemed necessary to perform the mandate.
On the other hand, if the damage is not caused by his fault in the assignment of the mandate, the manager can claim the compensation from the delegate. However, if the damage is intentional or the fault of a third party, the manager may only claim compensation to the delegate to the extent that no third party (third party) has received compensation.
Conversely, in the event that the Task Manager violates the above precautionary duties by causing damage to the Delegate, the Delegate may claim damages from the Manager. However, for non-commissioned contracts, the court may reduce the amount of damages.
Each party can terminate the mandate contract at any time. However, one party shall be liable for damages if the termination of the contract during the period which is detrimental to the interests of the other party, unless there are unavoidable reasons.
The mandate contract may be terminated for reasons such as if the heir or governing mandate has died or been declared bankrupt or has been declared a general guardian or declared a foster parent or a legal entity has been dissolved or is a legal entity. Combined with other legal entities or other reasons as determined by the agreement of the parties occurred.
However, the parties may agree that the mandate does not end even if the above-mentioned reasons have occurred, except for the death of the assignment manager, the commencement of the general guardianship for the assignment manager, or the dissolution or incorporation of the assignment manager. As a legal entity.
In summary, the mandate in this sense does not refer to the activities of public officials or deputies, but to the types of contracts stipulated in the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia. When creating a contract of this mandate or other contract, the people should make it in writing, even if the law does not stipulate that the creation of a contract in writing to avoid future problems related to rights and obligations or term. Time, for example.
