(Phnom Penh): The police force of the Economic Crime Police Department of the Ministry of Interior cooperated with the local police to crack down on the sale of counterfeit alcohol.
The operation was led by Mr. Say Nora, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Chan Van Thoeun, Director of the Economic Crime Police Department of the Ministry of Interior, and Mr. Long Sreng, Deputy Director of the Economic Crime Police Department of the Ministry of Interior, confiscated alcohol. A large number of counterfeits are illegally imported.
According to the authorities, the counterfeit alcohol confiscated included: 75 cans of alcohol, 19 barrels, 1 barrel weighing 163 kilograms.
Sources from the police at the scene also said that a large number of counterfeit alcohol was illegally imported by the warehouse owner.
After the inspection, the owner of the above location and the fake alcohol were taken away by the authorities to wait for the settlement at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in accordance with legal procedures.
On the afternoon of March 18, 2020, officials from the General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce continued to inspect pharmacies near the Olympic Market, seizing several liters of counterfeit alcohol from a pharmacy while Selling.
Four liters of methanol alcohol equal to 20 liters were confiscated and the General Department of CamControl would like to call on people not to buy any unlabeled and uncertified alcohol products to use for cleaning. Antiviral or prevent Covid-19 virus.
