(Kuwait): The Cambodian Embassy in Kuwait on March 21 issued a proclamation on the nine measures to prevent and combat the Covid-19 disease that the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced to the people and Cambodian students living in this state.
The nine measures include:
First, to be isolated for 14 days for those who travel from countries and territories such as Hong Kong, China, Egypt, South Korea, Italy, Iran, Iraq, Britain, Germany, France, Spain and the United States.
Second, all travelers from countries other than the above countries must stay at home for the same 14 days.
Third: Suspend all air travel to and from Kuwait.
Fourth, any embassy wishing to evacuate its citizens from Kuwait must meet the following conditions: * Send name and passport number * Detailed flight and travel reports * Request to the Department Consulate of the Kuwaiti Ministry of Foreign Affairs 72 hours in advance.
Fifth, gatherings are prohibited.
Sixth, all ministries, institutions of the state, the private sector, restaurants, and department stores shall be suspended from the date of this notification until March 29, 2020 or until a new notification is issued.
Seventh, during the above leave, the Kuwaiti Ministry of Foreign Affairs continues to work in some departments, with only reduced working hours and some unnecessary staff.
Eighth, all visas to Kuwait were suspended, except for two exceptions: official delegations and emergency visas issued by the Kuwaiti Embassy in those countries. Even visa-exempt countries require a visa from the Kuwaiti embassy there.
Ninth, the Kuwaiti Ministry of Foreign Affairs has deployed a number of staff in each department in the presence of the Assistant Minister.
