$ 8 Million South Korean Ear, Nose and Throat Treatment Center Starts Construction
(Phnom Penh): Construction of the Ear, Nose and Throat Treatment Center at Ang Duong Hospital has begun. The building is expected to cost a total of $ 8 million with the help of the South Korean government through the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA).
The Krong Pali Ceremony for the Construction of the Ear, Nose and Throat Center was held on March 21, 2020, with the participation of the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng and Mr. Nou Zun, Chief Representative of KOICA Agency.
The building is scheduled to take about 20 months to build and is scheduled to open in 2022. The Ear, Nose and Throat Center is 5 stories high.
The building will be equipped with the most modern and necessary equipment for examination, treatment and surgery to improve the quality of services in Preah Ang Duong Hospital to another level. In addition to improving the physical infrastructure, the capacity of all specialist doctors and staff will be enhanced through training programs and the transfer of knowledge and skills from Korean doctors.
Please note that Cambodia is one of the core partners of KOICA to receive development assistance in various fields. In Cambodia, KOICA has a Country Partnership Strategy (CPS) to assist the Royal Government of Cambodia in achieving its National Strategic Development Plan, integrating the strategy with Cambodia's National Strategic Development Plan and the Government's Rectangular Strategy.
