The humanitarian activities of the CRC Sub-Branch in Russey Keo District were organized with the participation of Mrs. Sous Solida, Honorary Vice President of the CRC Sub-Branch and Deputy District Governor, and all the officials and authorities who are members of the Red Cross Sub-Branch. Some other communes in Cambodia are located at No. 588, Street 99R, Group 8, Toul Sangke Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo on the evening of March 20, 2020.
Please be informed that for the humanitarian donation that the CRC Sub-Branch of Russey Keo District has brought to support the members of the people affected by the house fire, each family received: 30 kg of rice, 1 case of drink, 1 kg of salt, 2 sticks of soy sauce, 2 sticks of fish sauce, 1 metal plate, 1 frying pan, 1 frying pan, 1 ice bucket, and 100,000 Riels.
Before donating food, supplies and some budget, Ms. An Phalla Chea Pisey brought a message of visit and condolences from the Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross in Phnom Penh and especially Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cross. The Cambodian Red Cross offers condolences to the families of the victims of the house fire.
At the same time, Ms. An Phalla Chea Pisey reminded people to always pay high attention to the use of fire, incense, gas stoves and other items that are most flammable if we lack caution.
Ms. An Phalla reminded that in addition to being careful about the use of other objects that are easily and flammable, it is more important to use the right electrical technicians to avoid possible fires. Occurs eventually, combined with good health care, hygiene to avoid the risk of COVID-19 infection.
No one was injured in the blaze, which was caused by an electrical fault. This was confirmed by Mr. Chea Pisey, Governor of Russey Keo District and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, told Fresh News.
Mr. Chea Pisey stated that immediately after the house fire, there was the intervention of the authorities and the fire brigade 16 units that came out from various units to help intervene in time to prevent the fire from spreading to the house. Other residents were able to control and completely extinguish the fire within 40 minutes, using 12 units of water.
The Chob Koki and O'Smach border crossings next to Thailand will be temporarily closed while the Choam Sangam checkpoint is still open. From tomorrow, sales in Moeung Mai Thai Market will be temporarily suspended.
(Oddar Meanchey): The situation of the Cambodia-Thailand border checkpoint in Oddar Meanchey province as of March 21, 2020, the Chub Koki area checkpoint in Banteay Ampil district and the O'Smach international border crossing in Samrong city have been temporarily closed. Meanwhile, Choam International Border Crossing in Anlong Veng district is still open as usual. People who use passports or border cards can enter and exit normally.
According to the announcement of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration, which was received by Fresh News this morning, March 21, 2020, according to the actual situation and in the situation of Kovid 19 disease that is spreading globally and based on the announcement The Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration has confirmed that the Thai side will participate in preventing and controlling the spread of Kovid 19 worldwide.
* First, the Chob Koki border checkpoint in Banteay Ampil district (Saytakou checkpoint, Ban Kruot district, Borei Ram province) will be temporarily closed from March 19, 2020 until further notice.
* Second, the O'Smach International Border Gate in Samrong City (Chhong Cham International Border Crossing, Kab Cheung District, Surin Province) will be temporarily closed from March 21, 2020, without allowing people, vehicles and goods to pass through. Temporary entry until further notice, except for commercial goods and in accordance with the technical standards of both countries.
