The World Bank said in a statement that despite the significant improvements in access to public services in Cambodia over the past few years, the quality of these services remains a challenge. One yet.
The direct feedback from users who are aware of these services, especially from the general public, is one of the key factors driving public quality improvements around the world.
The facilitator will prepare a scoreboard for citizens to evaluate the quality of public services and agree on a number of joint action plans with service providers to further improve the quality of services.
A second grant of US $ 1.72 million has been provided to the Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development to strengthen the capacity of government service providers to provide information to the public. About the function and use of funds by this committee and in responding better to the opinions of citizens.
"Strengthening Citizen Involvement is one of the key areas in the World Bank's Partnership Framework," said Ingona Dobraja, World Bank Country Manager. In Cambodia.
The World Bank recognizes the government's social accountability framework as an important general effort to complement investment in education, health, water supply and other services through a systematic and sustainable approach to mobilization. Citizens should be involved and strengthen the capacity of sub-national authorities to ensure that service providers are accountable in the performance of their functions.
Both grants are intended to support the implementation of the second phase of the Social Accountability Framework project, which runs from 2019 to 2023. This framework is an integral part of the government's decentralization reform program, which aims to strengthen the government's response to the needs of the people.
The Committee is composed of representatives from various government ministries, including the Ministry of Interior, Education, Youth and Sports, Health, Economy and Finance, Industry and Handicraft, and Public Works and Transport, and civil society representatives.
Daniel Shell Vanayagam, World Vision International Country Director for Cambodia, said: “Based on our experience and achievements over the years, I am confident that this new assistance will further strengthen the public service response to Meet the needs of service users.
"This social accountability framework is a new era of public service delivery that accompanies the promotion of constructive dialogue at the grassroots level to bring about lasting change in service delivery," he added. "Public, especially for vulnerable groups."
