(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Court on March 21, 2020, ordered the detention of a young man in the case of driving a backup car to hit the provincial police officers are tightening the traffic law that he was carrying drugs while Driving too.
The case of driving a backup car to hit a traffic police officer happened on March 20, 2020 in Tuol Krasaing village, Takhmao city, while the police were tightening the traffic law and stopped the offending car, but for this person not only did not stop No car, even driving a car to hit the police.
According to the Kandal Provincial Traffic Police, the operation was led by Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, Brigadier General Ven Sovin, Deputy Commissioner for Public Order, and Brigadier General Sarun Sovannara, Commissioner. Deputy Post Officer, as well as Mr. Chheng Sam Oeun, Director of the Traffic Bureau.
The police officer said that the young man who was driving the backup car to hit the police was named Thorn David, 21 years old, without a driver's license, driving a right-hand drive car with license plate TK-0614, driving at high speed, then the police gave a signal to Stop to check, but the driver turned away and increased the speed to the target of the police, the police escaped from the front of the car to avoid accidents.
After that, the police chased the offending car about 2 kilometers from the checkpoint, then stopped and sent to the Office of Road Traffic Police and checked and tested the driver found positive drugs.
(Kandal): For the past few days, people living in Andong Teuk village, Lumhach commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province have erupted in protest as they have sold land to Mr. Keo Moniroth's company but have not received it. All the money, but the company wants to pour the land in violation of the contract.
The people mentioned that this act was a conspiracy by the local officials and the land brokers in order to prevent them from performing their role as the competent authority to serve the people.
The victims' complaint, which is scheduled to be filed in Kandal Provincial Court, states that during February 2020, they received information on the final payment for the land they sold to Keo Moniroth in Prices for each plot, with prices ranging from $ 16 per square meter to $ 53 per square meter.
Mr. Chip Chanrith, the lawyer representing Mr. Jai Houming, said that the land was to be cut off from Mr. Moniroth through an agreement to end the dispute, which Mr. Moniroth swindled to sell more than $ 2 million worth of wind land. His client is in Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province.
Failure to pay twice more than a year ago, the landowners said that some local officials do not serve the people, but only want to benefit from them, which prolongs the payment time. They have been like this for more than a year.
