The new figures, which have just been reported, have slightly increased the prevalence of COVID-19 in this country compared to the recent 100-day figure. Always the case. As of Friday, only 87 cases were reported.
While the government and development partners are working to prevent the spread of the virus, we all have an important role to play in this effort.
Experiences from countries such as Hong Kong, Taiwan and Singapore have shown that temporary reduction in social participation is an effective way to prevent the spread of the coronavirus. This is because the virus is transmitted through communication between the patient and the patient. And people with the virus may not show symptoms for up to 14 days, so during this time you can pass the virus on to others without realizing it.
Therefore, to reduce the risk that you may be infected or transmit the coronavirus to others, you can take the following actions:
* Suspend arranging and attending events such as birthday parties, housewarmings and gatherings of friends.
* Suspend travel abroad or to crowded tourist areas
Change the greeting and respect from a handshake into a salutation
Try to reduce contact with the face, eyes and nose before washing hands.
* Wear a mask when talking to others or keep a distance of 2 meters from the conversation partner.
Maintain good manners by covering your mouth and nose when you sneeze or cough.
Avoid sharing false information that can cause confusion and social unrest. Please research the source and accuracy of the information before sharing on social media.
Please consider that suspending the social activities of your friends, colleagues or neighbors in this circumstance is not discriminatory or hateful, but is necessary to maintain The health and life of you, your family and your siblings.
