Short video competition and knowledge on the use of digital libraries
(Phnom Penh): In the framework of the celebration of the 50th Francophone Francophone Day, the Office of the French Higher Education Agency (AUF) in Cambodia has organized a short video competition and a digital library literacy competition for students. Who speaks French is studying at AUF member universities.
A short video contest focused on the topic: What does Francophonie mean to you? Students were given the opportunity to express their views on the current use of the French language on the occasion of the 50th anniversary of the founding of the Organization of the French International (OIF).
To participate in the competition, students must create a video by taking a self-portrait via mobile phone or tablet in French for 1 minute and do not have to make any special cuts. Students then post their videos on the AUF video game website.
Forty-two students registered for the competition from various universities: University of Health Sciences, Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Royal University of Phnom Penh, Royal University of Law and Economics, Royal University of Fine Arts, and National Institute of Education. Of all the contestants, only 31 posted and posted their videos on their Facebook page.
The AUF jury selected the 13 best videos based on the right techniques, including originality and creativity, respect for the subject and accuracy of the content, image and sound quality and attractiveness according to the number of visitors on the Facebook page.
The 23 registered students are: University of Health Sciences, Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Royal University of Phnom Penh, Royal University of Law and Economics, and National Institute of Education.
