Takeo Provincial Commissioner Instructs Police Standing on the Border to Suspend Citizens' Travel to Vietnam to Prevent COVID-19
(Phnom Penh): Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sok Samnang on March 20, 2020, visited and disseminated the instruction of the General Commission of National Police on Emergency Measures to Prevent the Epidemic of COVID-19 and Instruction Of the Ministry of Interior on the temporary suspension of people's entry and exit to Vietnam to the National Police Officer of Border Guard Battalion No. 603 of Takeo Provincial Police.
Speaking on that occasion, Major General Sok Samnang reminded all border police officers to continue to advise people who have to travel to Vietnam to temporarily stop to prevent the spread of COVID-19. The commissioner added that the suspension was made until further notice.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia on March 19, 2020 issued a letter to the Vietnamese Embassy in Cambodia stating the temporary suspension of cross-border travel without the permission of the people of the two countries. No crossing. The implementation of this measure must take place from 23:59 pm on March 20, 2020.
Cambodia's decision to temporarily suspend travel along the Cambodian-Vietnamese border came after an order from Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen after the Vietnamese government decided to close the border immediately without notice. Royal Government of Cambodia.
The decision to suspend border crossings between the two countries was made in order to avoid difficulties at the two countries' border crossings, citing a sharp increase in the number of cases of Kovid virus infection 19. Vietnam has imposed travel restrictions that require 14 days of isolation for travelers from ASEAN member countries, including returning Vietnamese.
