The Senate will convene an extraordinary session early next week to review and pass six agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On March 23, 2020, the Senate will convene its extraordinary meeting of the fourth legislature to review and pass six major agendas. This is according to the press release of the General Secretariat of the Senate on the afternoon of March 20, 2020, which was received by Fresh News.
This press release said that on the morning of March 20, 2020 at 08:00, the Standing Committee of the Senate held a meeting chaired by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia.
After reviewing and discussing, the Standing Committee of the Senate set March 23, 2020 at 8:00 AM for the 4th Extraordinary Session of the Senate with the following agenda:
1. Review and comment on the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
2. Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of the second protocol on the amendment of the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement.
3. Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of the third protocol on the amendment of the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement.
4. Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of the first protocol to amend the ASEAN Trade Agreement.
5. Review and comment on the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on the Transfer of Prisoners between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
6. Review and comment on the draft law on the ratification of the Treaty on Mutual Legal Aid in the field of criminal law between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
