National Assembly Expert Committee holds meeting with representatives of the Royal Government to review three important draft laws
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly Expert Committee held a meeting with representatives of the Royal Government to review three important draft laws.
1. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Royal Group Investment Private Company for Investment Project for Construction of 700 MW Coal-Fired Power Plant in Koh Kong Province.
2: Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Hanseng Coleman Company for Investment Project for Construction of 230 KV Transmission Line from Oddar Meanchey Coal Power Plant to Siem Reap Substation East.
3. Draft Law on the Approval of the Payment Guarantee of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Hanseng Coleman Company for Investment Project for Construction of 265 MW Coal-Fired Power Plant in Oddar Meanchey Province.
Dr. Rath Cheam Yeap stated that at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, to hold an extraordinary session on the above draft law in accordance with the law. Therefore, the National Assembly will discuss and approve in the next extraordinary session of the National Assembly.
He said that with the three draft laws, there are only three articles. This draft law is only a ratification law. He added that the National Assembly has already approved more than 38 laws at the request of the Royal Government. The draft law is all the same, but the implementation is not the same, so the company will build the network.
He added that the construction of this plant as a source of electricity has both advantages and disadvantages. Therefore, the development of integrated energy sources is the right choice that can compensate for each other's shortcomings, ensure safety, sustainability, efficiency and affordability.
According to Dr. Rath, these draft laws could be approved by the National Assembly if the extraordinary session discusses them next week.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Issues 6 Guidelines for Passenger Company Owners to Prevent and Prevent COVID-19
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has issued a guideline on measures to prevent and control the spread of COVID-19 to all passenger transport companies in Cambodia.
Instructions received by Fresh News on the afternoon of March 20, 2020, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol instructed all bus company owners to implement the following important measures:
* First: Maintain a good customer service area, especially at the ticket office, waiting area, dining area, toilet, etc.
* Second: Check the health of drivers and service staff regularly and make sure they wear masks while working. If in doubt about their health, give them a break to monitor their health.
* Third: Measure the passenger's temperature and use alcohol to wash his hands before allowing him to board the car.
* Fourth: If the passenger is found to have symptoms such as: fever over 37.2 degrees Celsius, cough or sore throat or breathing problems, should not be allowed to get in the car and be advised to go to the health center. Call the nearest emergency number 115 of the Ministry of Health.
Fifth, the owner or manager of the passenger car must use alcohol or disinfectant to clean all the objects of the car that passengers often touch, such as bars, handrails, seats, etc. As often as possible.
* 6: Participate in promoting to all passengers to adhere to the rules of hygiene by washing hands after handling things before and after eating and have a mask or scarf to prevent coughing or sneezing during travel. Kampong Cham Provincial Administration Establishes Commission to Fight Covid-19 Disease
According to Kampong Cham provincial administration officials, after the Royal Government issued Resolution 29 pillars dated March 18, 2020 on the establishment of the National Commission for the Fight against Kovid 19 (Covid-19) with Samdech Techo Hun Sen The Prime Minister is the Chairman.
The Kampong Cham Provincial Administration has also established 19 Kovid Eradication Committees in its province, with Mr. Un Chanda, Provincial Governor of Kampong Cham, as the Chairman of the Joint Commission, and other government officials from relevant departments, units and institutions.
The same official also confirmed that the Kampong Cham provincial authorities have actively cooperated with the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Health and the World Health Organization in Cambodia, as well as civil society organizations and development partners to work closely together in the management. Implement measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia with high efficiency.
