Japanese government continues to provide more than $ 300,000 in grants for four projects in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has agreed to provide a total of $ 312,417 to four Cambodian units for the construction of health facilities, rehabilitation of irrigation systems and the installation of assistive devices to provide convenience to the rich. Physical disability under a grant for the Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni Assistance).
The signing ceremony was held on March 20, 2020 by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia and representatives of the four recipients.
This type of project is funded by the Japanese government because it includes:
* Second: The project to build a health center in Ratanakkiri province with a budget of $ 90,518 to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department.
In this project, a health center building with 10 health rooms will be built at a health center in Ratanakkiri province. Currently, the health center has only 3 rooms and medical services are limited.
Through this project, about 3,500 people in the coverage area will have better access to medical services, and health centers will provide quality medical services to their patients.
* Third: Rehabilitation project of Ponhea Leang Irrigation System, Prey Veng Province, $ 88,370 to Prey Veng Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology.
Japan's Kusanoni Grant began in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level.
This assistance aims to protect vulnerable people from a number of common factors, such as: Poverty and misfortune, which can directly threaten their livelihoods, livelihoods and dignity, as well as promote their self-reliance. Communities.
Since 1991, the Japanese government has provided more than $ 60 million to local authorities and NGOs to implement 632 Kusano projects across Cambodia. Ministry of Social Affairs issues guidelines on the implementation of preventive measures COVID-19 to national and international associations for child care centers and communities
