Farmers along the river harvest hundreds of tons of sesame this year
(Kampong Chhnang): Sesame crops this year have been cultivated by farmers living along the river because of the high price of sesame. In fact, in one month, farmers have harvested hundreds of tons of sesame seeds to sell in the market, and have been transported to Phnom Penh by middlemen to be sold in neighboring countries.
On the morning of March 19, 2020, at the Phsar Krom riverside port in Phsar Chhnang commune, several large boats carrying dozens of tons of sesame seeds were sold to brokers in Chong Koh village, Phsar Chhnang commune. In many riverside flats in Phsar Krom, there are brokers who buy tons of sesame stored in each house.
Kong Sophal, a sesame grower in Anlong Kanhchos village, Prolay Meas commune, Kampong Leng district, said he owned about five hectares of land and had planted all the sesame seeds. This year is more expensive than last year, although this year the weather is very hot and need to spend some oil pumping water to irrigate, he still made a decent profit.
He also said that the cultivation of sesame seeds needs to be closely monitored, especially to spray pesticides and spray pesticides thoroughly, which costs 500,000 to 600,000 per hectare to buy pesticides. Riel and will be repaid in 3 and a half to 4 months.
Separately, Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Chhnang Province, said on the afternoon of March 19, 2020 that according to the report he received from the district that farmers in Kampong Chhnang to grow sesame. The total area is 900 hectares, and the sesame harvest has reached 70% so far.
