The Ministry of Education calls on parents to teach their children more at home and use the program of the Ministry!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued a call to parents of all students to help train their children at home during the period when all levels of educational institutions are allowed to carry out vacations ahead of schedule.
In order to facilitate the learning of students, the Ministry of Education has launched a number of online curricula.
Recently, the Ministry has officially launched the "Children Learn, Children Know" program, which includes a set of reading and math materials at the primary level in primary school, such as instruction manuals for teachers and teaching and learning materials for use in Khmer language and mathematics. For first and second grade students who will supplement the existing Khmer textbook.
This program will help all Cambodian children, including children with disabilities, to develop their Khmer language and math skills better for a solid foundation to continue their education to the next level.
First graders will learn basic skills such as reading letters, spelling to read words, reading sentences and simple texts, and writing. To learn math, children need to learn numbers, shapes, geometry and the basics of calculation.
