The following is a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanking Duke Kith Meng and Lok Chumteav: Domestic violence leads to self-immolation, Preah Vihear provincial governor leads the force to intervene overnight
(Preah Vihear): A house was engulfed in flames, causing complete damage, which was caused by domestic violence, the husband could not resist and set himself on fire.
This shocking incident happened at 8:30 pm on March 19, 2020 in Tuol Tumnup village, Kampong Pranak commune, Preah Vihear city, Preah Vihear province.
Colonel Chao Vuthea, police inspector of Preah Vihear city, said on the morning of March 20, 2020 that before the incident, the host couple had an argument after arguing and then the wife walked out to relatives To make her husband angry up to 100 degrees Celsius, he pulled out a bottle of gasoline and poured it on his own house, causing a huge fire.
After the incident, Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, together with the provincial leaders, visited the scene and intervened to prevent the fire from burning to the houses of the neighbors.
Mr. Chao Vuthea said that in the fire incident, the police intervened by using 3 fire trucks and 15,000 liters of water to completely extinguish the fire at 9:30 pm on the same day. That.
According to the Preah Vihear City Inspector, the house that caught fire was 5m x 12m, made of wood, brick, zinc, including property damage: 10 million Khmer Riel, a gold necklace, a gold bracelet. 5 grams, 1 pair of platinum earrings, 3 beds, 1 glass cabinet and some other materials. Separately, the suspect who caused the incident, her husband Seng Thy, 41 years old, was arrested by the police.
Separately, on the morning of March 20, 2020, Mr. Prak Sovann led the team to visit and bring humanitarian donations of the Cambodian Red Cross, including materials and funds to the victims.
