Mr. Touch Kosal stated that the workers complained to the Arbitration Council of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, demanding four working conditions. Base plus subsistence allowance, 2nd: mental health compensation, 3rd: notice compensation and 4th: remaining annual leave.
He added that on February 20, 2020, the Arbitration Council issued an order for hotel owners to pay workers three points: First: Payment of seniority compensation before 2019 by the base wage plus secondary, Second: Notification compensation and third: Remuneration for the remaining annual leave. As for compensation for mental illness, the Arbitration Council opposes the workers' demands.
Mr. Touch Kosal said that the order of the Central Arbitration Council gave time for the second party to appeal. If there is no objection from both parties, the order becomes obligatory, and for this order, both the workers and the hotel owner do not object, which automatically becomes an obligatory order. To be implemented.
"Due to the neglect of compensation, the workers plan to continue protesting," he added. We are waiting to see the intentions of the hotel if next Monday or Tuesday there is no response, there may be another strike. Therefore, please call on the Royal Government and relevant ministries and institutions to help promote compensation to workers who are struggling, some have to deal with bank debt to feed family members.
