(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on March 19, 2020 issued a notification reminding factories, enterprises, especially factories in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags must implement 12 measures. Points to prevent and control the spread of Kovid 19 in factories. According to an announcement received by Fresh News a little earlier.
Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, told Fresh News that the reason the ministry issued the announcement was to increase the focus of factory owners on the prevention of smallpox and to strengthen the ministry's notice. Issued on January 28, 2020 on measures to prevent and control the spread of Kovid 19 in factories, as well as guidelines or rules issued by the Ministry of Health in the past.
He added that this announcement is also a response or reminder to some individuals who did not follow the Ministry's efforts to pay attention to the well-being of factory workers in the past. In fact, the Ministry has been taking action since the end of January and has been working closely with the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia and factory owners to implement preventive measures to ensure that workers in this sector do not have any external infections.
