According to a letter from Prince Sar Kheng, the discovery of 19 Kovid virus has increased dramatically and while the Vietnamese government has restricted travel, requiring isolation for a period of time. For 14 days for travelers from ASEAN countries, including Vietnamese nationals returning to Cambodia, the Ministry of Interior would like to make the following recommendations:
1: All entry into Cambodia by Vietnamese citizens and entry into Vietnam by Cambodians by land, sea and air will be temporarily suspended from 23:59 pm on March 20. 2020. This measure aims to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
2. The above measures do not apply to Vietnamese and Cambodian citizens holding diplomatic and official passports.
3. The provincial authorities bordering the Socialist Republic of Vietnam shall coordinate with the Vietnamese side to facilitate the repatriation of all Cambodian citizens who are being isolated in Vietnam, if any.
4. The governors of the provinces bordering the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and all the competent forces at the border gates must coordinate with the Vietnamese side to ensure that the transit of goods across the border can be carried out unhindered.
Authorities in the provinces bordering the Socialist Republic of Vietnam must inform the Vietnamese side of the measures and seek understanding, and continue to strengthen cooperation and joint efforts to stop the spread of Kovid 19.
