Ministry of Interior Issues Guidelines for Emergency Measures to Prevent and Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid 19 for Subordinate Units
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior has issued guidelines on emergency measures for the prevention and control of the Kovid 19 epidemic for all units under the Ministry of Interior and sub-national administrations. This is according to the instruction of the Ministry of Interior, which was received by Fresh News this morning, March 19, 2020.
The instructions of the Ministry of Interior on emergency measures for the prevention and control of the Kovid 19 epidemic include:
* First: greet each other with respect, pressure or raise your hand in the Khmer tradition to avoid shaking hands.
* Third: Provide alcohol or soap for hand washing in all units and clean the halls of the meeting room with disinfectant or soap properly and often.
* Fourth: If you have any symptoms such as: fever, runny nose, sore throat, cough, sneezing, difficulty breathing, go to the nearest health center or referral hospital for treatment.
* 5: When coughing, sneeze, cover mouth, nose with a towel, elbow or paper and throw it in the trash properly, then wash your hands with soap or alcohol.
* Sixth: When communicating with a person with symptoms such as fever, cough, sneezing, runny nose, sore throat, difficulty breathing, keep a safe distance of more than 1.5 meters will require him to wear a mask.
* Seventh: For officials who have just returned from countries with a severe epidemic of Kovid 19, they must be isolated for 14 days from the date of their return to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
* Eighth: All overseas missions must be suspended for a period from the date of receipt of this instruction, unless necessary and with the approval of the Ministry.
9th: All units under the Ministry of Interior and all sub-national administrations must regularly monitor and report on the health status of their officials. In the event of any official suspicion of Kovid syndrome, call 115 immediately.
