Regarding the inspection operation, Mr. Kong Vuthy said that his team will continue to inspect other pharmacies in the capital and provinces in the country, while some drug owners or traders take the opportunity. Niyom sells counterfeit alcohol and hand sanitizers and has no clear source of production to maximize profits without harming consumers as Cambodia spreads COVID-19.
However, Mr. Kong Vuthy also called on all Cambodians to buy items, especially alcohol and hand washing gel, with the correct label and clear source to avoid counterfeit and substandard products that cause harm. Our health when using that.
He said that 4 liters of methanol alcohol equal to 20 liters was confiscated and the General Department of Camcontrol would like to call on people not to buy any alcohol without a label and no clear source to use. Cleansing, disinfecting or preventing Covid-19 virus.
