The following is a letter from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs:
With the hosting of the 13th Asia-Europe Summit, Foreign Ministry officials and researchers have similar views on the importance of this meeting for Cambodia's hosting.
She said that the Asia-Europe Summit, which will be hosted by Cambodia in 2020, Cambodia has raised a topic called "Promoting multilateralism for the common good" in this topic. Participation to promote multilateralism, given the current political and economic environment.
She said that in the world, a small number of countries have shifted from the implementation of the policy of multilateral unification, which is moving towards unilateralism, which is causing a resurgence and affecting small countries such as Asia. Europe, made up of small nations.
She added that this is what makes it difficult to promote international law, strengthen security as well as economically and politically. In what way?
Mr. Lim Meng Hour, a representative from the Asian Eye Institute (AVI), said that the Asia-Europe Summit is a forum for meetings and discussions between the Royal Government from countries in two major regions, Europe and Asia The initiative of the meeting began in 1996 in Bangkok, Thailand, with a biennial meeting.
He added that 53 participants (countries and institutions) attended the Asia-Europe Summit, including 30 from Europe and 21 from Asia, from the ASEAN Secretariat and community representatives. Europe, too. Therefore, these 53 actors will discuss three main issues, including political, economic and socio-cultural issues.
He stressed that the Asia-Europe Summit is a big meeting and allows all members to have the opportunity to discuss and debate global challenges. The Asia-Europe Meeting is a big meeting because if you look at Europe and Asia as a region that represents up to 60 percent of the world's population, if you look at the economic size of these two regions up to 65 percent. .
He said that the Asia-Europe Summit is a forum to promote multilateral mechanisms in which all members participate in resolving all issues multilaterally, and also to provide opportunities for all states, especially small states, to have opportunities. Express views and contribute to solving the challenges that the world is facing.
