(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan has provided US $ 249,529 to two Cambodian units for the construction of a bridge in Kratie province and a road improvement project in Kampot province under a grant for a small-scale project for human security. Kusanoni).
1: Road improvement project in Wat Ang Khang Tbong commune, Banteay Meas district, Kampot province, which includes: * US $ 62,638 * Recipient unit: Kampot Provincial Department of Rural Development.
In this project, an existing old bridge will be replaced by three concrete box drains in Wat Ang Khang Tbong, Banteay Meas District, Kampot Province. The project is expected to benefit about 37,000 people in the region. We also expect that the improved road will make it easier for local people to travel to schools, hospitals and markets, and especially boost people's economic activity by improving connectivity in the region. .
2: The project to build a bridge in Khsem commune, Snoul district, Kratie province, which has: * Budget of 186,890 US dollars * The receiving unit is the Department of Rural Development of Kratie province.
In this project, a 20-meter bridge and a 9-meter box drain will be built in Khsem commune, Snuol district, Kratie province. Residents are now using wooden bridges that are prone to collapse after the old concrete drains were severely damaged by floods. The project is expected to benefit about 3,000 people in the area with safe access to schools, hospitals and markets, as well as improve the transportation of agricultural products.
