Conflict with brother, mistakenly cut off one arm in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, police force cracked down on 5 perpetrators
(Banteay Meanchey): Five assailants were arrested by Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police in connection with a case of aggravated violence by cutting off a young man, causing him to lose one arm while riding a motorcycle on the road. This incident happened on the night of March 16, 2020 in front of Huy Leng Market in Soeur Village, Soeur Commune, Mongkul Borei District.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General At Cam told Fresh News on the afternoon of March 18, 2020 that five of the seven perpetrators involved in this case were arrested by police on March 17 yesterday.
While riding on the road, the suspect suddenly cut his brother's arm, causing him to lose his arm. The victim, Det Vanlyda, 15 years old, living in Bao Lok village, Soeur commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, was immediately sent to the Japanese hospital in Mongkul Borei district.
Currently, the five perpetrators have been sent to the specialized office to build a case for further proceedings.
