To date, the teacher has received about 160 martial arts students and has given morning, evening and evening shifts for students and night shifts for civil servants because they understand that practicing bokator can lead them to good health. Far from drugs and other tricks, especially can maintain the traditional Khmer martial arts.
Many martial arts students who are training say that the training is a bit difficult because the teacher lacks the resources to buy materials such as training equipment and traditional Khmer clothes. On the other hand, some students do not respect discipline, but teachers still try to teach and transfer the knowledge that teachers have to let them know and understand how good our Khmer martial arts are.
Mr. Am Yum said that not only our Cambodian children are interested in bokator, even foreigners who have time to relax in Kampong Chhnang province also came to study with about 10 teachers. But now they have returned to their homeland, promising to take some of the martial arts they learned to train their friends to learn about traditional Khmer martial arts.
It should be reminded that in Kampong Chhnang province, Mr. Am Yum has been teaching Bokator for almost 6 years, in which he has sent students to participate in many national competitions and received gold, silver and bronze medals. Also. In addition to the national competition, the teacher also sent students to show the people, national and international tourists in Angkor Sankranti in Siem Reap every year, especially all other national festivals in Kampong Chhnang.
