Cambodians wishing to enter South Korea must meet three conditions to prevent the spread of Kovich 19
1: Restaurant and restaurant owners must publicly disseminate knowledge and advice to prevent the spread of this infectious disease to guests and staff, such as posters explaining hand washing and wearing masks. That's right.
2: Provide hand sanitizer soap and alcohol to wash hands. Handwashing and massage facilities should be set up around the restaurant, especially in areas such as entrances, toilets, checkout counters, etc. To provide hygiene services to customers and staff in its restaurants and tourist canteens.
4: Schedule regular cleaning of appliances or areas with regular contact, such as tables, handles, doors, toilets, disinfection and alcohol at least twice a day.
5: Be careful when collecting waste such as used toilet paper in the bathroom or toilet paper that is dirty due to mucus or saliva. Wearing gloves or using a dirty garbage collector is important to prevent infection. When disposing of dirty rubbish, keep the mouth of the bag close and wash your hands to prevent the spread of germs.
6: For large restaurants with a large staff should follow this guide before starting work. If employees are sick, they should be allowed to return home to prevent the spread of the disease. If someone has a serious illness, they should seek immediate medical attention.
