Minister Tram Iv Tek said that the field of information and communication technology (ICT) and digital sector is now growing and we will move towards the implementation of a digital government to promote the digital economy, the use of the Internet of Things (IoT) and the participation of technology. Which fueled the 4.0 generation industrial revolution.
"Information security is a very important issue. If we do not take ownership of it, promoting digital government and the digital economy will definitely be a challenge," he said.
In addition, the digital economy, especially e-commerce and online payments, is not yet running smoothly, which may be due to fears of cyber-attacks and hacking. E-commerce activities are still small.
Minister Tram Iv Tek added that, therefore, when we need to expand, we need to strengthen cyber security and safety in terms of technical, legal and human resources.
Meanwhile, Minister Tram Iv Tek said that countries in the region as well as globally are beginning to develop computer emergency response mechanisms (CERT / CSIRT) in almost all countries, but through this mechanism the work is still limited. Still low, just mediate to deal with cyber security incidents.
To address the challenges posed by the growing number of cybercriminals, and at the national level, the management of national ICT security needs to be expanded. Broader scope by developing relevant laws, policies and legal norms.
