The Ministry of Health Instructs Pharmacy Owners in Cambodia to Purchase Alcohol from a Well-Sourced Source While High Demand for Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has issued a notice instructing pharmacy owners and pharmacists in charge of Pharmacies in Cambodia need to buy alcohol from a well-sourced source while there is a high demand to prevent Kovid 19.
The Ministry of Health has announced that a number of pharmacies and sub-pharmacies are currently buying and selling alcohol without a clear source of substandard quality, as people are in desperate need of alcohol to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus in Cambodia. Some alcohols mix methanol with ethanol and some do not contain ethanol, only methanol. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Health.
The Ministry of Health has informed the public that the disinfectant is a mixture of ethanol with water, without the addition of other substances, especially methanol. Methanol is not used for disinfection because it has the weakest antiseptic function, but it can be toxic and even life-threatening if used improperly.
