Military forces arrest man who brutally tortured his girlfriend in Kien Svay district
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie has launched an operation to arrest a man who brutally tortured his girlfriend without cutting a finger. This incident happened on February 9, 2020 at Prek Tanop village, Kampong Svay commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
A report from the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of March 18, 2020, confirms that the suspect, who was her boyfriend, was arrested by the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces on the 15th. March 2020 at a guesthouse in Kampong Samnang commune, Takhmao city.
According to the police, the suspect, Poeun, 36, a resident of the commune, used a knife to cut the victim, his ex-girlfriend, Srey Leak, 25, a farmer, living in Prek Tanop 2 village. Kampong Svay commune, Kien Svay district, caused serious injuries, including amputation of a finger of her right hand and thumb, index finger (middle bone (skin only), right forearm, bone and right bat.
After the incident, Brigadier General Sam Tola, Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, led the direct command of the provincial and district experts to immediately arrive at the scene to rescue the victims and search for suspects. Take legal punishment.
Through careful research day and night, fearless, experienced, willing, under the direct leadership of Colonel Touch Inan and the attention of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, especially with the permission of Prosecutors from Kandal Provincial Court arrested a suspect named Poeun on March 15, 2020.
In front of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, the suspect confessed that he and the victim were ex-girlfriends who used to live together because they were too jealous of the victim (they lived apart for a while) on the day of birth. Because he wanted to live with the victim, his ex-girlfriend came to the victim's house and shouted for him to open the door, but the victim did not open the door.
