(Phnom Penh): To help prevent the spread of gonorrhea in Cambodia, the Ministry of Tourism has issued guidelines on measures to prevent the spread of gonorrhea 19 for spa-massage businesses in the country. This is according to the instruction of the Ministry of Tourism, which was received by Fresh News on the afternoon of March 18, 2020.
In the instructions of the Ministry of Tourism said that the instructions to the manager of the spa-massage business are as follows:
* First, managers must disseminate knowledge and advice to prevent the spread of the disease to guests and staff, such as posters explaining how to wash their hands and wear masks properly.
* Third: Raise awareness among service staff and sanitation staff about the risks and vulnerabilities of this new virus, highlighting the importance of self-protection, such as wearing masks and gloves while working. Managers should support hygienic care for employees to protect themselves, such as hand washing before or after work, and be prepared for any material that is frequently touched.
* Fourth: Proper waste and water management. Be careful when collecting trash, such as used towels or toilet paper that is contaminated by guest sneezes or saliva. Prevents the formation of viruses.
* Fifth: The trader must check the staff temperature before starting work. If employees are sick or show a fever, they need to be allowed to return home to prevent the spread of the disease. If someone is seriously ill, allow them to go to the hospital for emergency treatment.
Instructions for Spa-Massage staff are as follows:
* First: Protect yourself from infection by observing the symptoms of guests with fever, cough, sore throat, nasal congestion or difficulty breathing. If guests have these symptoms, you should refer them to the masseuse to go to the hospital for emergency treatment and tell their travel history.
* Second: Be careful in dealing with guests during work. Employees should wear a mask at all times when near guests, wash their hands frequently with soap and water and alcohol. Do not touch your eyes, nose, or hands when you are not feeling well.
* Third: Do not share personal items with others, such as glasses, straws, spoons, hand towels and towels.
