(Kampong Cham): On the morning of March 18, 2020, Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, led the forces of the Provincial Police Commission to pay their respects to the late Commander-in-Chief. Narin, ID 48293, Order Officer of Kampong Cham City Police Inspectorate.
Colonel Keo Narin passed away on March 17, 2020 at the age of 52 (with severe burns all over his body in case of house fire) on March 12, 2020. At present, the family organizes a traditional ceremony at the mortuary in Svay Chrum village, Koh Mit commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province, following the Buddhist tradition.
At the same time, Major General Em Kosal brought 3 million Riels, 1 bag of rice, 2 boxes of orange juice, 2 cases of pure water and 2 boxes of noodles, as a gift from General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police. Presented to the family of the corpse to arrange the ceremony according to the Buddhist tradition and donated some money to another family who suffered from a house fire at the same time as the fire of the house of Mr. Keo Narin.
