(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, strongly supported the Vietnam Industrial Alliance, which has tens of thousands of hectares of rubber plantations in Cambodia, recruiting tens of thousands of workers to work on rubber plantations. Each is guaranteed a decent salary, accommodation and some support services.
The agreement was reached during a meeting with a Vietnamese delegation led by Tycoon Leng Rithy, President of the Vietnam Rubber Plantation Association in Cambodia, accompanied by the Vietnamese Businessmen's Club in Cambodia, the Vietnam Agricultural Bank (AGRI Bank), and the Vietnamese Embassy in Cambodia. THADI Vietnam this morning, March 18, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
On that occasion, Mr. Oknha Leng Rithy said that currently the Thai Rubber Industry Coalition and the Vietnamese Rubber Plantation Company in Cambodia, which are partners with more than 20,000 hectares of rubber plantations in Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri and Kratie provinces, are in need of labor. By 2020-2021, there will be more than 150,000 people, and for urgent work, the company needs about 9,000 workers immediately.
He said that currently those who work in the rubber plantations receive a minimum wage of 800,000 riels for rubber planters can earn from 1 million to 1.5 million riels, and workers have a decent place to stay without having to pay for water. And electricity bills.
The Minister was very pleased with the Vietnamese side's suggestion and suggested that the company cooperate with the National Employment Agency (NEA) to visit and recruit local workers or those who have lost their jobs. Due to the inability of its establishment to operate due to Kovid-19 disease.
The minister said that Cambodia currently has a total workforce of 10 million, of which 4 million are in the agricultural sector, 1.5 million in industry and handicrafts, and 2.4 million in the informal economy. Overseas, there are more than 1.2 million people and 500,000 civil servants, these are the sources where we can mobilize the labor force according to the needs of the sector.
The Minister requested the association to cooperate with the National Employment Agency (NEA), which has 12 provincial employment centers, as well as mobile employment centers, to go directly to the local level in the provinces in collaboration with Provincial authorities invite people to register immediately.
