According to the instruction of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which was received by Fresh News this morning, March 18, 2020, in order to prevent Covid 19 disease, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport would like to introduce to all levels Leaders and staff under all subordinates, please cooperate to implement a number of measures, such as:
* First, all civil servants must be careful to keep clean by washing their hands with soap or alcohol regularly, disinfected several times and must wear a mask regularly if necessary.
* Second, the administrative officer who works directly to receive documents or traffic officer, documents related to external units must wear a mask regularly, must wear protective gloves, and must wash their hands regularly with soap or alcohol before and After holding the document.
* Third: All entry and exit documents must be disinfected, especially the documents handed over to each entry and exit of the Office of Administrative Documents.
* Fourth: All machines, tools, means of daily use that are used together in public places that have a lot of impact, such as elevators, handrails, stairs, bathrooms, meeting rooms, office equipment such as tables, chairs, etc. must be washed or wiped. Clean with alcohol or disinfectant regularly.
* Fifth: Change the attitude from shaking hands to salutation and maintain a reasonable distance (within 1.5 meters to 2 meters) during communication with people from behind and colleagues.
* Sixth: Minimize the number of members attending the meeting, as a meeting can only be attended by the relevant stakeholders, and the meeting seats should be kept separate for each official.
* Seventh: Encourage all units under the Ministry by using the telegram communication system to send certain types of documents and correspondence daily to avoid face-to-face encounters.
* Eighth: Security agents must check the temperature (not more than 37.2 degrees) for officers who come to work daily or guests who have duties and work relations at the entrance. Leaders and civil servants who measure their temperature above 37.2 degrees must be allowed to take time off work and will have to go to the hospital immediately for a personal checkup in a responsible manner.
