Kandal Provincial Administration issues notice on 5 cruise ships after Vietnam does not allow them to dock
(Kandal): The Kandal Provincial Administration has issued a notice on five cruise ships that Vietnam is not allowed to dock at this time to the Phnom Penh International Port, leaving the port on March 17. 2020.
Kandal Provincial Hall's announcement, obtained by Fresh News on March 18, 2020, confirms that five Cambodian cruise ships carrying a total of 200 tourists and crew were allowed to leave the port. Samnakom towards Phnom Penh International Port after Chattalysak officers checked for COVID-19 virus for those on board.
It should be noted that the four Cambodian cruise ships that Vietnam did not allow to dock returned to Kham Samnor Port in Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province on the evening and night of March 16, 2020. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, confirmed that in addition to the four cruise ships returning from Vietnam, there is currently a cruise ship docked there.
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that out of the five cruise ships that will be docked at the port (one is already docked), three ships have tourists. The other two ships, only the crew and crew were not tourists. The Minister of Public Works and Transport said that the five ships were carrying a total of 200 people, including 77 tourists, 123 staff and crew.
It should be noted that the return of four tourists to the pot came after Vietnam did not allow guests to park. Phan Soben, owner of a cruise ship, described on his Facebook page on March 15 that four of his Cambodian-registered vessels carrying passengers from Siem Reap to Vietnam were stranded in the middle of a river in Vietnam. Because Vietnamese authorities do not allow ships to carry guests.
The fact that Vietnam does not allow this will cause the ship to suffer from a shortage of water, fuel and food on board. After Vietnam did not allow the dock, Mr. Phan Soben asked Samdech Techo to intervene in this matter. After receiving a request from the ship owner, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia immediately ordered Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to intervene to solve this problem. .
Both Phan Soben, the ship owner, as well as the crew on board were very happy after receiving the intervention of the head of government for them to return to the country.
