1: For Cambodian fixed mobile and telecommunication service providers:
* Check and ensure that all fixed mobile phone users can make free calls to 115 anytime, anywhere with mobile service, with or without account balance.
* Continue to monitor the traffic of the call to 115 and the connection to the Ministry of Health Emergency Response. In the event of an increase in usage traffic of up to 70% of the Trunk capacity for connection number 115, the operator must take immediate action to expand the connection capacity to avoid any interruption or technical disruption of service.
Assign responsible focal points to prepare for technical support and coordination, especially for Operation 115 with the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia and Telecom Cambodia.
2: For mobile and internet service providers must:
* Inspect and increase the capacity of the power bank (Power Bank) and install generators and solar systems at each service station and network management center as an additional source of power supply to ensure the efficiency and sustainability of service.
