Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Introduces 8 Important Measures to Fight Drugs
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, outlined eight key measures for the National Authority for Combating Drugs, Ministries, Institutions, Secretariat of the Campaign, Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committee and all relevant departments. All must pay attention to the organization and implementation of work by sector and expertise.
Measures issued by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng at the meeting to review the results of drug control work in 2019 and set the work direction for 2020 and close the meeting to review the results of the implementation of the plan to fight against illegal drugs on March 17. This 2020 includes:
* First, all ministries and institutions that are members of the National Authority for Combating Drugs must continue to develop mechanisms and strengthen mechanisms within ministries and institutions and continue to pay attention to the implementation of their roles and responsibilities set out in the five-year national plan on combating drugs. Anti-Drug Implementation of the Anti-Drug Action Plan 2020 set by the Conference and implement the action plan of the 5th Anti-Drug Campaign.
* Second, the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, the Anti-Drug Committee of the Ministry of Interior and the Committee for the Implementation of the Safe Village, Commune and Sangkat Policy must jointly establish a specific mechanism to implement the Village, Sangkat and Sangkat Policy. No drugs nationwide. This organization must have specific documents and reports on the organization and operation in each capital-province.
* Third: The General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and the Secretariat of the Anti-Drug Campaign of the Ministry of Interior must continue to further strengthen their roles and responsibilities in order to facilitate, monitor and promote the implementation of the anti-drug campaign. The fifth law to be more effective.
* Fourth, the National Committee for Drug Treatment and Rehabilitation must pay more attention to strengthening the quality, efficiency and reliability of services in the treatment, rehabilitation and integration of drug addicts.
* Sixth, all relevant units must thoroughly strengthen professional ethics to ensure that their law enforcement officers are not really involved or behind criminal activities by inspiring a social movement to promote the implementation of the direction. Three slogans should be reported strictly: do not be involved, do not intervene, do not make exceptions, and must provide information related to drug offenses to the competent authorities and the people widely.
8th: With the announcement to continue the implementation of the 5th anti-drug campaign in 2020, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng would like to support and appreciate the campaign of joint operation of the Greater Mekong Subregion. The Mekong, dubbed Operation Fifteen Eleven, was unveiled at the 1993 K-16 Ministerial Meeting in Bangkok on November 15, 2019.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng instructed all relevant ministries, institutions and units, especially law enforcement units to pay attention to participate effectively.
