Experts on Khmer Civilization: Khmer Tradition, World Health Care
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, said that today, in terms of the global virus Covid-19, which is invading the world and the leaders, heads of state, heads of major countries - Small children around the world have changed the tradition of shaking hands or shaking hands to raise their hands in a formal greeting or salute to avoid infection.
It means that "Khmer worship is becoming a civilization that has spread all over the world." Because this salutation tradition is Khmer, we are one of the oldest races in Southeast Asia, have a culture, civilization, traditions, good traditions from the beginning.
In fact, in the Khmer tradition of worship, we see from the Funan period at Kampong Po pagoda, the image of the goddess made of burnt clay, wearing short skirts with many folds, in the posture of sitting on his knees and holding both hands to the chest, soft, gentle and brave as evidence .
If so, the Khmer salutation tradition is an act of "respect" that embodies the essence of gratitude, gratitude, loyalty, combined with the deepest and deepest affectionate affection. Because in Khmer philosophy, it is popular to value what is mentally internal, called "ideology", which is different from white people is to show "external image".
Because the value of Khmer worship is to send a signal to express the spirit, express emotions or dedication without touching each other. And through this salutation gesture, we can know the depth of the other party's feelings or emotions. Meaning that "Khmer people use a lot of spirit."
In conclusion, Mr. Rath Sandab stated that if so, in the tradition of Khmer worship, we can know the depth of heart. In contrast, Western cultures, or whites, value rights by shaking hands or touching. This means that only when touching each other can the depth of the other party's feelings or emotions be estimated.
If so, we, the Cambodian people, must bring more to this tradition of salutation to tell the world the beautiful national identity of our Cambodians.
