The urging of senior officials of the Ministry of National Defense was made on the occasion of his participation in presiding over the inauguration of the gates, fences and achievements in Wat Ti Chotivanaram called Wat Memol on the morning of March 15, 2020 in Memol Village, Mes Prachan District. Pea, Prey Veng province.
He added that the local authorities as well as the national working group to help Mes Prachan commune must participate in making the people in this commune achieve their desires and achieve their dreams.
It should be noted that the ceremony of crossing the gates, fences and achievements in Wat Ti Chotivanaram called Wat Memol in Memol village, Mes Prachan commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province will last for 3 days, from March 14 to 16, 2020. Ministry of Education postpones annual meeting due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued a notification on March 16, 2020, confirming the postponement of the meeting to review the evaluation of the results of education, youth and sports 2018-2019 and the direction for the 2019 academic year. -2020.
The Ministry of Education claims that the decision to postpone is to help prevent and control the spread of Kovid 19 virus. The ministry stated that the conference was scheduled to be held on March 23-25, 2020, but was temporarily suspended until further notice.
According to the report, all passengers on domestic and international flights to and from Vietnam must wear the same mask both on and off the airport.
So far, Vietnam has had 57 cases of COVID-19, including 20 foreigners, according to the Ministry of Health. The Southeast Asian nation also has 102 suspected cases, while nearly 300,000 people are being isolated for medical check-ups.
Kratie Provincial Administration Holds a Meeting to Summarize Work Results for 2019 and Work Orientation for 2020
(Kratie): On the morning of March 16, 2020, Kratie Provincial Administration organized the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results for 2019 and work direction for 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Hoeur Siyem, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Council and Mr. Vathon Governor Kratie province, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. Provincial Councilors, provincial governors, leaders of departments around the province and more than 500 relevant officials.
Mr. Wathon also stated that the meeting will be divided into discussion groups on the main topics that the working group has already prepared for the members of the conference, so all members should work hard. A spirit to actively participate in discussions on achievements, challenges and solutions, as well as to provide good experiences for the implementation of the work direction in 2020 to be more effective.
Mr. Wathon also confirmed the COVID-19 virus, we must not panic and believe the rumors, we must all work together to prevent the spread of the disease by cleaning the body, especially washing. Wash your hands often with soap or alcohol before eating or touching your nose or mouth.
