(Phnom Penh): The Rural Development and Agriculture Bank, which recently transformed from a specialized bank into a commercial bank, on March 16, 2020, announced the process of implementing a special grant of $ 50 million of the Royal Government to support the sector. Agricultural, agro-industrial and agricultural processing to enable enterprises in these sectors to survive during the Covid-19 crisis and the suspension of parts of the EBA system.
The $ 50 million loan package is open to enterprises in the agro-processing, agro-industrial and agricultural sectors with a credit facility of up to $ 300,000 for five years at low interest rates.
Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, said at a press conference that the $ 50 million special financing package is expected to help about 500 enterprises in Cambodia to strengthen their capacity and meet quality standards.
He said that the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has a policy to provide loans, especially to small and medium enterprises involved in the agricultural sector. He said that in order to be able to borrow this loan, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has set some conditions for small and medium enterprises, including:
* Take this package to strengthen the work between 5 to 10 places in each enterprise. * The interest rate offered is a low interest rate of 6% per annum for working capital and 6.5% for working capital that can be provided to small and medium enterprise owners working in the agricultural sector. * For collateral, the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank still accepts, offering up to 80% of the value of the debt.
The Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture also has the flexibility to provide collateral, not only real estate, but also factories, materials and machinery can provide collateral. The Bank will train those enterprises to prepare a business plan, clear financial statements in collaboration with the Bank's team.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: The army must understand the role, duties, army, discipline, order and other military knowledge
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army, met with newly recruited soldiers this morning, March 16, 2020. Kork 2020 is training in the Army Training Center and at the 3rd Military Academy, 3rd Military Zone, Kampong Speu Province.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet congratulated the newly recruited soldiers to join the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) through a thorough screening and selection process from a large number of candidates who have volunteered to apply. And who are undergoing training in the Army Training Center and at the 3rd Military Academy, the 3rd Military Region to become a national army, ready to serve the people and protect the peace.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet emphasized that volunteering for the army is not just about changing into a uniform, as an army, it is about understanding the roles and responsibilities of the army, discipline, order and military knowledge. Go through proper and rigorous training.
On the other hand, this training course is also an important basis for new soldiers to be able to go out and perform their duties in the units, as well as for them to grasp the roles and responsibilities from the military level before they can gain more knowledge. From practical work or continue to learn, which in the future can also become a capable officer.
Mr. HUN Manet sent all trainees to pay attention to study, strive to respect discipline, listen to the teachings of the military and strive to grow to each other to become good soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for their own future and the future of the army and also to strengthen The spirit of unity, building and maintaining friendships to the next day before being assigned to work in units after completing the training.
