Local suppliers call on Cambodians to turn to local safety products to support business and health
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Vutha, Deputy Director of Angkor Gap, a local supplier of safe agricultural products, called on Cambodians to support and use local safety products to support local businesses and to protect their own safety.
According to Mr. Sun Vutha on March 15, 2020, he said that Angkor Gap wants to be the success of all Cambodian farmers who strive to produce carefully selected quality and safety for consumers.
He added that therefore, let all people turn to support Khmer products and seek to buy quality and safe products such as Angkor Gap products that can ensure good health.
He continued, "I hope that the safety products of Angkor Gap will attract the attention of customers as well as the entire Cambodian people, because this product of Angkor Gap is made to a standard with good quality, safety and reasonable price, especially as a product." Locally produced by Khmer children.
He stated that Angkor Gap's products include: safe pork, safe chicken, some processed agricultural products, especially other safe seasonal fruits and vegetables.
He added that the products of Angkor Gap are the products of real Cambodian farmers, grown and raised locally and under the provision of techniques and consulting in accordance with good agricultural standards and hygienic production rules from breeding. Cultivation, care, harvesting, slaughtering, processing, packaging and delivery to consumers.
He stated that Angkor Gap currently has 8 distribution branches and 8 locations and main markets in Phnom Penh.
Tbong Khmum Governor Inaugurates a Modern Private Hospital in Suong City to Meet Health Care Needs
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, said that "the private sector has contributed a lot to facilitate and supplement to provide health services to people in the treatment of diseases."
On the occasion, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan and Ms. Meng Van Danin presided over the inauguration of the "Tep Nimmith" Maternity and Maternity Hospital, owned by Dr. Chhorn Mony and Ms. Sok Thida, located in Sangkat Suong, Suong City, a leading private hospital in Tbong Khmum province has standard rooms, comfortable, state-of-the-art equipment and a team of doctors with more than 20 years of experience waiting for examination and treatment 24 hours a day.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan said that the hospital has been open for 22 years and has examined and treated many people who have recovered. These are all contributions from the government hospital with the Royal Government of Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who liberated the people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, liberated them from suffering, liberated them from war, as well as examined and treated people from various diseases.
In addition, the provincial governor also mentioned measures and called on people to be hygienic, prevent and protect themselves from the Covid-19 virus that is spreading around the world, especially in Cambodia. There have been a series of infections in recent times.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan expressed his pleasure that this private hospital has really contributed a lot to the treatment of people with various serious diseases using the latest equipment and professional doctors who are good partners. And replenish effectively after public hospitalization.
Dr. Chhorn Mony, Advisor to Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Deputy Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department and Director of Tep Nimmith Maternity and Maternity Hospital, said that the hospital has been operating for 22 years. Today, the new building was officially inaugurated, equipped with the latest equipment, with a team of highly experienced doctors from France waiting for examination and treatment 24 hours a day.
He added that there are 25 staff members, including 6 specialists, 4 doctors and nurses, 1 pharmacist, 15 nurses and midwives, 40 rooms, operating room, delivery room, etc. Painless childbirth means we take painkillers.
Dr. Chhorn Mony emphasizes that the most special things include:
He added that all of the above machines have a team of doctors who have graduated from France to examine, translate and diagnose diseases.
Also available are pediatric and geriatric services, general surgery and orthopedic surgery, antenatal and obstetrics, general health package services, ear, nose and throat examination by endoscope, heart rate measurement, vaccination. For all genders, there is an ambulance 24 hours a day.
A concrete road damaged by landslide in Roka Kong I commune, Kandal province was repaired by the Ministry of Water Resources
(Kandal): A concrete road in Prek Pdao village, Roka Kong I commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, which was damaged by river bank collapse this morning, March 16, 2020, was attacked by Mr. Mao Hak, Deputy Chief of Tonle Sap National Authority. Of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, with the guidance of Mr. Vongsey Vichet, the Central Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party and the Roka Kong I Commune Rehabilitation Team led the team to repair and upgrade.
