Four Cambodian cruise ships will arrive at Kham Samnor this evening after Vietnam does not allow them to dock
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the four cruise ships will not be allowed to enter the shore when they arrive, but will be left about two kilometers from the shore.
In addition to the four cruise ships returning from Vietnam, there is currently a cruise ship docked at Kham Samnor. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol.
The Minister of Public Works and Transport said the five ships were carrying a total of 200 people, including 77 tourists, 123 crew members and crew.
It should be noted that the return of four tourists to the pot came after Vietnam did not allow guests to park.
Phan Soben, owner of a cruise ship, described on his Facebook page on March 15 that four of his Cambodian-registered vessels carrying passengers from Siem Reap to Vietnam were stranded in the middle of a river in Vietnam. Because Vietnamese authorities do not allow ships to carry guests.
The fact that Vietnam does not allow this will cause the ship to suffer from a shortage of water, fuel and food on board. After Vietnam did not allow the dock, Mr. Phan Soben also asked Samdech Techo to intervene on this issue.
After receiving the request, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, immediately ordered Senior Minister Sun Chanthol to intervene to solve this problem.
Both Mr. Phan Soben as well as the crew on the ship were very happy after receiving the intervention of the head of the Royal Government for them to return to the country.
Ministry of Land Management and General Department of Taxation are studying together to pay stamp duty at the OWSO to save time (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction is discussing together with General Department of Taxation To be stamped when transferring property ownership at the OWSO to facilitate people saving time and reducing informal expenses.
This is according to Mr. Seng Lot, Spokesman of the Ministry of Land Management, this morning, March 16, 2020, in the press conference on "Progress and further direction of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction" organized by the unit. Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia. The conference was held at the Assembly Hall of the Council of Ministers.
Mr. Seng Lot's remarks related to the simplification of tax payment procedures at the OWSO by creating a room for officials of the General Department of Taxation after raising concerns about the difficulty of paying taxes. They have to pay the tax in person at the General Department of Taxation, while other administrative documents have to be filled in at the OWSO.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Land Management claimed that the ministry had discussed the matter three times in the past and had informed the General Department of Taxation to find out if there were enough tax officials to submit the tax. At the one-stop shop at the sub-national administration?
"In this regard, the tax authorities are considering this and I believe that soon we will receive a positive response from the tax authorities to work together to make this public service faster and better," he said. "Before people can come and collect taxes and pay through the banking system."
The senior official of the Ministry of Land Management expressed his belief that this case would be possible due to the current technological advancement.
(Kandal): During the two-day campaign to enforce traffic laws in Takhmao City, the provincial police fined 32 vehicles illegally and fined nearly 12 million riels, while some cars belonged to Mr. Thom, but by following Will the law and obey the orders of Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner.
Chheng Sam Oeun, director of the Land Traffic Office of Kandal Provincial Police, told Fresh News reporters in Kandal province that traffic police will start tightening fines for traffic offenses in order to reduce daily traffic accidents. This is especially in accordance with the regulations of the Ministry of Interior.
The Land Traffic Police Force of Kandal Provincial Police has been enforcing the Road Traffic Law since March 13 on the main national roads around Phnom Penh and Takhmao City and fined one hundred illegal vehicles. Percentage. The operation was ordered by Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, and led by Mr. Chheng Sam Oeun, Mr. Ok Sophea and Mr. Selada.
Mr. Chheng Sam Oeun said that in case of finding illegal vehicles, the authorities will bring the cars and drivers who violate the law to work one hundred percent fine at the Office of Road Traffic in accordance with the law.
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, stated that Buddhism is the state religion that has contributed greatly to the maintenance of peace and social stability, while Buddhism is also a major foundation of the barn of knowledge and strong human resources. Of Cambodia, we too.
The Governor of Kandal Province said this at a ceremony to receive humanitarian donations from Samdech Preah Udom Mony Chea Sam Ang, Chief of Kandal Province and Chief of Wat Sovanvary, also known as Wat Prek Taten, in Prek Taten Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province on the afternoon of March 15, 2020.
Mr. Kong Sophoan expressed his gratitude to the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kandal Province as many achievements appeared in the field of Buddhism, especially in the pagodas, and the province also saw a lot of progress. There are plans to further support Buddhism and many other achievements.
For Samdech Preah Mony Chea Sam Ang, the priest expressed his support for the humanitarian work of the Cambodian Red Cross to help the poor and people affected by disasters in Kandal province. Japan invites Cambodia to attend 4th APWS Forum
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan has invited the Royal Government of Cambodia to attend the 4th Asia-Pacific Water Environment Forum to be held in Japan in October 2020. This is according to the result of the meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, with Mr. ISHIKAWA Hiroshi, Assistant Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, on the morning of March 16, 2020 at the Ministry.
Speaking to the media after the meeting, Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, said that according to the Assistant Foreign Minister of Japan, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia will attend the 4th APWS Forum. In addition, Japan will host a Foreign Ministers' Meeting, and Japan has even invited Prak Sokhon to attend. Mr. Prak Sokhon replied that he would attend the meeting at the invitation of Japan.
Mr. Koy Kuong stated: "His Excellency also mentioned that Japan will organize an Asia-Pacific Forum on Water Environment in October this year, in which the Prime Minister is scheduled to attend and Japan will organize Foreign ministers to meet in November His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister also replied that he would attend.
The Asia-Pacific Water Environment Forum will be held in October 2020 in Kumatomo, Japan. The forum will be attended by high-level delegates, including government leaders and government representatives and leaders, as well as representatives from international organizations in the Asia-Pacific region, where issues related to water will be discussed.
The fourth edition of APWS will also share with the world on Kumatomo's long-term efforts to conserve groundwater, as well as its efforts to recover from the 2016 Kumamoto earthquake. The third APWS in 2017 was held in Myanmar and also adopted the Yangon Declaration to set the direction of sustainable development with a water perspective.
Japanese man sentenced to death for stabbing to death 19 and injuring many more in 2016
Yokohama: A Japanese man has been sentenced to death for the murder of 19 people with intellectual disabilities in a knife attack in 2016, one of the worst massacres for the nation. Japan after World War II. This is according to a quote from Reuters on Monday afternoon, March 16, 2020.
It is noteworthy that this heinous murder has caused a great deal of consternation throughout the Japanese community, where such crimes are extremely rare due to the strict laws governing the use of weapons. The crime also sparked a renewed debate about the need for change in Japanese society, where people with disabilities continue to suffer stigma, discrimination and shame.
