(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, requested all unions to participate in preventing illegal acts or incitement activities to demand something that is illegal.
The Minister made the remarks on the occasion of allowing Mr. Ly Veng, President of the Cambodian Trade Union Confederation, and his colleagues from five other trade unions to pay a courtesy call and accept recommendations to further strengthen their work in providing Protect and promote workers' rights this morning, March 16, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
During the meeting, Mr. Ly Veng informed the Minister about the past efforts of the Cambodian Trade Union Confederation, which has contributed to supporting the right policy of the Royal Government, which has made the country continue to grow in all areas of workers. Get job opportunities, better wages, protect rights and get many benefits, especially access to social protection.
The Minister recommended that the Union of Trade Unions continue to engage in more active activities to ensure that the implementation of policies as well as new measures of the Royal Government to achieve success to ensure employment for factory workers can still Continuing production, business, workers' rights and benefits are still guaranteed.
The Minister requested that the union be involved in preventing illegal acts or incitement activities to demand something illegal, which leads to loss of workers, factory owners and, in general, to the country. Nation at once.
Must work together for the benefit of the nation, because if the factory can not operate, and not to mention the union has the right to demand this, then the union itself will end its career.
He also reminded the trade unions to support and implement the Royal Government's measures to prevent and prevent the spread of the global Kovid-19 pandemic.
The Cambodian Trade Union Confederation is committed to implementing all the good recommendations to ensure that the practice of the profession as a union can play a better role in protecting the rights and interests of workers involved in the factory owners. Profit as well as participate in the development of the nation.
It should be noted that the Khmer Labor Union has 5 member union federations and a total of 102 local unions, with a total of 23,322 workers.
This afternoon, the court will begin the case of the gunman who shot a woman with a broken thigh in the "Lux Sary" club.
The criminal case was brought to trial after the court repeatedly announced it.
It is remembered that at dawn on May 28, 2019, a shooting occurred in a nightclub with the brand "Lux Sary" located at 53, Street 214, Village 5, Sangkat Boeung Reang, Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh, caused by the accused Vin Sokrpanha opened fire on the victim, Nim Lina, female, 29 years old, causing a broken thigh.
It should be noted that Ms. Ser Vanny, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, has decided to charge Win Sok Panha with attempted murder under Articles 27 and 199 of the Penal Code. Then, Mr. Than Leng, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued a temporary detention order for the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison (PJ) on the afternoon of May 31, 2019.
