APSARA Authority is studying to repair the Takeo gate of Angkor Thom
(Siem Reap): The Takeo Gate is one of the five gates of Angkor Thom, located west of Bayon Temple. Due to the age of the war, the lack of maintenance and the growth of the trees caused many statues, giants and angels to collapse and also damaged the structure of most of the gates, especially the four elephants. Which requires repair to rescue and preserve.
Ms. Meng Sovanlylin, Architect of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology and Supervisor of the Gate Repair Site, said that currently there are architectural experts, design team, stone finder and scaffolding team and scaffolding team working on the design. Inside the gate, find the stone fragments of the gate, the elephant, the deity, and the receipt.
The archeological team plans to conduct archaeological excavations to find more fragments of stone, as well as to study the foundation structure of the gate and the railing when the excavation of the topsoil is completed.
This work has been underway since December 2019, and the project will take about two years to implement.
She added that the Takao gate is at high risk in the body of the gate at the point of the Elephant God because the weight from the top of the gate falls under the four elephants. Therefore, the first phase of repairs required the repair and reinforcement of the elephant to support the structure of the gate. The second phase will repair the body of the gate, and the third phase will study and strengthen the hill around the gate.
Ms. Ly Lin also stated that in the past three months, the team has installed about 60% of the internal scaffolding to help support the structure of the gate when moving the stone to be repaired.
In addition, the four scattered stones are divided into 4 areas according to each direction. The team also tried to assemble the giant stone receipts when they found the body parts and the giant hand box when searching for the stones.
As a follow-up work, the team will also conduct archeological excavations to study the foundations of the handrails and re-compact the foundations, and then study the paths that cross the water-carrying slope to correct the topography and level the soil. With the foundation of giant receipts and angels on both sides prevent erosion.
