70th Brigade successfully closes third generation car driving and repair training course
(Phnom Penh): The Closing Ceremony of the 3rd Generation Driving and Repairing Training Course with 63 trainees of the 70th Brigade who received training on driving and car repairing skills was completed on the morning of March 16th. In 2020, he will also receive a certificate of education.
The handover ceremony took place at the 70th Brigade Command, presided over by Major General Kong Vannarith, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Technical Equipment, Ministry of National Defense, and was attended by the Deputy Commander of the 70th Brigade and officers. Deputy and about 300 soldiers.
The purpose of this course is to increase knowledge in the use and maintenance of vehicles in accordance with the correct and technical standards, especially to be able to deal with various obstacles in a timely manner, minor damage while performing the task of ensuring all haulage. Requirements.
At the same time, the relationship with development partners has grown significantly, with the support of the technical sector in the form of budgets, technical vehicles, trailers, trailers, machinery and other spare parts. Contribute to the technical development of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for continuous development.
Lt. Gen. Kong Vannarith also advised to drive carefully, consider the safety of those in the car and check the safety of vehicles before departure.
Please be informed that this training course on driving and repairing vehicles has helped to build military resources to take turns to play an important role in accomplishing the task of mobile transport and operation of the brigade. Ministry of Land Management and Administration of Phnom Penh Holds a Dissemination Course on Construction Law to Authorities and Sub-National Authorities to Improve the Efficiency of Public Delivery
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, and more than 300 officials at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. KHOURN Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, stated that the dissemination of the construction law to the competent authorities and professional officials of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration was held in order to increase the understanding of the construction law as stated in the construction law to improve. The effectiveness of providing public services to our officials to provide better services to the people.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also mentioned that in the construction sector in Phnom Penh, as of 2019, we have 237 Boreys and flats, 1,247 four-storey buildings and 634 guesthouses, 534 five-star hotels. 4 260 luxury hotel locations and received 1030 new construction projects with an estimated investment of about 3.4 billion US dollars.
He added that along with this growth, Phnom Penh also has many challenges, especially in the construction sector, because the more construction, the larger the building, the higher the building, which makes it more complicated for us to pay attention to strengthen the mechanism. Manage all construction processes and construction sites properly according to the quality standards of construction techniques to ensure the strength, aesthetics, quality of construction and to avoid accidents at work.
Mr. Chea Sophara said that with the efforts of the authorities and the competent forces, Phnom Penh has developed and has better security.
Mr. Chea Sophara said that the construction law that has been disseminated has 22 chapters and 111 articles, and the purpose of creating this dissemination includes:
* First, want all authorities and officials to know the principles and important rules to ensure proper implementation, unanimously fulfill their competent responsibilities responsibly. * Second: Promoting the promotion of the code. Professional ethics of companies working in the construction sector * Third: Increase efficiency in managing the construction sector by increasing the trust of investors and customers in all sectors.
He continued, "We have already trained on this work in some provinces, the capital, including Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Phnom Penh, while the province and the capital has a lot of construction, and we have already advertised, such as in Kampong Speu. Kampong Cham, Kep and Tbong Khmum provinces.
He also stated that in the past in Banteay Meanchey and Sihanoukville, there are about 75% illegal construction, now we have the law. Therefore, in order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of the construction law, he asked all the competent authorities not to allow the construction. The law is already in place, and the perpetrators will be punished more. UK Continues $ 4.3 Million to End Second Global Mine Action Program in Cambodia
