General Vong Pisen announces the transfer of duties to appoint new senior officers under the General Command
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 16, 2020, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presided over the handover ceremony of senior officers under the General Command.
Pursuant to the Royal Government's sub-decree, the announcement of the Ministry of National Defense and the decision of the Commander-in-Chief to transfer the duties of 3 officers to the position of Deputy Chief of Joint Staff and to appoint 4 new officers, including: Chief of Staff of the Commander-in-Chief Chief of Inspectorate, Chief of Staff of the Air Force and Chief of Joint Secretariat.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen considered that the appointment and change of officers was a normal task to adjust the duties and in accordance with the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
General Vong Pisen expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the transferred officers who have worked hard in the past to fulfill their responsibilities responsibly.
The Commander-in-Chief also instructed the newly-appointed officers to be loyal to the nation, the Royal Government and strictly implement the laws, statutes, general rules of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the regulations of the leadership, and strengthen internal unity and With relevant institutions for work efficiency.
Road cleaning truck of Khmer Breweries Company in Battambang for the 3rd time
(Phnom Penh): The road cleaning truck of Khmer Breweries Company, which is carrying out road cleaning mission all over the country, has arrived in Battambang province and is cleaning the roads in this province from March 7 to 20.
This is the third time that Khmer Breweries' road cleaning truck has fulfilled its mission in Battambang province to contribute to the beautification of Battambang province.
A representative of the Battambang Provincial Administration confirmed that the people in this province applauded the presence of the road cleaning truck of Khmer Breweries Company, which cleaned the road in this province.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, said that the work of road cleaning vehicles in Battambang is very valuable and has received a lot of support from people living in this province. This road cleaning truck keeps the streets in the province clean and hygienic.
It should be noted that there are 4 road cleaning vehicles of Khmer Breweries Company, 2 of which are on missions in Phnom Penh and 2 of which are on mobile missions in 24 provinces.
