The order from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia to intervene on the four ships came after the ship owner requested directly to Samdech Techo Prime Minister through his Facebook page.
Phan Soben, owner of a cruise ship, wrote on his Facebook page on March 15 that four of his Cambodian-registered vessels carrying passengers from Siem Reap to Vietnam were stranded in the middle of the river. In Vietnam, because Vietnamese authorities do not allow ships to carry guests.
Mr. Soben said that there were a total of 90 crew members and more than 60 multi-ethnic guests on board. The fact that Vietnam does not allow this will cause the ship to suffer from a shortage of water, fuel and food on board.
Mr. Phan Soben asked Samdech Techo to intervene to pave the way for the four ships to return to Cambodia.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that of the four ships, three were carrying tourists, mostly from European countries, and the other was not carrying tourists, only the crew.
The minister confirmed that so far the ship as well as the Ministry is coordinating to dock in Vietnam. However, if Vietnam still does not allow it, the Royal Government will allow the four ships to return, having to stop at Kham Samnor to check their health first.
In case the tourists on the ship do not have any health problems, they will be transported to Phnom Penh.
