The Royal Government-Private Sector Forum is held once a year by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a dialogue mechanism led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and with the participation of ministers from all ministries, institutions, governors in all capitals. Provinces representing the private sector in all fields, the Ambassador to Cambodia and representatives of some international institutions.
Royal Government Forum - The private sector provides an opportunity for the private sector to raise challenges and suggestions to the Royal Government to review and take appropriate action to resolve, and all decisions in this forum are considered by the Council of Ministers.
The 13th Private Sector Working Group of the Royal Government Forum - The private sector has been recognized by the Royal Government of Cambodia to participate in dialogue on various issues with the Royal Government.
