The 3rd Anniversary Ceremony and Remembrance of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An to End, Led by Samdech Say Chhum and Samdech Kong Sam Ol
(Phnom Penh): The 3rd Anniversary Ceremony and Remembrance Ceremony of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An The Marching Parade was completed this afternoon, March 15, 2020, led by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia. And Samdech Chao Feang Vor Vieng Chey, President of Sri Lanka Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Royal Palace.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. and Mrs., who are senior national dignitaries, tycoons, national and international guests, government officials from ministries and institutions and government officials from the districts of Takeo province, especially Kirivong and Traing districts. Which is the hometown of many Samdech Vibol Panha to take the remains of Samdech Vibol Panha to be kept at the stupa in Wat Saravan Techo, Phnom Penh along the Buddhist path.
The ceremony started at 6 am to gather all the guests and relatives to pay their respects to the remains of Samdech Vibol Panha and the monks of the Natthi Dhamma (birth) before starting the procession of the remains of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An to Wat Saravan Techo Phnom Penh on foot.
The great success of the service of the nation and the motherland and the success of building a harmonious family life are clear testimonies that Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An is a truly successful person in his life. .
It should also be noted that the stupa of the relics of Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An was built in accordance with the style and rules of construction in the field of Buddhism and the rules of ancient Khmer architecture, completely designed by Khmer architects. The most meticulous.
In addition to the beautiful design and Khmer style, this stupa also has a bright golden mosaic, which emphasizes the beauty and luxury of the building with a unique style in line with the development of modern society. The stupa was held to raise the umbrella and get married on Sunday morning, February 16, 2020.
It should be noted that Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, passed away at 6:32 pm on March 15, 2017 at a hospital in Beijing, China at the age of 66.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health of Cambodia yesterday and today issued an official statement banning foreigners from six countries, including Italy, Germany, Spain, France, the United States and Iran, from entering Cambodia for 30 days. From Monday, March 17 for Italy, Germany, Spain, France and the United States and from March 18 for Iran as an emergency measure to prevent the spread of Covid-19.
Ms. Vandin stated that the decision to suspend foreigners to six countries: Italy, Germany, Spain, France, the United States and Iran is the first step that the Ministry has set out, but the Ministry is still waiting to see what new developments. Further consideration will be given to whether to stop foreigners from entering Cambodia to prevent the spread of Covid-19 disease.
She gave an example of measures to suspend foreigners from entering Cambodia, saying that from March 17, 2020, if any foreigners from Italy enter Cambodia or pass through Cambodia, they will not be allowed to enter Cambodia. But a person who travels nationally but does not live in Italy or other than the six countries where Cambodia is suspended and he does not have a 14-day history of entering all six countries, he can enter Cambodia.
At the same time, Ms. O Vandin also called on travelers from the six countries that Cambodia has banned, please understand and do not be offended, because this is a measure to prevent the spread of Covid-19. At the same time, even the United States adheres to this principle, suspending almost all European countries from entering the United States.
She said that for Cambodians who wish to travel to the six banned countries from March 17, 2020 is not allowed, and for Cambodians who have gone away, but it is time to return. He may return, but upon return, report to the medical team stationed at the airport, and if there are any health problems related to Covid-19, immediately report to Special 115.
