(Phnom Penh): Speaking at the opening ceremony of the Golden Dragon 2020 exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese armies, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, made six points to the soldiers of the two countries' armies as well as the soldiers involved.
On March 15, 2020, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army launched the fourth joint Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 under the theme "Together against Terrorism and Humanitarian Work" at Techo Sen Chum Real Shooting Range. Kiri of the 70th Infantry Brigade is located in O village, Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province.
General Vong Pisen instructed the soldiers of the two countries' armies as well as the soldiers involved in some of the following content:
1. All soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) must work closely together to successfully implement the noble recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, on the occasion of the 20th anniversary of the establishment of the Army on January 29. 2019 has passed. At the same time, it is necessary to pay attention to study and strictly abide by the rules of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
3. To strive to acquire new and good knowledge and skills for the fulfillment of the task of defending and building our homeland, as well as contributing to the maintenance of world peace and stability.
4. To promote the bonds of solidarity, friendship, sincerity in the spirit of operation and mutual respect equally, in order to make the process of this meaningful and important Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 to achieve high results.
5: Strengthen the promotion of good health, prevent infectious diseases in accordance with the call of the Royal Government of Cambodia: Stay clean. * If in doubt, go to the hospital, do not be afraid.
6: All committees and working groups must strive to perform their core roles thoroughly and ensure that all work supply work is guaranteed to be divided properly and correctly according to the set rules, especially to ensure the safety of both people and equipment. Both during and after the exercise 100%.
It should be noted that the 4th Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 between the Cambodian-Chinese army, the Chinese People's Liberation Army sent 256 troops to participate. Separately, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces sent 2,746 troops to participate in the exercise, including 463 people directly to participate in the exercise and the rest for the opening and closing ceremonies.
