(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Russey Keo District, Chea Pisey, and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, led the movement to strengthen the awareness of river cleaning, environmental sanitation for a clean city, starting from all of us in Celebrate the 6th River Festival 2020 under the theme "River of Peace, River of Prosperity".
The celebration of the 6th River Festival 2020 under the theme "River of Peace, River of Prosperity" to clean up the river, clean up the environment, led by Russey Keo District Governor and a member of the Secretariat of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia With the participation of more than 200 people in the Democratic Park, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo on March 14, 2020.
Please be informed that the river is a source of livelihood, a place where training and culture and civilization are nurtured. From ancient times the human race has lived along rivers and lived in clusters from one generation to the next.
The river is a gift from nature, a reference for human life and a natural bond of mutual support. The river connects the countries that consume the water of the same river to become a community of equal destiny, with equality, helping each other as honestly and intimately as one family.
Seeing the value of such a river, the Royal Government of Cambodia celebrated the River Festival. The river festival has been held for five years in the provinces along the river and around the Tonle Sap Lake. The event has become a festive event to promote tourism potential, products and send a message to the people to take care of the environment along the river, preserve the biodiversity along the river as well.
To commemorate the values of peace that promote prosperity and prosperity, the River Festival in 2020 is held under the theme "River of Peace, River of Prosperity."
