Colonel Sok Min, Commander of the O'Yadao District Local Armed Forces, told Fresh News this morning, March 15, 2020, that the operation took place on March 14, 2020, with the coordination of Leang Ou. Deputy Prosecutor of Ratanakkiri Provincial Court.
The commander confirmed that the arrest of the above suspects was based on the complaint of the military officers on the country. On February 19, 2020, their forces went to prevent forest crime and found a motorbike. Three spare logs transported to Vietnam at a rice field in Pak Touch village, Som Thom commune, O'Yadao district.
At that time, they (the National Gendarmerie Force) called to stop back, but the timber truck pulls the steel pipe and walks towards the uncomfortable situation, and for safety's sake, they withdrew and left a motorbike to operate at That was destroyed by the transporters, but the O'Yadao District Armed Forces intervened in time to return the motorcycle to the Armed Forces across the country.
Colonel Son Min said that after receiving complaints from military officers across the country about the attempted murder and intentional damage, his officers conducted a thorough search, with the suspects fleeing into the forest. On the evening of March 14, the guards arrested a suspect named Ro Chamnev, the ringleader, while the other four accomplices fled to Vietnam.
