Please note that in this traffic accident, 7 bodyguards were injured, one of them was seriously injured in the arm. All victims are currently being treated at the Bakan District Referral Hospital. Preah Vihear provincial authorities recommend rebuilding Phnom Chhat Sen Chey Secondary School in Choam Ksan district after collapsing due to strong winds
(Preah Vihear): Phnom Chhat Sen Chey Secondary School, located in Sen Chey Village, Sra Em Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, which was completely destroyed by strong winds, has been rebuilt by the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority to provide opportunities for students to attend school as soon as possible.
The instruction to accelerate the construction of Phnom Chhat Sen Chey Secondary School was made this morning, March 14, 2020, under the direct supervision of Mr. Ko Subunsoeut, Acting Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on behalf of Mr. Prak Sovann, Provincial Governor. Deputy Commander of the 3rd Intervention Brigade, Commander of the 7th Intervention Brigade, Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie, as well as Choam Ksan District Authority, teachers, students and many others.
Mr. Ko Subunsoeut said that after the actual inspection, the working group agreed to rebuild the school in its original form, made of galvanized iron and 8x24 meters in size. Another room and office. The deputy governor confirmed that we decided to rebuild the original form because some of the wood of the collapsed school is still usable.
On behalf of the Provincial Governor, Mr. Ko Subunsoeut also thanked Major General Duong Samneang, Commander of the 7th Intervention Brigade for his position in rebuilding this school, and thanked the Forestry Administration for providing some timber. The provincial authorities will also help with cement for sowing.
It should be noted that Phnom Chhat Sen Chey Secondary School was completely collapsed by the strong wind on the afternoon of March 13, 2020, but this incident did not cause any students to be injured. Morocco Transport Minister crosses COVID-19 after returning from duty in Europe
