Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Presiding Over the Opening Ceremony of the River Festival in Battambang Province
(Battambang): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Saturday evening, March 14, 2020, presided over the opening ceremony of the 6th River Festival in Battambang Province. The ceremony was also attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, representatives of the embassies of friendly countries, as well as government officials, armed forces and a large crowd.
The following are the main remarks made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the River Festival:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and highly commended the Inter-Ministerial Commission of the Ministry of Tourism, relevant ministries and institutions of Battambang Provincial Administration and the private sector for their active cooperation in organizing this important festival.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that currently, Cambodia's tourism sector is growing remarkably in the last decade, making Cambodia an attractive tourist destination to contribute to the development of society.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 2019, the number of international tourists to Cambodia was about 6.6 million, three times more than 10 years ago, which was only 2.1 million.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that tourism is a green gold and a pillar of the national economy. Gross revenue from international tourism in 2019 was 4919 million US dollars, or nearly 13% of GDP.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in terms of value added, the tourism sector contributed about 4.4% of GDP in 2019 and is also the fourth largest sub-sector in the service sector after trade, transportation and Telecommunications and real estate. The tourism sector has directly created more than 630,000 direct tourism jobs and jobs, and tens of thousands more indirect jobs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that at the beginning of 2020, international tourists to Cambodia decreased by about 30.5%, of which Chinese tourists decreased by around 40% compared to the same period in 2019.
* Samdech Techo stated that according to this data, compared to tourist destinations in neighboring countries, the rate of decline in the number of international tourists to Cambodia is still small.
* Samdech Techo stated that the measures that have been put in place now are only the first round of short-term measures, and he will continue to introduce a new package of reform measures in the Royal Government and the private sector forum. Scheduled to take place on April 1, 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told to take care of the airport land in Battambang province, which in the future will have to build an airport to serve development needs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if the airport can not be an international airport, it can also be used for domestic flights.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovit 19 can make Battambang province less affected by tourism but not agriculture and industry.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen shows his willingness to build a road connecting Battambang to Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo calls on people to join the fight against false information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as of 2 March 14, 2020, 146 countries and territories as well as the Prince Diamond were attacked by 19 Kovit.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen congratulates the Chinese government for overcoming Kovit 19 and helping other countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that so far there is only one Cambodian citizen with 19 cases of Kovit. But found up to seven foreigners.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has worked closely with all partners, especially the World Health Organization.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has no reason to hide the case of Kovit disease. On the contrary, the Royal Government only calls on the people to show up if there is a suspicion of Kovit disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked for the understanding of some embassies for refusing to take passengers on the dock in Kampong Cham to stay in a star hotel in Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen replied that a group of people repeatedly forbade the citizens of France, Spain, Germany, Italy and the United States to enter Cambodia as people without Khmer resin blood.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the ban on these five countries from entering Cambodia because these countries are putting some countries and regions in a state of emergency.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the world today is full of discrimination.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the closure of these five countries to Cambodia is not discriminatory, just a measure to prevent smallpox.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia may consider placing Iran as a country banned from entering Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls again to the people to prevent the spread of Kovit 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the culture of the Buddhist country is being used by the Christian country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests all TV stations to broadcast educational videos on the 19 cases of Kovit infection.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his happiness to see people use krama to protect their health.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to inspire Cambodians to use Khmer krama for health care
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 19 cases of Kovit have reached the ladder of a group of people who distort the story of Kovit abroad.
