(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on March 13, 2020, decided to provide 17 more water wells at a cost of 32,300 US dollars. Three hundred US dollars) to provide 275 families (equivalent to 1,058 people) living in drought areas in Rong Roeung, Romney, Romtom and Romdos communes of Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
This is the provision of clean water wells in the second phase of 2020 for the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Preah Vihear province, the first phase of Preah Vihear province received 19 wells on January 30, 2020.
