Elephant stabs a boy to death in Ratanakkiri province
(Ratanakkiri): A vicious male elephant caught a young boy and tricked him into hitting a tree stump, causing his death in Ratanakkiri province.
This incident happened at 09:11 on March 14, 2020 at Phnom Krouch in Ka Teang village, Lbang 2 commune, Lumphat district.
After reports from residents, police from the administrative post of Lbang 2 commune arrived, but the boy was taken to the hospital by Mor Damrey with serious injuries and could not be rescued.
According to Post 2 police, the 32-year-old male elephant named Pok Mai is owned by Khay Chenda, owner of the Teru Hotel in Banlung, Ratanakkiri Province. As for Mor Damrey, Bun Roeung Phlal, 31 years old, a Preav (fugitive) and Hiek Chieu, 10 years old, a Preav, a 10th grade student, were at the scene. Legal proceedings.
