(Battambang): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Saturday evening, March 14, 2020, will preside over the opening ceremony of the 6th River Festival in Battambang Province. The ceremony was also attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, representatives of the embassies of friendly countries, as well as government officials, armed forces and a large crowd.
Cambodia is one of the countries in Southeast Asia that has suffered the most from the fires of war. Through win-win politics, Cambodia ended the dark pages of the era, the pages of the history of division returned to the end of the fires of war and the reunification of history at the end of 1998.
Peace born of a win-win policy has given the Cambodian people the opportunity to continue their struggle to stand up, with Cambodia growing at a rate of about 7 percent in the last two decades. Peace has brought development and progress in all fields in the hope of a glorious and bright future.
The concept of peace has also boosted Cambodia's tourism, which is cultural and nature tourism, and the Royal Government, dubbed the "Green Gold", has proudly achieved remarkable growth, with positive growth every year and employment. Much directly and indirectly to the Cambodian people.
To commemorate the values of peace that promote prosperity and prosperity, the River Festival in 2020 is held under the theme "River of Peace, River of Prosperity".
Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the river festival in Battambang province in 2020 has expanded because Battambang city is not next to the river, but there are rivers next to the river.
He said that according to the concept of organizing the river festival and the recommendation of the Prime Minister, the river festival can be held in the provinces along the river or river. In this sense, the long-famous Stung Sangke is a river that connects Battambang to the Tonle Sap and Tonle Sap lakes in response to the concept of the river festival.
He added that Battambang is considered the country's largest rice barn, a civilized city, a heritage city, and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. By many resorts, including intangible heritage tourism, ecotourism, community tourism, agro-tourism and eco-tourism in many places.
At the same time, there are also some pre-event activities such as workshops accompanied by the distribution of prizes to outstanding tourism businesses, including accommodation, food, transportation, selected from 5 provinces in Battambang. Pursat, Pailin, Banteay Meanchey and Kampong Chhnang.
