Ms. Sum Sorangsy pointed out that the cultivated cocoa will be collected by her enterprise and resold to Thai companies that have entered into an agreement to process into other products.
According to Ms. Sum Surangsey, this planting can not be planted according to the people want to plant, the Thai company set to plant only one million trees. This is to ensure that the cocoa grown by the people will not be left behind.
Ms. Sorangsey said that the company sells a cocoa tree to the people for 12,000 riel, but if they buy 100 or more coconuts, the company charges only 70% of the price from the grower, while the other 30% will be paid at harvest time. .
According to Ms. So Rainsy, one hectare of land can grow 635 cocoa trees, and the first year in one cocoa tree can get about 20 kg of fruit, and the following year can increase the yield according to maintenance. The owner of the enterprise also confirmed the price of a kilogram of fresh cocoa, the company buys at a minimum price of 1,200 riel, and if the market price rises, the company will buy even higher.
Ms. Phanny claimed that the company decided to invest in planting in Cambodia because it has a lot of vacant land, which is highly favorable for cocoa.
The representative of the Thai company also claimed to buy cocoa when people can grow it. According to the representative of the company, Khmer Surin, he assured that when the people can grow, the company will not buy out because there is a valid contract, and on the other hand, there is a high demand for cocoa products on the market.
Ms. Panny stated that what the company wants to invest in this cultivation is not to make a profit from selling cocoa seedlings, what the company wants is cocoa to process the seeds into various products.
