Minister: Ministry of Culture continues to demand that Cambodian antiquities lost during the war from the United States
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, claimed that the Ministry of Culture is currently continuing to reclaim artifacts that Cambodia lost in the war from the United States while there are 42 statues and demanded the return of Cambodia. .
This statement was made on the occasion of Ms. Phoeung Sakona participating in the discussion "Women in Cultural Protection" organized by the US Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts at the National Museum in Phnom Penh on the evening of March 13. 2020.
Speaking to reporters, Ms. Pheung Sakona stated, "In 2019, we received 42 statues from the United States and we are continuing to work to reclaim as much as we can from what we have lost." "Available in the United States."
Ms. Pheung Sakona added, "In this work, we have worked closely with the Embassy's partners to find lost Cambodian artifacts."
At the same time, Ms. Phoeung Sakona also said that since 2001 until now in the US Department of Culture has helped Cambodian culture with a total of 4.5 million US dollars.
The Minister of Culture stated that all of these grants are related to the rehabilitation of temples, including Bak Kheng, Banteay Srei at Preah Vihear, and the establishment of the Phnom Da Museum in Angkor Borei District, Takeo Province, with assistance from US Embassy.
In addition, Ms. Phoeung Sakona emphasized that in addition to the work, the US Embassy Foundation focused on the care of the victims' clothing at the Tuol Sleng Museum, as well as the creation of a genocide-related essay.
Minister Phuong Sakona also mentioned that the United States' involvement in the preservation of national heritage and documents related to Cambodian history is part of a focus on strengthening the relationship between Cambodia and the United States.
In addition, as well as supporting Cambodia in its efforts to repatriate invaluable and stolen artifacts from the country. This was further confirmed by the US Ambassador to Cambodia.
(Battambang): Following the recommendation of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the National Committee for Clean City Assessment, on March 14, the Department of Clean City Support and Competition launched a clean-up campaign along the Sangke Sala River. Learn and organize the River Festival in Battambang to contribute to make the city clean, green and clean to celebrate the 6th River Festival 2020.
The campaign activities were attended by Battambang provincial and municipal authorities, many youth volunteers from the Battambang branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, the Peace-loving Youth Union, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and some other youth volunteers. The team also went to Samdech Ov High School with the cooperation of many teachers and students.
Mr. Hout Rithy, Director of the Department of Clean City Support and Competition Promotion, said that in addition to cleaning up the garbage and cleaning up the environment at the river festival venue, the campaign also raised awareness among local and international tourists. Living in Battambang province and those who come to visit the river festival.
Mr. Hout Rithy continued that this morning, the team of the Department of Clean City Support and Competition also went to Samdech Ov High School, which participated in cleaning inside and outside the campus on the streets near the location. Celebrate the River Festival by distributing banners, slogans and other cleaning materials to keep it clean and green as a contribution to the River Festival celebration.
He added that yesterday, the team of his department in collaboration with Coca-Cola provided four large metal cage bins to two universities in Battambang: University of Battambang and Global. Belle Bright High School to help students understand how to sort garbage and store it in individual drawers.
On the occasion of the river festival, garbage was also cleaned in about 10 other places in Battambang, Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Kratie and some riverside provinces.
At the same time, Mr. Hout Rithy also called on the people, youth, government officials, local authorities to clean up the city, river, river, lake, lake in their locality regularly to contribute to make Cambodia clean and green, especially to be ready to welcome tourists. Millions more international that Cambodia will host in the upcoming 2023 SEA Games.
Wing Welcomes Government Delegation to Demonstrate Leading Technology in Payment
(Phnom Penh): Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited has welcomed a Royal Government delegation at its head office to introduce mobile financial services and electronic payment services on March 13, 2020.
The visit was led by Duke Kith Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited, in the presence of Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications (MPTC) and a delegation of 17 other senior officials.
During the visit, Wing showed the delegation how to use the latest technology in digital financial transactions that support e-commerce as well as e-governance to support government initiatives. Cambodia in the development of the digital economy.
Mr. Tram Iv Tek said, "I am very interested in how Wing has deployed the use of state-of-the-art technology and methods to drive Cambodia's economy through financial ecosystems." "Digital payment solutions are one of the most important global trends in promoting sustainable inclusive growth as Cambodia moves towards a digital economy."
With more than 5 million customers, most of whom are not in the banking network, Wing has supported the Cambodian economy by facilitating transactions worth nearly 90% of the country's GDP through more than 130 million transactions. Last year.
Mr. Manura Chan, General Manager of Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited, stated, “Wing always emphasizes its outstanding performance in striving to maintain efficient business operations throughout the organization as well as to strengthen the sustainability of innovation. Of financial solutions to meet the daily needs of the Cambodian people.
In addition to providing money transfer services, bill payments, mobile top-ups, cash withdrawals and online and offline payments through a robust mobile ecosystem, Wing provides overseas remittance services such as: Philippines, Vietnam, Thailand and South Korea. Benefit the people of Cambodia as well as migrant workers living in more than 200 countries around the world.
Mr. Manora Chan added that they have selected Wing's international partners to effectively send money to Cambodia through their Wing accounts to their family members.
Tomorrow, the Cambodian-Chinese Army will launch the Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 under the theme "Together against terrorism and humanitarian work" in Kampot
(Kampot): On March 15, 2020, tomorrow, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army will launch the fourth joint Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 under the theme "Together against terrorism and humanitarian work". The larger one is located at the Techo Sen Chum Kiri real shooting range of the 70th Infantry Brigade in O village, Trapeang Reang commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province.
The opening ceremony of the Golden Dragon Exercise 2020 will be presided over by General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and Mr. Wang Vinthean, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia. The closing ceremony will be presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
For the Golden Dragon Exercise 2020, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces will use 4 helicopters, 10 T55 tanks, 12 DMT1 armored vehicles and 6 122 D30 artillery, 12 mortars, as well as several automatic rifles. First, intelligence equipment, demining equipment, enemy clearance equipment and chemical neutralization equipment, etc.
The Chinese People's Liberation Army will use six helicopters, three 122 D30 mobile artillery pieces, nine armored vehicles and 28 other vehicles for the 2020 Golden Dragon exercise and other equipment. Well.
