Hor Nambora will end his mission as Cambodian Ambassador to Indonesia on March 31
(Indonesia): Mr. Hor Nambora, Cambodian Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary to the Republic of Indonesia, will end his mission as Cambodian Ambassador to Indonesia on March 31, 2020, before concluding this mission. Thank you to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia for giving me the opportunity to serve the motherland for the past 32 years.
"For this page, there will be no more diplomatic work, only the activities of retired officials," he said. It is time for me to relax and live a beautiful life with the achievements I have built, to serve the nation, religion, the King for the past 32 years, and also to thank Samdech Techo Prime Minister for giving me this precious opportunity. This is for me. ”
Hor Nambora is not only a Doctor of Ben Violin, but also a former Representative of the Secretary-General of Cambodia from 1994 to 1997 at the United Nations Headquarters in New York, USA.
Hor Nambora is recognized as an ambassador for many national achievements in the country as well as in ASEAN. University students as well as the diplomatic community should read this book, which is an important guide for further self-study.
Interestingly, Mr. Hor Nambora was appointed as an Advisor to the Minister in charge of the Royal Government of Cambodia in 2009, and at the same time was appointed Special Envoy of the Prime Minister of Cambodia in 2011 in charge of the Campaign for the Promotion of Candidates. Of Cambodia to the United Nations Security Council in 2013-2014.
Mr. Hor Nambora was re-appointed as Ambassador to Cambodia to Ethiopia, the Permanent Representative of Cambodia to the African Union in 2011, based in London and currently as Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary Ambassador. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the Republic of Indonesia.
40 Poor Families in Pailin Province Receive Donations and Water Pumps from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Red Cross Branch and Mr. Meas Rithy, Deputy Director General of Hang Meas TV 40 poor families will be provided with clean water wells located in Dey Krahorm Village, Sangkat Otavao, Pailin City, Pailin Province.
Mr. Phan Chanthul expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always cares about the well-being of the people and provided clean water wells to help solve the difficulties of the people in a timely manner. He said that health is a major factor for all of us, so clean water is also a necessary factor for all of us in our daily lives to eat and use permanently.
He says water is the energy that nourishes the human body, animals and plants. He said that this well is also a new achievement for the people in Dey Krahorm village used by everyone who does not cause the problem of water shortage in both the dry and wet seasons, as well as the cultivation of mixed crops.
He encouraged people to grow mixed crops near their homes to facilitate their daily lives. He also instructed the people to take good care of this well for the long-term use.
It should be noted that during the handover ceremony, Mr. Phan Chanthul and Mr. Meas Rithy donated alcohol, hand washing, disinfection and gifts to 40 poor families, each family received 25 kg of rice and fish sauce. 1 bag of noodles, 1 box and a budget of 20,000 riels. On the occasion of the River Festival! Minister Thong Khon and Battambang Governor Lead Activities to Promote Tour Packages in the Province to Introduce Tourists
