(Kandal): Mr. Ney Chary, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, ordered the district and municipal authorities to take measures to disseminate education and guidance to all mining business owners, including transportation, to respect the law and technical standards that dare to violate the relevant guidelines. Absolutely no understanding, no conspiracy and no corruption.
The warning was made at a meeting to review the sand dredging, sand depot and sand transport business in Kandal province, which was attended by 11 provincial governors and relevant departments around the province. All on March 12, 2020 yesterday.
At the same time, Mr. Ney Chary also warned all companies and mining business owners, including transportation, to be legal in advance and comply with the principle No. 0310 of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, to ensure This business is regulated by law, and especially the trucking team must strictly follow the law to avoid causing problems that are of concern to the public and affect the environment.
