Report: "Mey Cheat Contributes to Promoting Khmer Reputation" (Phnom Penh): Under the roof of peace, Cambodia is moving forward relentlessly to build and develop this country for further progress. Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has changed its face from a country that has experienced the flames of war to a country on an equal footing with other countries in the region and internationally.
The National Noodle Factory is an enterprise that has been actively involved in local food production to contribute to the supply of domestic demand as well as export to foreign markets. The presence of a national noodle factory is also a result of the Royal Government of Cambodia's industrial policy to boost domestic production.
Establishing local enterprises to produce their own products In the past, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always encouraged and supported because it increases income, helps prevent migration and contributes to reducing poverty in Cambodia. . This is according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the opening ceremony of the 14th Cambodian Products and Import-Export Fair at Koh Pich Center during December 2019.
This is the best time for Cambodia to have a local food factory to meet the needs of more than 16 million people, which will help reduce dependence on foreign or neighboring production chains.
Noodles can be said to be a popular daily meal in addition to eating and spending less time cooking, which is suitable for those who have less time and do not have enough time to cook. This product is suitable for the general population of all levels, low, medium and high, who can eat almost any time, whether morning, evening or night.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has always considered the private sector as a sector that has contributed significantly to the development of the national economy, especially the diversification of the economic base, as well as the creation of job opportunities and increase income for the people.
Of course, in addition to doing business for profit, the company also contributes in part to the society by donating money to charity, materials and food, which is an important contribution to the Royal The Cambodian government to fill the gaps and needs in society as well.
Purchasing Cambodian products, more or less, is tantamount to creating jobs and income for the people, as well as stabilizing local production to diversify on-site exports as well as exports to key international markets. In addition, the purchase of Cambodian products will also contribute to enhancing Cambodia's competitiveness in the international arena.
Therefore, for the progress of Cambodia and for the pride of Cambodia, we, the Cambodian people, must support and work together to promote Cambodian products in the market and together for the progress of Cambodia.
National Assembly approves draft law on establishment of Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation
(Phnom Penh): The draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation has already been approved by the National Assembly of Cambodia by 116 to 118 votes in the extraordinary session of the 6th legislature this morning, March 13, 2020.
The meeting was chaired by Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and was attended by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as members of the National Assembly and representatives of the Royal Government.
According to a statement by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation was approved by the Council of Ministers at a plenary session of the Council of Ministers on February 27, 2020. Request for review and approval from the legislature, which consists of 8 articles and the main summary as follows:
Articles 1 to 4 define the name of the new ministry, the authority of the ministry and the authority to manage the ministry.
Article 5 sets out the provisions to ensure the sustainability of the implementation of the new legal norms.
Article 6 identifies issues related to the management of the Ministry in accordance with the law and legal documents related to the implementation of the law.
* On the establishment of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, which must be implemented until a new legal document replaces it * in accordance with the provisions of this new law.
Articles 7 to 8 determine the repeal of the law and the promulgation of the law as a matter of urgency.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on January 25, 2020 agreed to change the name of the Ministry of "Industry and Handicraft" to "Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation".
The agreement came after a request from Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, the current Minister of Industry and Handicrafts.
According to a letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers to Senior Minister Cham Prasidh on January 24, 2020, the Royal Government has agreed to amend the law and other legal documents, in addition to agreeing to change the name of the ministry. Involvement in the structure and functioning of the renamed ministry.
At the same time, the Royal Government also agreed to establish two new units, the General Department of Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Institute of Science, Technology and Innovation, which have the same level as the General Department. The establishment of these two entities does not require the addition of a state framework, ie the use of existing frameworks that are relevant to the work of science, technology and innovation.
The Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts was originally called the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy. In the fifth mandate, the Royal Government decided to create a new ministry called the Ministry of Mines and Energy, so the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy was renamed the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts.
